\n/work/mercor-work/activegraph-surrealdb/docs/compatibility.md\\n/work/mercor-work/activegraph-surrealdb/docs/architecture.md\\n/work/mercor-work/activegraph-surrealdb/docs/adr/0004-projection-order.md\\n/work/mercor-work/activegraph-surrealdb/docs/adr/0003-native-query-pushdown.md\\n/work/mercor-work/activegraph-surrealdb/docs/adr/0002-version-and-transport-support.md\\n/work/mercor-work/activegraph-surrealdb/docs/adr/0001-provider-boundaries.md\"}],\"metadata\":{\"count\":11,\"truncated\":false}}","session_id":"ses_ecce71390ffe11p6yPgte61c3p","status":"completed"}}
ll the development dependencies, then run the layers explicitly:\\n26: \\n27: ```bash\\n28: python -m pip install -e '.[dev]'\\n29: pytest -m 'not surrealdb and not qualification'\\n30: pytest -m surrealdb tests/integration\\n31: ACTIVEGRAPH_PACKS_PATH=/path/to/activegraph-packs pytest -m packs tests/packs\\n32: ACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_QUALIFY=1 pytest -m qualification tests/qualification\\n33: ```\\n34: \\n35: The live layers require the environment described in [deployment.md](deployment.md).\\n36: The qualification command must target only the disposable container it is\\n37: authorized to restart and kill.\\n38: \\n39: ## Required invariants\\n40: \\n41: Promotion evidence must include at least:\\n42: \\n43: - released EventStore and GraphStore conformance;\\n44: - exact JSON round-trip and literal canonical/hash golden values;\\n45: - append-before-projection ordering (a rejected append leaves no projection);\\n46: - native query pushdown for every overridden GraphStore hook;\\n47: - projected objects returned in the reference store's insertion order;\\n48: - an in-place, data-preserving schema upgrade and rejection of a newer schema;\\n49: - loading the published pack library onto one SurrealDB-backed Runtime;\\n50: - running each pack's own fixture suite on SurrealDB-backed stores, with any\\n51:   non-portable suite recorded as an explicit expected divergence;\\n52: - transaction rollback without an orphan event or advanced head;\\n53: - deterministic same-run stale-writer rejection and independent run progress;\\n54: - scope/run isolation across reads, clears, truncation, forks, and relations;\\n55: - native `TYPE RELATION` records with bound `RecordID` endpoints;\\n56: - replay that clears stale state, marks failure, and becomes ready only on success;\\n57: - prefix-only forks with traceable parent metadata and independent suffixes;\\n58: - rejection of unsupported compacted histories;\\n59: - close/reopen, server restart, and abrupt container termination; and\\n60: - an existing-database upgrade test before any supported-version change.\\n61: \\n62: ## Recording evidence\\n63: \\n64: A repeatable result records:\\n65: \\n66: - repository commit SHA and clean/dirty status;\\n67: - Python, ActiveGraph, SDK, and server versions;\\n68: - Docker image digest, command, transport, and storage engine;\\n69: - exact commands and marker selections;\\n70: - pass, fail, skip, and expected-failure counts;\\n71: - host/OS and test timestamp; and\\n72: - logs for any failure or replay repair.\\n73: \\n74: CI status is implementation evidence only for its recorded environment. It is\\n75: not a performance benchmark, deployed-service proof, backup proof, or proof that\\n76: an application has modeled authorization correctly.\\n77: \\n78: ## Contract-first status\\n79: \\n80: Tests may intentionally be RED while a contract is being implemented. That is\\n81: useful only when the failure is the expected missing behavior. Do not mark a\\n82: test xfail, weaken an assertion, or replace a live path with a mock merely to\\n83: produce green CI. Make the provider satisfy the contract, then record the green\\n84: trace.\"}],\"metadata\":{\"truncated\":false}}","session_id":"ses_ecce71390ffe11p6yPgte61c3p","status":"completed"}}
