\n68: \\n69: ## Pack harness lane\\n70: \\n71: The pack lane loads the external ActiveGraph pack library onto a Runtime whose\\n72: event log and graph projection both live in the test database. Point the harness\\n73: at a checkout:\\n74: \\n75: ```bash\\n76: ACTIVEGRAPH_PACKS_PATH=/path/to/activegraph-packs pytest -m packs tests/packs\\n77: ```\\n78: \\n79: When `ACTIVEGRAPH_PACKS_PATH` is unset the harness uses the reference checkout\\n80: baked into this environment; the lane skips cleanly when neither is present. The\\n81: lane is read-only with respect to the pack repository — it imports packs and\\n82: loads them, and never modifies the checkout.\\n83: \\n84: ## Qualification lane\\n85: \\n86: Qualification checks the exact SDK/server versions, image command, RocksDB\\n87: engine, transactional WebSocket path, graceful restart, abrupt container kill,\\n88: and reopening persisted event/graph state.\\n89: \\n90: It controls the container named by\\n91: `ACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_DOCKER_CONTAINER`, including `docker kill`, removes and\\n92: recreates it against `ACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_DOCKER_VOLUME`:\\n93: \\n94: ```bash\\n95: ACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_QUALIFY=1 pytest -m qualification tests/qualification\\n96: ```\\n97: \\n98: Use only the disposable Compose container. A pass proves the asserted data\\n99: survived those test sequences on that host; it does not prove crash consistency\\n100: under every failure, storage durability guarantees, or restore readiness.\\n101: \\n102: ## Backup and restore\\n103: \\n104: Backup and restore are promotion gates, not completed features of this preview.\\n105: A production evaluation must document and exercise:\\n106: \\n107: 1. the SurrealDB-supported backup/export mechanism for the selected deployment;\\n108: 2. credential and encryption handling;\\n109: 3. restoration into a separate clean environment;\\n110: 4. event-chain and run-head verification after restore;\\n111: 5. graph clear/replay after restore; and\\n112: 6. recovery-time and recovery-point observations.\\n113: \\n114: A copied file, successful export command, or green application health check is\\n115: not by itself restore proof.\\n116: \\n117: ## Production evaluation checklist\\n118: \\n119: Before any production use, require evidence for all of the following:\\n120: \\n121: - pinned, supported versions and a documented upgrade/rollback test;\\n122: - external TLS and least-privilege identities rather than root credentials;\\n123: - network isolation and authorization for every application table;\\n124: - backup and clean-environment restore;\\n125: - monitoring for failed/incomplete projections and hash-chain verification;\\n126: - capacity, latency, and failure testing on representative data;\\n127: - an explicit high-availability design, if required; and\\n128: - operator acceptance of the non-atomic event/projection boundary.\"}],\"metadata\":{\"truncated\":false}}","session_id":"ses_ecce71390ffe11p6yPgte61c3p","status":"completed"}}
wned then by the coordinator); `docker compose down` and remove the old dev volume |\\n| V1 | unit | `pytest -m 'not surrealdb and not qualification'` green, including converted known-issue tests |\\n| V2 | live integration | `docker compose up -d` on a fresh volume; `pytest -m surrealdb tests/integration` green. Failure of a 3.3.0-specific wire issue triggers the fallback: coordinator re-pins `v3.2.5` in the WP1 files, records it, and re-runs V2 and V3 |\\n| V3 | qualification | `ACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_QUALIFY=1 pytest -m qualification tests/qualification` green (restart and kill sequences) |\\n| V4 | example | `python examples/replay_fork_diff.py` completes its published trace |\\n| V5 | Lane B upgrade | the new `upgrade` test passes end to end, including the export-restore rollback rehearsal; failure keeps the roadmap item open and is recorded |\\n| V6 | Lane A TLS | generate a local CA (`mkcert` or `openssl`) trusted by the host; start the TLS lane; `surreal is-ready --endpoint https://127.0.0.1:8000` responds; `ACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_TEST_URL=wss://127.0.0.1:8000` with the same suites as V2 and V3 green |\\n| V7 | Lane C surrealkv | engine variable `surrealkv`, its own volume; live integration suite green; qualification optional; recorded as beta evidence |\\n| V8 | Lane D embedded | isolated `.venv-embedded` with `surrealdb[embedded]==3.0.0b10`; the `embedded` marker test passes as the expected rejection evidence |\\n| V9 | records and parity | full `ruff check`, `ruff format --check`, `mypy`, `build`, `twine check`; unit suite green once more; update ADR 0003 status with evidence links; finalize the compatibility matrix and ROADMAP checkboxes; the coordinator makes the final commit |\\n\\n## Commit plan\\n\\nThe coordinator commits one logical change per accepted package, after\\nreview, in this order:\\n\\n1. `feat: pin SurrealDB 3.3.0 and parameterize lane deployment` (WP1)\\n2. `feat: upgrade ActiveGraph to 1.12.0` (WP2)\\n3. `test: convert v1.10 known issues for ActiveGraph 1.12.0` (WP3)\\n4. `docs: update pins, ordering, and lane documents` (WP4, WP5)\\n5. `test: add upgrade, TLS, surrealkv, and embedded lane harness` (WP6)\\n6. `docs: record lane evidence and accept ADR 0003` (V9)\\n\\n## Dependency graph\\n\\n```mermaid\\nflowchart LR\\n    E[WP1..WP6 editors in parallel] --> B[coordinator review and commits]\\n    B --> V0[V0 pre-flight]\\n    V0 --> V1[V1 unit] --> V2[V2 integration] --> V3[V3 qualification]\\n    V3 --> V4[V4 example] --> V5[V5 upgrade lane] --> V6[V6 TLS lane]\\n    V6 --> V7[V7 surrealkv lane] --> V8[V8 embedded lane] --> V9[V9 records]\\n    V2 -. fallback re-pin 3.2.5 .-> F[coordinator fallback] --> V2\\n    V3 -. fallback .-> F\\n```\\n\\n## Sub-agent prompts\\n\\nSpawn editors in parallel, one prompt per work package:\\n\\n```text\\nIn this repository, read docs/upgrade-plan.md fully, especially\\n\\\"Shared context\\\" and the brief for your package. Execute work package\\n<WPn> exactly.\\n\\nScope: edit only the files that package owns. Do not commit, do not\\nbranch, do not start Docker, do not run pytest or mypy.\\n\\nVerify: run `ruff check` and `ruff format --check` on the files you own.\\n\\nReport back: (1) each file changed with a one-line summary;\\n(2)…[truncated 22053 chars]","session_id":"ses_ecce71390ffe11p6yPgte61c3p","status":"completed"}}
