reproducible fork/diff/replay trace evidence.\\n\\n## Phase 2 — Stable qualification\\n\\n- [x] Pass live isolation, rollback, native-edge, and exact-JSON tests.\\n- [ ] Pass pinned RocksDB graceful restart and abrupt container termination tests.\\n- [x] Add an in-place, data-preserving schema upgrade lane and reject a newer schema.\\n- [x] Add a schema rollback lane before changing support.\\n- [x] Exercise backup and clean-environment restore, then verify event integrity and replay.\\n- [ ] Record bounded performance observations on controlled, representative data.\\n\\n## Phase 3 — Upstream lifecycle alignment\\n\\n- [x] Re-evaluate append/projection ordering after ActiveGraph 1.12 incorporated it\\n  (CONTRACT v1.11 #2); see\\n  [ADR 0003](docs/adr/0003-latest-stable-pins-and-exploration-lanes.md).\\n- [ ] Adopt a public store-driver/registry contract if upstream accepts one.\\n- [ ] Adopt store-neutral load/resume without phantom-run or stale-projection behavior.\\n- [ ] Design snapshot/compaction hydration only against an explicit upstream contract.\",\"mime\":\"text/markdown\",\"offset\":1,\"truncated\":true,\"next\":41},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Read file /home/mercor/orca/workspaces/activegraph-surrealdb/mercor-vm/ROADMAP.md, lines 1-40\\n1: # Roadmap\\n2: \\n3: This roadmap describes evidence gates, not release dates. Work moves forward\\n4: only when the previous boundary is repeatably demonstrated.\\n5: \\n6: ## Phase 0 — Contract-first research preview\\n7: \\n8: - [x] Separate authoritative event and disposable graph responsibilities.\\n9: - [x] Pin ActiveGraph `1.12.0`, SurrealDB `3.2.4`, and Python SDK `2.0.0` lanes.\\n10: - [x] Define serialization, isolation, replay, fork/diff, and qualification contracts.\\n11: - [x] Record upstream lifecycle limitations without private runtime patches.\\n12: \\n13: ## Phase 1 — Generic provider implementation\\n14: \\n15: - [x] Pass unit serialization/configuration contracts.\\n16: - [x] Pass released EventStore and GraphStore conformance.\\n17: - [x] Implement transactional append/head checks and deterministic stale-writer tests.\\n18: - [x] Implement native relation storage without an in-memory mirror.\\n19: - [x] Push object, relation, existence, and neighbourhood queries into native SurrealQL; `match_chain` composes those primitives.\\n20: - [x] Implement fail-closed replay readiness and uncompacted prefix forks.\\n21: - [x] Load the published pack library onto one SurrealDB-backed Runtime.\\n22: - [x] Publish reproducible fork/diff/replay trace evidence.\\n23: \\n24: ## Phase 2 — Stable qualification\\n25: \\n26: - [x] Pass live isolation, rollback, native-edge, and exact-JSON tests.\\n27: - [ ] Pass pinned RocksDB graceful restart and abrupt container termination tests.\\n28: - [x] Add an in-place, data-preserving schema upgrade lane and reject a newer schema.\\n29: - [x] Add a schema rollback lane before changing support.\\n30: - [x] Exercise backup and clean-environment restore, then verify event integrity and replay.\\n31: - [ ] Record bounded performance observations on controlled, representative data.\\n32: \\n33: ## Phase 3 — Upstream lifecycle alignment\\n34: \\n35: - [x] Re-evaluate append/projection ordering after ActiveGraph 1.12 incorporated it\\n36:   (CONTRACT v1.11 #2); see\\n37:   [ADR 0003](docs/adr/0003-latest-stable-pins-and-exploration-lanes.md).\\n38: - [ ] Adopt a public store-driver/registry contract if upstream accepts one.\\n39: - [ ] Adopt store-neutral load/resume without phantom-run or stale-projection behavior.\\n40: - [ ] Design snapshot/compaction hydration only against an explicit upstream contract.\\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 41]\"}],\"metadata\":{\"truncated\":true}}","session_id":"ses_ecd1f104affewX9x4cIqy5fLvq","status":"completed"}}
r multi-node high availability.\\n-- TLS certificate, proxy, or workload-identity qualification.\\n+- TLS qualification beyond the pinned preview lane: public CAs, proxy\\n+  termination, least-privilege identities, and certificate rotation.\\n - Atomic event-plus-projection acceptance.\\n+\\n+## Provider schema\\n+\\n+The provider schema is versioned and additive. Schema v1 introduced the\\n+event/graph tables; schema v2 adds the indexes that back the native query\\n+pushdown; schema v3 records the object counter that gives projection reads the\\n+reference store's insertion order. Opening an older database upgrades it in\\n+place without data loss; a database written by a newer provider is rejected\\n+rather than mis-read. The upgrade path is pinned by\\n+`tests/integration/test_schema_upgrade.py`, and the backup / clean-environment\\n+restore rehearsal (export, restore into a fresh database, integrity and\\n+projection parity, newer-provider rollback rejection) by\\n+`tests/integration/test_backup_restore.py`.\\n\"}],\"metadata\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"truncated\":false,\"exit\":0}}","session_id":"ses_ecd1f104affewX9x4cIqy5fLvq","status":"completed"}}
