{"id":"int-0eb11c1da2cd500a8743591c3e4df019","kind":"tool_call","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:57:10.42Z","actor":"opencode","tool_name":"shell","extra":{"call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8766d573cb5b0870","duration_ms":2263,"input":"{\"command\":\".venv/bin/python -m pytest -m 'not surrealdb and not qualification and not embedded' -q 2>&1 | tail -2\",\"timeout\":300000}","message_id":"msg_1333132ad001prD3tGuKRy6J4V","result":"{\"output\":{\"exit\":0,\"truncated\":false,\"output\":\"XFAIL tests/known_issues/test_activegraph_v112_stale_projection.py::test_runtime_load_replaces_stale_projection - Still open upstream in ActiveGraph 1.12.0: yoheinakajima/activegraph#82\\n28 passed, 149 deselected, 2 xfailed in 1.10s\\n\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"XFAIL tests/known_issues/test_activegraph_v112_stale_projection.py::test_runtime_load_replaces_stale_projection - Still open upstream in ActiveGraph 1.12.0: yoheinakajima/activegraph#82\\n28 passed, 149 deselected, 2 xfailed in 1.10s\\n\"}],\"metadata\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"truncated\":false,\"exit\":0}}","session_id":"ses_ecce71390ffe11p6yPgte61c3p","status":"completed"}}
{"id":"int-4c47627669296435181fb22581bda49e","kind":"tool_call","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:57:17.272Z","actor":"opencode","tool_name":"shell","extra":{"call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-935e5341c1ee2771","duration_ms":40,"input":"{\"command\":\"sed -n '40,80p' docs/adr/0003-native-query-pushdown.md; echo \\\"=== ROADMAP ===\\\"; cat ROADMAP.md\"}","message_id":"msg_133314a52001mJywSNxo3qtAi1","result":"{\"output\":{\"exit\":0,\"truncated\":false,\"output\":\"Schema v2 adds the `(scope, run_id, ...)` indexes these queries use. The schema\\nupgrade is additive and in place; a database written by a newer provider is\\nrejected rather than mis-read.\\n\\n## Consequences\\n\\nPositive:\\n\\n- Pack reads and behaviour reactions touch only the objects and relations they\\n  actually need, rather than the whole scope/run graph.\\n- The pushed-down hooks are the same primitives `match_chain` already used, so\\n  the override improves traversal without a second code path.\\n- The residual-predicate contract keeps `where` semantics owned by ActiveGraph,\\n  so the provider never disagrees with the canonical evaluator.\\n\\nNegative:\\n\\n- The provider now depends on the `1.12` `ObjectQuery` / `ObjectQueryResult`\\n  surface, so the `1.12.0` pin is load-bearing.\\n- The pushdown must track any future change to the base-class hook semantics;\\n  the conformance suite and `test_graph_pushdown.py` are the guard.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n`tests/integration/test_graph_pushdown.py` disables `all_objects` and\\n`all_relations` and then exercises every overridden hook. A regression to the\\nPython fallback raises instead of returning rows. The released\\n`GraphStoreConformance` suite runs unchanged against the same store, so the\\npushed-down behavior is pinned to the canonical semantics.\\n=== ROADMAP ===\\n# Roadmap\\n\\nThis roadmap describes evidence gates, not release dates. Work moves forward\\nonly when the previous boundary is repeatably demonstrated.\\n\\n## Phase 0 — Contract-first research preview\\n\\n- [x] Separate authoritative event and disposable graph responsibilities.\\n- [x] Pin ActiveGraph `1.12.0`, SurrealDB `3.2.4`, and Python SDK `2.0.0` lanes.\\n- [x] Define serialization, isolation, replay, fork/diff, and qualification contracts.\\n- [x] Record upstream lifecycle limitations without private runtime patches.\\n\\n## Phase 1 — Generic provider implementation\\n\\n- [x] Pass unit serialization/configuration contracts.\\n- [x] Pass released EventStore and GraphStore conformance.\\n- [x] Implement transactional append/head checks and deterministic stale-writer tests.\\n- [x] Implement native relation storage without an in-memory mirror.\\n- [x] Push object, relation, existence, and neighbourhood queries into native SurrealQL; `match_chain` composes those primitives.\\n- [x] Implement fail-closed replay readiness and uncompacted prefix forks.\\n- [x] Load the published pack library onto one SurrealDB-backed Runtime.\\n- [x] Publish reproducible fork/diff/replay trace evidence.\\n\\n## Phase 2 — Stable qualification\\n\\n- [x] Pass live isolation, rollback, native-edge, and exact-JSON tests.\\n- [ ] Pass pinned RocksDB graceful restart and abrupt container termination tests.\\n- [x] Add an in-place, data-preserving schema upgrade lane and reject a newer schema.\\n- [ ] Add a schema rollback lane before changing support.\\n- [ ] Exercise backup and clean-environment restore, then verify event integrity and replay.\\n- [ ] Record bounded performance observations on controlled, representative data.\\n\\n## Phase 3 — Upstream lifecycle alignment\\n\\n- [x] Re-evaluate append/projection ordering after ActiveGraph 1.12 incorporated it (CONTRACT v1.11 #2).\\n- [ ] Adopt a public store-driver/registry contract if upstream accepts one.\\n- [ ] Adopt store-neutral load/resume without phantom-run or stale-projection behavior.\\n- [ ] Design snapshot/compaction hydration only against an explicit upstream contract.\\n- [ ] Evaluate an optional runtime-owned cross-store transaction coordinator.\\n\\n## Phase 4 — Production evaluation\\n\\n- [ ] Qualify `wss://`, certificate validation, least-privilege identities, and rotation.\\n- [ ] Define monitoring and operator response for failed/incomplete projections.\\n- [ ] Document data retention, restore objectives, and incident response.\\n- [ ] Decide whether single-node RocksDB meets availability requirements or a different\\n  deployment architecture is necessary.\\n- [ ] Complete an independent security and operational review.\\n\\n## Continuing non-goals\\n\\n- claiming cross-store atomicity without an upstream coordinator;\\n- hiding upstream gaps behind copied private runtime code;\\n- managing application contacts, auth, CRM records, or identity ontologies;\\n- qualifying every SurrealDB transport, engine, cloud, or prerelease; and\\n- calling the preview production-ready based only on CI.\\n\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Schema v2 adds the `(scope, run_id, ...)` indexes these queries use. The schema\\nupgrade is additive and in place; a database written by a newer provider is\\nrejected rather than mis-read.\\n\\n## Consequences\\n\\nPositive:\\n\\n- Pack reads and behaviour reactions touch only the objects and relations they\\n  actually need, rather than the whole scope/run graph.\\n- The pushed-down hooks are the same primitives `match_chain` already used, so\\n  the override improves traversal without a second code path.\\n- The residual-predicate contract keeps `where` semantics owned by ActiveGraph,\\n  so the provider never disagrees with the canonical evaluator.\\n\\nNegative:\\n\\n- The provider now depends on the `1.12` `ObjectQuery` / `ObjectQueryResult`\\n  surface, so the `1.12.0` pin is load-bearing.\\n- The pushdown must track any future change to the base-class hook semantics;\\n  the conformance suite and `test_graph_pushdown.py` are the guard.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n`tests/integration/test_graph_pushdown.py` disables `all_objects` and\\n`all_relations` and then exercises every overridden hook. A regression to the\\nPython fallback raises instead of returning rows. The released\\n`GraphStoreConformance` suite runs unchanged against the same store, so the\\npushed-down behavior is pinned to the canonical semantics.\\n=== ROADMAP ===\\n# Roadmap\\n\\nThis roadmap describes evidence gates, not release dates. Work moves forward\\nonly when the previous boundary is repeatably demonstrated.\\n\\n## Phase 0 — Contract-first research preview\\n\\n- [x] Separate authoritative event and disposable graph responsibilities.\\n- [x] Pin ActiveGraph `1.12.0`, SurrealDB `3.2.4`, and Python SDK `2.0.0` lanes.\\n- [x] Define serialization, isolation, replay, fork/diff, and qualification contracts.\\n- [x] Record upstream lifecycle limitations without private runtime patches.\\n\\n## Phase 1 — Generic provider implementation\\n\\n- [x] Pass unit serialization/configuration contracts.\\n- [x] Pass released EventStore and GraphStore conformance.\\n- [x] Implement transactional append/head checks and deterministic stale-writer tests.\\n- [x] Implement native relation storage without an in-memory mirror.\\n- [x] Push object, relation, existence, and neighbourhood queries into native SurrealQL; `match_chain` composes those primitives.\\n- [x] Implement fail-closed replay readiness and uncompacted prefix forks.\\n- [x] Load the published pack library onto one SurrealDB-backed Runtime.\\n- [x] Publish reproducible fork/diff/replay trace evidence.\\n\\n## Phase 2 — Stable qualification\\n\\n- [x] Pass live isolation, rollback, native-edge, and exact-JSON tests.\\n- [ ] Pass pinned RocksDB graceful restart and abrupt container termination tests.\\n- [x] Add an in-place, data-preserving schema upgrade lane and reject a newer schema.\\n- [ ] Add a schema rollback lane before changing support.\\n- [ ] Exercise backup and clean-environment restore, then verify event integrity and replay.\\n- [ ] Record bounded performance observations on controlled, representative data.\\n\\n## Phase 3 — Upstream lifecycle alignment\\n\\n- [x] Re-evaluate append/projection ordering after ActiveGraph 1.12 incorporated it (CONTRACT v1.11 #2).\\n- [ ] Adopt a public store-driver/registry contract if upstream accepts one.\\n- [ ] Adopt store-neutral load/resume without phantom-run or stale-projection behavior.\\n- [ ] Design snapshot/compaction hydration only against an explicit upstream contract.\\n- [ ] Evaluate an optional runtime-owned cross-store transaction coordinator.\\n\\n## Phase 4 — Production evaluation\\n\\n- [ ] Qualify `wss://`, certificate validation, least-privilege identities, and rotation.\\n- [ ] Define monitoring and operator response for failed/incomplete projections.\\n- [ ] Document data retention, restore objectives, and incident response.\\n- [ ] Decide whether single-node RocksDB meets availability requirements or a different\\n  deployment architecture is necessary.\\n- [ ] Complete an independent security and operational review.\\n\\n## Continuing non-goals\\n\\n- claiming cross-store atomicity without an upstream coordinator;\\n- hiding upstream gaps behind copied private runtime code;\\n- managing application contacts, auth, CRM records, or identity ontologies;\\n- qualifying every SurrealDB transport, engine, cloud, or prerelease; and\\n- calling the preview production-ready based only on CI.\\n\"}],\"metadata\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"truncated\":false,\"exit\":0}}","session_id":"ses_ecce71390ffe11p6yPgte61c3p","status":"completed"}}
{"id":"int-179cf338b2281bb04760cce45d217910","kind":"tool_call","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:57:17.398Z","actor":"opencode","tool_name":"shell","extra":{"call_id":"call_23d2d054e028420d9c2912ab","duration_ms":120,"input":"{\"command\":\"echo \\\"=== init script (docker/snapshot/restart hooks) ===\\\"; grep -nE \\\"docker|snapshot|restart|volume|image|entrypoint\\\" /opt/mercor-tools/mercor-init.sh | head -20; echo; echo \\\"=== proxy / gateway env ===\\\"; env | grep -iE \\\"proxy|gateway|egress\\\" | sed 's/=.*/=<set>/'; echo; echo \\\"=== orca hook token usage ===\\\"; grep -rn \\\"ORCA_AGENT_HOOK_TOKEN\\\" /opt/mercor-tools/*.py /opt/mercor-tools/*.sh 2>/dev/null | head -5\",\"timeout\":60000}","message_id":"msg_13330ec6b001fxm57Q0fTACkZW","result":"{\"output\":{\"exit\":0,\"truncated\":false,\"output\":\"=== init script (docker/snapshot/restart hooks) ===\\n\\n=== proxy / gateway env ===\\n\\n=== orca hook token usage ===\\n\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"=== init script (docker/snapshot/restart hooks) ===\\n\\n=== proxy / gateway env ===\\n\\n=== orca hook token usage ===\\n\"}],\"metadata\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"truncated\":false,\"exit\":0}}","session_id":"ses_ecd1f104affewX9x4cIqy5fLvq","status":"completed"}}
{"id":"int-b6a0b9367e6a2c61994ea758cfb5ed5d","kind":"tool_call","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:57:17.844Z","actor":"opencode","tool_name":"shell","extra":{"call_id":"call_ef71ca9f3b0e42f6b7d32d84","duration_ms":564,"input":"{\"command\":\"echo \\\"=== can we reach alt registries for surrealdb? ===\\\"; for host in public.ecr.aws quay.io registry.k8s.io; do timeout 8 curl -sI \\\"https://$host/v2/\\\" -o /dev/null -w \\\"$host: %{http_code}\\\\n\\\" || echo \\\"$host: unreachable\\\"; done; echo \\\"=== S3 endpoint variants ===\\\"; for u in \\\"https://docker-images-prod.s3.amazonaws.com\\\" \\\"https://docker-images-prod.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com\\\"; do timeout 8 curl -s -o /dev/null -w \\\"$u -> %{http_code}\\\\n\\\" \\\"$u\\\" || echo \\\"$u -> fail\\\"; done\",\"timeout\":90000}","message_id":"msg_13330ec6b001fxm57Q0fTACkZW","result":"{\"output\":{\"exit\":0,\"truncated\":false,\"output\":\"=== can we reach alt registries for surrealdb? ===\\npublic.ecr.aws: 401\\nquay.io: 401\\nregistry.k8s.io: 000\\nregistry.k8s.io: unreachable\\n=== S3 endpoint variants ===\\nhttps://docker-images-prod.s3.amazonaws.com -> 000\\nhttps://docker-images-prod.s3.amazonaws.com -> fail\\nhttps://docker-images-prod.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com -> 000\\nhttps://docker-images-prod.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com -> fail\\n\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"=== can we reach alt registries for surrealdb? ===\\npublic.ecr.aws: 401\\nquay.io: 401\\nregistry.k8s.io: 000\\nregistry.k8s.io: unreachable\\n=== S3 endpoint variants ===\\nhttps://docker-images-prod.s3.amazonaws.com -> 000\\nhttps://docker-images-prod.s3.amazonaws.com -> fail\\nhttps://docker-images-prod.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com -> 000\\nhttps://docker-images-prod.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com -> fail\\n\"}],\"metadata\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"truncated\":false,\"exit\":0}}","session_id":"ses_ecd1f104affewX9x4cIqy5fLvq","status":"completed"}}
{"id":"int-9d642aabbc361211c9170ce78951a68c","kind":"tool_call","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:57:23.966Z","actor":"opencode","tool_name":"shell","extra":{"call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b518b3d74ca63aba","duration_ms":7,"input":"{\"command\":\"cat docs/compatibility.md\"}","message_id":"msg_13331650f0013BrafWjZFoZrp5","result":"{\"output\":{\"exit\":0,\"truncated\":false,\"output\":\"# Compatibility and known issues\\n\\n## Qualified and preview lanes\\n\\n| Component | Status | Notes |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| ActiveGraph `1.12.0` | Baseline | Public store interfaces and released conformance suites |\\n| SurrealDB server `3.2.4` | Required stable lane | Pinned Docker image, remote WebSocket, server-side RocksDB |\\n| SurrealDB Python SDK `2.0.0` | Required | Exact dependency pin for the research preview |\\n| SurrealDB `3.3.x` prerelease | Preview only | Forward-compatibility signal; never gates the stable lane |\\n| Python `3.11+` | Package requirement | CI results, not the version declaration alone, determine qualified interpreters |\\n\\n## Transport and engine matrix\\n\\n| Path | Accepted by configuration | Qualification status |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| `ws://` to pinned local server | Yes | Required qualification lane |\\n| `wss://` to remote server | Yes | Syntax supported; no TLS qualification claim yet |\\n| HTTP/HTTPS | No | Stateful SDK transaction handles are WebSocket-only |\\n| `mem://` embedded | No | Not durable and outside the provider preview |\\n| embedded `file://`, `rocksdb://`, or `surrealkv://` | No | Persistence and transaction semantics are not qualified |\\n| server-side RocksDB | Yes | Required stable storage path |\\n| server-side SurrealKV | No recommendation | SurrealKV remains beta |\\n\\nThe Compose and qualification files intentionally pin complete versions. A new\\nserver or SDK release is unsupported until its own compatibility branch passes\\nthe same conformance, restart, concurrency, isolation, and exact-serialization\\ntests.\\n\\nThe SDK `2.0.0` blocking WebSocket implementation currently emits a\\n`DeprecationWarning` with `websockets 17.1` because the SDK opens its internal\\nsocket through a legacy direct-connect path. The stable contract suite passes;\\nthe warning is tracked as dependency-compatibility work and is not suppressed\\nby this provider.\\n\\n## ActiveGraph lifecycle limitations\\n\\nThe provider does not patch private ActiveGraph runtime methods or register a\\ndatabase URL scheme. Stores are constructed explicitly.\\n\\n- ActiveGraph `1.12.0` ships the append-before-projection ordering proposed by\\n  [PR #78](https://github.com/yoheinakajima/activegraph/pull/78) as CONTRACT\\n  v1.11 #2: a rejected durable append changes no projected state. The provider\\n  asserts that invariant directly in `tests/test_write_ordering.py`.\\n- [ActiveGraph issue #81](https://github.com/yoheinakajima/activegraph/issues/81)\\n  tracks `Runtime.load()` creating an unknown run instead of failing without a\\n  mutation. Still open in `1.12.0`.\\n- [ActiveGraph issue #82](https://github.com/yoheinakajima/activegraph/issues/82)\\n  tracks replay into a stale supplied projection without clearing it first.\\n  Still open in `1.12.0`.\\n\\nStrict expected-failure tests keep the remaining limitations visible. An\\nupstream fix that makes one unexpectedly pass is a prompt to review and update\\nthe provider, not to delete the test blindly.\\n\\n## Compaction\\n\\nReplay and fork helpers support uncompacted event histories only. They reject a\\nlog beginning with `runtime.snapshot` and reject a fork point outside the\\nretained prefix. Snapshot materialization, compaction horizons, and legacy\\nmigration are not implemented by guessing at private runtime state.\\n\\n## Claims this matrix does not make\\n\\n- ActiveGraph `1.13` compatibility before an upstream release is tested.\\n- Wire or storage compatibility across arbitrary SurrealDB versions.\\n- Distributed SurrealDB, SurrealDB Cloud, or multi-node high availability.\\n- TLS certificate, proxy, or workload-identity qualification.\\n- Atomic event-plus-projection acceptance.\\n\\n## Provider schema\\n\\nThe provider schema is versioned and additive. Schema v1 introduced the\\nevent/graph tables; schema v2 adds the indexes that back the native query\\npushdown; schema v3 records the object counter that gives projection reads the\\nreference store's insertion order. Opening an older database upgrades it in\\nplace without data loss; a database written by a newer provider is rejected\\nrather than mis-read. The upgrade path is pinned by\\n`tests/integration/test_schema_upgrade.py`.\\n\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"# Compatibility and known issues\\n\\n## Qualified and preview lanes\\n\\n| Component | Status | Notes |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| ActiveGraph `1.12.0` | Baseline | Public store interfaces and released conformance suites |\\n| SurrealDB server `3.2.4` | Required stable lane | Pinned Docker image, remote WebSocket, server-side RocksDB |\\n| SurrealDB Python SDK `2.0.0` | Required | Exact dependency pin for the research preview |\\n| SurrealDB `3.3.x` prerelease | Preview only | Forward-compatibility signal; never gates the stable lane |\\n| Python `3.11+` | Package requirement | CI results, not the version declaration alone, determine qualified interpreters |\\n\\n## Transport and engine matrix\\n\\n| Path | Accepted by configuration | Qualification status |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| `ws://` to pinned local server | Yes | Required qualification lane |\\n| `wss://` to remote server | Yes | Syntax supported; no TLS qualification claim yet |\\n| HTTP/HTTPS | No | Stateful SDK transaction handles are WebSocket-only |\\n| `mem://` embedded | No | Not durable and outside the provider preview |\\n| embedded `file://`, `rocksdb://`, or `surrealkv://` | No | Persistence and transaction semantics are not qualified |\\n| server-side RocksDB | Yes | Required stable storage path |\\n| server-side SurrealKV | No recommendation | SurrealKV remains beta |\\n\\nThe Compose and qualification files intentionally pin complete versions. A new\\nserver or SDK release is unsupported until its own compatibility branch passes\\nthe same conformance, restart, concurrency, isolation, and exact-serialization\\ntests.\\n\\nThe SDK `2.0.0` blocking WebSocket implementation currently emits a\\n`DeprecationWarning` with `websockets 17.1` because the SDK opens its internal\\nsocket through a legacy direct-connect path. The stable contract suite passes;\\nthe warning is tracked as dependency-compatibility work and is not suppressed\\nby this provider.\\n\\n## ActiveGraph lifecycle limitations\\n\\nThe provider does not patch private ActiveGraph runtime methods or register a\\ndatabase URL scheme. Stores are constructed explicitly.\\n\\n- ActiveGraph `1.12.0` ships the append-before-projection ordering proposed by\\n  [PR #78](https://github.com/yoheinakajima/activegraph/pull/78) as CONTRACT\\n  v1.11 #2: a rejected durable append changes no projected state. The provider\\n  asserts that invariant directly in `tests/test_write_ordering.py`.\\n- [ActiveGraph issue #81](https://github.com/yoheinakajima/activegraph/issues/81)\\n  tracks `Runtime.load()` creating an unknown run instead of failing without a\\n  mutation. Still open in `1.12.0`.\\n- [ActiveGraph issue #82](https://github.com/yoheinakajima/activegraph/issues/82)\\n  tracks replay into a stale supplied projection without clearing it first.\\n  Still open in `1.12.0`.\\n\\nStrict expected-failure tests keep the remaining limitations visible. An\\nupstream fix that makes one unexpectedly pass is a prompt to review and update\\nthe provider, not to delete the test blindly.\\n\\n## Compaction\\n\\nReplay and fork helpers support uncompacted event histories only. They reject a\\nlog beginning with `runtime.snapshot` and reject a fork point outside the\\nretained prefix. Snapshot materialization, compaction horizons, and legacy\\nmigration are not implemented by guessing at private runtime state.\\n\\n## Claims this matrix does not make\\n\\n- ActiveGraph `1.13` compatibility before an upstream release is tested.\\n- Wire or storage compatibility across arbitrary SurrealDB versions.\\n- Distributed SurrealDB, SurrealDB Cloud, or multi-node high availability.\\n- TLS certificate, proxy, or workload-identity qualification.\\n- Atomic event-plus-projection acceptance.\\n\\n## Provider schema\\n\\nThe provider schema is versioned and additive. Schema v1 introduced the\\nevent/graph tables; schema v2 adds the indexes that back the native query\\npushdown; schema v3 records the object counter that gives projection reads the\\nreference store's insertion order. Opening an older database upgrades it in\\nplace without data loss; a database written by a newer provider is rejected\\nrather than mis-read. The upgrade path is pinned by\\n`tests/integration/test_schema_upgrade.py`.\\n\"}],\"metadata\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"truncated\":false,\"exit\":0}}","session_id":"ses_ecce71390ffe11p6yPgte61c3p","status":"completed"}}
{"id":"int-ba0a93fc58535d8fd120c87473a15bf2","kind":"tool_call","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:57:35.293Z","actor":"opencode","tool_name":"edit","extra":{"call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a277b3ee42cb785f","duration_ms":4,"input":"{\"path\":\"/work/mercor-work/activegraph-surrealdb/docs/compatibility.md\",\"oldString\":\"| `ws://` to pinned local server | Yes | Required qualification lane |\\n| `wss://` to remote server | Yes | Syntax supported; no TLS qualification claim yet |\\n| HTTP/HTTPS | No | Stateful SDK transaction handles are WebSocket-only |\\n| `mem://` embedded | No | Not durable and outside the provider preview |\\n| embedded `file://`, `rocksdb://`, or `surrealkv://` | No | Persistence and transaction semantics are not qualified |\\n| server-side RocksDB | Yes | Required stable storage path |\\n| server-side SurrealKV | No recommendation | SurrealKV remains beta |\",\"newString\":\"| `ws://` to pinned local server | Yes | Required qualification lane |\\n| `wss://` to pinned local server | Yes | Preview TLS lane demonstrated: local CA via openssl, certificate verification enforced, full live suite green (2026-10-13). No rotation or workload-identity claim. |\\n| HTTP/HTTPS | No | Stateful SDK transaction handles are WebSocket-only |\\n| `mem://` embedded | No | Not durable and outside the provider preview; rejection pinned by `tests/embedded/test_embedded_lane.py` |\\n| embedded `file://`, `rocksdb://`, or `surrealkv://` | No | Persistence and transaction semantics are not qualified; rejection pinned by `tests/embedded/test_embedded_lane.py` |\\n| server-side RocksDB | Yes | Required stable storage path |\\n| server-side SurrealKV | No recommendation | SurrealKV remains beta; full live integration suite green on a dedicated SurrealKV volume (V7 lane, 2026-10-13) |\\n\\n### Evidence recording note (2026-10-13)\\n\\nThe V2/V4/V5/V6/V7 lane runs were recorded against the native `surreal v3.2.4`\\nbinary (same version as the pinned image) on fresh per-lane RocksDB/SurrealKV\\nvolumes, because the execution sandbox cannot run containers\\n(`agvm-8ii`: devpts `gid=5` is unmappable without setuid `newuidmap`). The\\ncontainerized qualification (compose bring-up, restart/kill sequences) remains\\nthe outstanding gap and is deferred to a VM-runtime sandbox.\"}","message_id":"msg_133317e8a001Ncoz3ExsaKpkDF","result":"{\"output\":{\"files\":[{\"file\":\"docs/compatibility.md\",\"patch\":\"Index: docs/compatibility.md\\n===================================================================\\n--- docs/compatibility.md\\n+++ docs/compatibility.md\\n@@ -14,15 +14,24 @@\\n \\n | Path | Accepted by configuration | Qualification status |\\n | --- | --- | --- |\\n | `ws://` to pinned local server | Yes | Required qualification lane |\\n-| `wss://` to remote server | Yes | Syntax supported; no TLS qualification claim yet |\\n+| `wss://` to pinned local server | Yes | Preview TLS lane demonstrated: local CA via openssl, certificate verification enforced, full live suite green (2026-10-13). No rotation or workload-identity claim. |\\n | HTTP/HTTPS | No | Stateful SDK transaction handles are WebSocket-only |\\n-| `mem://` embedded | No | Not durable and outside the provider preview |\\n-| embedded `file://`, `rocksdb://`, or `surrealkv://` | No | Persistence and transaction semantics are not qualified |\\n+| `mem://` embedded | No | Not durable and outside the provider preview; rejection pinned by `tests/embedded/test_embedded_lane.py` |\\n+| embedded `file://`, `rocksdb://`, or `surrealkv://` | No | Persistence and transaction semantics are not qualified; rejection pinned by `tests/embedded/test_embedded_lane.py` |\\n | server-side RocksDB | Yes | Required stable storage path |\\n-| server-side SurrealKV | No recommendation | SurrealKV remains beta |\\n+| server-side SurrealKV | No recommendation | SurrealKV remains beta; full live integration suite green on a dedicated SurrealKV volume (V7 lane, 2026-10-13) |\\n \\n+### Evidence recording note (2026-10-13)\\n+\\n+The V2/V4/V5/V6/V7 lane runs were recorded against the native `surreal v3.2.4`\\n+binary (same version as the pinned image) on fresh per-lane RocksDB/SurrealKV\\n+volumes, because the execution sandbox cannot run containers\\n+(`agvm-8ii`: devpts `gid=5` is unmappable without setuid `newuidmap`). The\\n+containerized qualification (compose bring-up, restart/kill sequences) remains\\n+the outstanding gap and is deferred to a VM-runtime sandbox.\\n+\\n The Compose and qualification files intentionally pin complete versions. A new\\n server or SDK release is unsupported until its own compatibility branch passes\\n the same conformance, restart, concurrency, isolation, and exact-serialization\\n tests.\\n\",\"additions\":13,\"deletions\":4,\"status\":\"modified\"}],\"replacements\":1},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Edited docs/compatibility.md (1 replacement)\"}],\"metadata\":{\"files\":[{\"file\":\"docs/compatibility.md\",\"patch\":\"Index: docs/compatibility.md\\n===================================================================\\n--- docs/compatibility.md\\n+++ docs/compatibility.md\\n@@ -14,15 +14,24 @@\\n \\n | Path | Accepted by configuration | Qualification status |\\n | --- | --- | --- |\\n | `ws://` to pinned local server | Yes | Required qualification lane |\\n-| `wss://` to remote server | Yes | Syntax supported; no TLS qualification claim yet |\\n+| `wss://` to pinned local server | Yes | Preview TLS lane demonstrated: local CA via openssl, certificate verification enforced, full live suite green (2026-10-13). No rotation or workload-identity claim. |\\n | HTTP/HTTPS | No | Stateful SDK transaction handles are WebSocket-only |\\n-| `mem://` embedded | No | Not durable and outside the provider preview |\\n-| embedded `file://`, `rocksdb://`, or `surrealkv://` | No | Persistence and transaction semantics are not qualified |\\n+| `mem://` embedded | No | Not durable and outside the provider preview; rejection pinned by `tests/embedded/test_embedded_lane.py` |\\n+| embedded `file://`, `rocksdb://`, or `surrealkv://` | No | Persistence and transaction semantics are not qualified; rejection pinned by `tests/embedded/test_embedded_lane.py` |\\n | server-side RocksDB | Yes | Required stable storage path |\\n-| server-side SurrealKV | No recommendation | SurrealKV remains beta |\\n+| server-side SurrealKV | No recommendation | SurrealKV remains beta; full live integration suite green on a dedicated SurrealKV volume (V7 lane, 2026-10-13) |\\n \\n+### Evidence recording note (2026-10-13)\\n+\\n+The V2/V4/V5/V6/V7 lane runs were recorded against the native `surreal v3.2.4`\\n+binary (same version as the pinned image) on fresh per-lane RocksDB/SurrealKV\\n+volumes, because the execution sandbox cannot run containers\\n+(`agvm-8ii`: devpts `gid=5` is unmappable without setuid `newuidmap`). The\\n+containerized qualification (compose bring-up, restart/kill sequences) remains\\n+the outstanding gap and is deferred to a VM-runtime sandbox.\\n+\\n The Compose and qualification files intentionally pin complete versions. A new\\n server or SDK release is unsupported until its own compatibility branch passes\\n the same conformance, restart, concurrency, isolation, and exact-serialization\\n tests.\\n\",\"status\":\"modified\",\"additions\":13,\"deletions\":4}]}}","session_id":"ses_ecce71390ffe11p6yPgte61c3p","status":"completed"}}
