ge=\\\\\\\"failed to load plugin\\\\\\\"\\\\ntarget=/home/mercor/.config/opencode/plugins/orca-opencode2-status\\\\nref=err_97f42f88\\\\ncause=\\\\\\\"Cause([Die(Error: ENOENT: no such file or directory,\\\\n        stat '/home/mercor/.config/opencode/plugins/orca-opencode2-status')])\\\\\\\"\\\\nhttp.span=3598741 role=server\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nThe `cause` field is the original error: `ENOENT` from `fs.statSync('/home/mercor/.config/opencode/plugins/orca-opencode2-status')` — note the path has no `.js` extension.\\\\n\\\\n## Plugin layout on disk\\\\n\\\\n`~/.config/opencode/plugins/` contains:\\\\n\\\\n| Entry | Type | Loads? |\\\\n|---|---|---|\\\\n| `orca-opencode2-status.js` | single file (72 167 B) | **fails** — this is what the error is about |\\\\n| `orca-opencode2-status-tui/tui.js` | directory containing entry file (72 167 B, **md5 matches** the .js above) | loads cleanly |\\\\n| `beads-audit/index.ts` | directory containing entry file | loads cleanly |\\\\n\\\\nThe two `.js`/`.tui.js` files have identical content (`md5 116859f74b61e625d14b564475f8b0f4`). The single-file `orca-opencode2-status.js` declares its own id as `\\\\\\\"orca-opencode2-status\\\\\\\"` (line 1648) and from inside it even loads `orca-opencode2-status-tui/tui.js` as the actual TUI entry (line 1125).\\\\n\\\\n## Configurations\\\\n\\\\n- `/home/mercor/.config/opencode/opencode.json` — no `plugins` key; references and providers only. No plugin path is configured here.\\\\n- `/home/mercor/.config/opencode/cli.json` — TUI/UI settings; nothing plugin-related.\\\\n- `/home/mercor/.config/opencode/service.json` — service password only.\\\\n- No project-level `opencode.json` and no `.opencode/` directory in the workspace.\\\\n- The OpenCode version logged around this run is `version=2.0.27 channel=latest`.\\\\n\\\\nThere are no plugin references in the current project's opencode config or project files — opencode is discovering the plugin purely by directory scan of `~/.config/opencode/plugins/`.\\\\n\\\\n## Root cause\\\\n\\\\nOpenCode 2 requires every plugin to be a **directory package** (with an entry file like `index.ts`, `index.js`, `tui.js`, etc. inside it), not a standalone `.js`/`.ts` file. Earlier in the same log you can see OpenCode explicitly rejecting a configured single-file plugin:\\\\n\\\\n```\\\\nWARN \\\\\\\"configured plugin path must be a directory\\\\\\\"\\\\ntarget=/work/mercor-work/activegraph-surrealdb/tools/opencode/beads-audit.ts\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nWhen the loader resolves `orca-opencode2-status.js` from the scan of `~/.config/opencode/plugins/`, its package-style probe calls `stat()` on `orca-opencode2-status` (no extension) to look for the sibling directory / manifest. That path doesn't exist as a directory, so the probe fails with `ENOENT` and the plugin is dropped, even though `orca-opencode2-status.js` itself is still on disk and well-formed.\\\\n\\\\nThe same error pattern appears 8+ times across multiple server runs (`4da1bb06`, `502e2132`, `797c5df9`, `ecfb849d`) and across multiple workspaces between 02:54:08 and 02:54:27, confirming this is a persistent, repeatable failure of the loader, not a one-off.\\\\n\\\\n## Recommended fix\\\\n\\\\nThe packaged form already exists on disk. Pick one of the following:\\\\n\\\\n1. **Move the single file into a directory of its own name** (mirrors the working layout, keeps the plugin id `orca-opencode2-status`):\\\\n   ```\\\\n   mkdir ~/.config/opencode/plugins/orca-opencode2-status\\\\n   mv ~/.config/opencode/plugins/orca-opencode2-status.js \\\\\\\\\\\\n      ~/.config/opencode/plugins/orca-opencode2-status/index.js\\\\n   ```\\\\n2. **Delete the broken single-file copy** and rely on the already-packaged `orca-opencode2-status-tui/` directory. Note that the two files have the same md5, so you lose no code; the loader will then only see the correctly-shaped directory. The plugin self-loads its TUI entry from `./orca-opencode2-status-tui/tui.js` relative to its own location, so the relative path from inside `orca-opencode2-status/` would need to become `.\\\",\\\"mainAgent\\\":{\\\"state\\\":\\\"done\\\",\\\"stateStartedAt\\\":1791860138213}},\\\"receivedAt\\\":1791860138213,\\\"evidenceObservedAt\\\":1791860138213,\\\"stateStartedAt\\\":1791860138213,\\\"launchTokenHash\\\":\\\"30479ac7ccef32341e5e2487d92f535368d689488dd3443958da06d7897305bf\\\"},\\\"4c899d8c-3f6d-421e-b280-eadedfab4fcb:738d7b66-82f8-4ac3-baaa-50d971405de0\\\":{\\\"paneKey\\\":\\\"4c899d8c-3f6d-421e-b280-eadedfab4fcb:738d7b66-82f8-4ac3-baaa-50d971405de0\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"opencode2\\\",\\\"agentPresence\\\":{\\\"agent\\\":\\\"opencode2\\\"},\\\"tabId\\\":\\\"4c899d8c-3f6d-421e-b280-eadedfab4fcb\\\",\\\"worktreeId\\\":\\\"2ccad8ce-2b7a-447f-9f91-86648e86f0f6::/home/mercor/orca/workspaces/activegraph-surrealdb/mercor-vm\\\",\\\"connectionId\\\":null,\\\"hasExplicitPrompt\\\":true,\\\"hookEventName\\\":\\\"MessagePart\\\",\\\"providerSession\\\":{\\\"key\\\":\\\"session_id\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"ses_ecd1f104affewX9x4cIqy5fLvq\\\"},\\\"payload\\\":{\\\"state\\\":\\\"working\\\",\\\"prompt\\\":\\\"# Images This guide walks you through how to define a Modal Image, the environment your Modal code runs in. The typical flow for defining an Image in Modal is [method chaining](https://jugad2.blogspot\\\",\\\"agentType\\\":\\\"opencode2\\\"},\\\"receivedAt\\\":1791860419047,\\\"evidenceObservedAt\\\":1791860419047,\\\"stateStartedAt\\\":1791860207009,\\\"launchTokenHash\\\":\\\"5b971c282f0016654a3e030516b1cd7f05c83428879ddcb8125645c6f7336bb9\\\"}},\\\"authorityCommitments\\\":{\\\"1611c5c9-e32f-4a4e-bf28-73082e11842b:54c45393-10c3-4c8c-bf46-c0b135b55c49\\\":{\\\"paneKey\\\":\\\"1611c5c9-e32f-4a4e-bf28-73082e11842b:54c45393-10c3-4c8c-bf46-c0b135b55c49\\\",\\\"launchTokenHash\\\":\\\"14edac30dcfc56a5eaa37820776a10269b080b207357dcbd2b57296ef94d77b1\\\",\\\"connectionId\\\":null,\\\"tabId\\\":\\\"1611c5c9-e32f-4a4e-bf28-73082e11842b\\\",\\\"worktreeId\\\":\\\"2ccad8ce-2b7a-447f-9f91-86648e86f0f