{"id":"int-34006230bde61e1e8c4b12c559b31620","kind":"tool_call","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:06:37.719Z","actor":"opencode","tool_name":"read","extra":{"call_id":"call_x5gmaHhkhkKbS9pIETNW0bUB","duration_ms":11,"input":"{\"path\":\"/work/.mercor-home/orca/workspaces/activegraph-surrealdb/integration-activegraph-adaptor/scripts/arize_conformance.py\",\"limit\":30}","message_id":"msg_13339d63c0018FpyLoOs9Ohp7D","result":"{\"output\":{\"type\":\"text-page\",\"content\":\"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Rerun the conformance contract as Arize AX datasets and experiments.\\n\\nThe mirror is built from tests/telemetry/conformance_cases.py, which\\nenumerates every case this repository tracks: the 11 released event-store\\nconformance cases, the 25 released graph-store conformance cases, and the\\nupstream known issues.\\n\\nCommands:\\n\\n  cases     Print the mirrored case registry (offline, no credentials).\\n  sync      Create one Arize AX dataset per suite (idempotent).\\n  run       Rerun every case live against the pinned SurrealDB lane and\\n            record the outcomes as an Arize AX experiment.\\n  register  Register the outcome evaluator in Arize AX so the platform\\n            renders the same scoring the local evaluators apply.\\n\\nRequired environment:\\n\\n  ARIZE_API_KEY, ARIZE_SPACE_ID    Arize AX target (sync, run, register)\\n  ACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_TEST_URL   live SurrealDB lane (run; see\\n                                   docs/deployment.md)\\n\\nEvery experiment task executes the real pytest case in a subprocess; outcomes\\nare scored with the mapping shared with the pytest telemetry plugin. The\\nmirror is metadata only: no event payloads, graph objects, relations, or\\nquery text leaves the machine.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\",\"mime\":\"application/octet-stream\",\"offset\":1,\"truncated\":true,\"next\":31},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Read file /work/.mercor-home/orca/workspaces/activegraph-surrealdb/integration-activegraph-adaptor/scripts/arize_conformance.py, lines 1-30\\n1: #!/usr/bin/env python3\\n2: \\\"\\\"\\\"Rerun the conformance contract as Arize AX datasets and experiments.\\n3: \\n4: The mirror is built from tests/telemetry/conformance_cases.py, which\\n5: enumerates every case this repository tracks: the 11 released event-store\\n6: conformance cases, the 25 released graph-store conformance cases, and the\\n7: upstream known issues.\\n8: \\n9: Commands:\\n10: \\n11:   cases     Print the mirrored case registry (offline, no credentials).\\n12:   sync      Create one Arize AX dataset per suite (idempotent).\\n13:   run       Rerun every case live against the pinned SurrealDB lane and\\n14:             record the outcomes as an Arize AX experiment.\\n15:   register  Register the outcome evaluator in Arize AX so the platform\\n16:             renders the same scoring the local evaluators apply.\\n17: \\n18: Required environment:\\n19: \\n20:   ARIZE_API_KEY, ARIZE_SPACE_ID    Arize AX target (sync, run, register)\\n21:   ACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_TEST_URL   live SurrealDB lane (run; see\\n22:                                    docs/deployment.md)\\n23: \\n24: Every experiment task executes the real pytest case in a subprocess; outcomes\\n25: are scored with the mapping shared with the pytest telemetry plugin. The\\n26: mirror is metadata only: no event payloads, graph objects, relations, or\\n27: query text leaves the machine.\\n28: \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n29: \\n30: from __future__ import annotations\\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 31]\"}],\"metadata\":{\"truncated\":true}}","session_id":"ses_eccd12d4cffe3Dd6d2N0q7gQQs","status":"completed"}}
{"id":"int-63d32ada3f7764c32af451f14a412b70","kind":"tool_call","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:06:37.725Z","actor":"opencode","tool_name":"read","extra":{"call_id":"call_1I37plg510rvZUpiaGhU8KW9","duration_ms":19,"input":"{\"path\":\"/work/.mercor-home/orca/workspaces/activegraph-surrealdb/integration-activegraph-adaptor/docs/adr/0001-provider-boundaries.md\",\"limit\":30}","message_id":"msg_13339d63c0018FpyLoOs9Ohp7D","result":"{\"output\":{\"type\":\"text-page\",\"content\":\"# ADR 0001: Keep the event log authoritative and the graph disposable\\n\\n- Status: accepted for the research preview\\n- Date: 2026-08-30\\n- Decision owners: TrendpilotAI\\n- Upstream baseline: ActiveGraph `v1.12.0` (`50d8405923b79e4e823a73a3045bb969436a872c`)\\n\\n## Context\\n\\nActiveGraph deliberately separates two jobs:\\n\\n1. the `EventStore` preserves what happened; and\\n2. the `GraphStore` answers questions about the current projected state.\\n\\nSurrealDB can host both jobs, plus application documents and native graph\\nrelations, in one deployment. That does not make the two jobs interchangeable.\\nIf a projection is lost, replay must rebuild it. If the event log is lost, the\\nstory is lost.\\n\\nAn initial application prototype demonstrated a promising co-located shape,\\nbut it was application-specific and did not satisfy the complete released\\nActiveGraph store contracts. Those choices are design evidence, not a general\\nprovider implementation.\\n\\n## Decision\\n\\nThis package must expose two independent, manually constructed provider seams:\\n\\n- `SurrealEventStore`: a per-scope, per-run ActiveGraph event log that must pass\\n  the released `EventStoreConformance` suite.\",\"mime\":\"text/markdown\",\"offset\":1,\"truncated\":true,\"next\":31},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Read file /work/.mercor-home/orca/workspaces/activegraph-surrealdb/integration-activegraph-adaptor/docs/adr/0001-provider-boundaries.md, lines 1-30\\n1: # ADR 0001: Keep the event log authoritative and the graph disposable\\n2: \\n3: - Status: accepted for the research preview\\n4: - Date: 2026-08-30\\n5: - Decision owners: TrendpilotAI\\n6: - Upstream baseline: ActiveGraph `v1.12.0` (`50d8405923b79e4e823a73a3045bb969436a872c`)\\n7: \\n8: ## Context\\n9: \\n10: ActiveGraph deliberately separates two jobs:\\n11: \\n12: 1. the `EventStore` preserves what happened; and\\n13: 2. the `GraphStore` answers questions about the current projected state.\\n14: \\n15: SurrealDB can host both jobs, plus application documents and native graph\\n16: relations, in one deployment. That does not make the two jobs interchangeable.\\n17: If a projection is lost, replay must rebuild it. If the event log is lost, the\\n18: story is lost.\\n19: \\n20: An initial application prototype demonstrated a promising co-located shape,\\n21: but it was application-specific and did not satisfy the complete released\\n22: ActiveGraph store contracts. Those choices are design evidence, not a general\\n23: provider implementation.\\n24: \\n25: ## Decision\\n26: \\n27: This package must expose two independent, manually constructed provider seams:\\n28: \\n29: - `SurrealEventStore`: a per-scope, per-run ActiveGraph event log that must pass\\n30:   the released `EventStoreConformance` suite.\\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 31]\"}],\"metadata\":{\"truncated\":true}}","session_id":"ses_eccd12d4cffe3Dd6d2N0q7gQQs","status":"completed"}}
