{"id":"int-08f5c7947e1dd7ba280f1736b475ada2","kind":"tool_call","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:06:55.488Z","actor":"opencode","tool_name":"write","extra":{"call_id":"call_uLKUInkVfwDKNrR3m0Pu2SKH","duration_ms":8,"input":"{\"path\":\"/work/.mercor-home/orca/workspaces/activegraph-surrealdb/integration-activegraph-adaptor/docs/adr/0004-opencode-plugin-v2-directory-layout.md\",\"content\":\"# ADR 0004: Package OpenCode 2 plugins as directories, not single files\\n\\n- Status: accepted\\n- Date: 2026-10-13\\n- Decision owners: TrendpilotAI\\n- Upstream baseline: OpenCode `2.0.27` (`channel=latest`)\\n\\n## Context\\n\\nOpenCode 2 rejects single-file plugin paths. During a server startup on\\n`/work/.mercor-home/orca/workspaces/activegraph-surrealdb/integration-activegraph-adaptor`\\nthe loader emitted:\\n\\n```\\nWARN message=\\\"failed to load plugin\\\"\\n     target=/home/mercor/.config/opencode/plugins/orca-opencode2-status\\n     ref=err_97f42f88\\n     cause=\\\"Cause([Die(Error: ENOENT: no such file or directory,\\n              stat '/home/mercor/.config/opencode/plugins/orca-opencode2-status')])\\\"\\n```\\n\\nThe plugin source file existed at\\n`/home/mercor/.config/opencode/plugins/orca-opencode2-status.js` (1651 lines,\\n72 167 B). OpenCode resolved its `id` to `orca-opencode2-status.js`, then ran\\n`stat()` on the path **without** the extension (`orca-opencode2-status`) to\\nperform a directory-package probe. That path did not exist, the probe raised\\n`ENOENT`, and the plugin was dropped even though the file itself was\\nwell-formed.\\n\\nOpenCode 2 explicitly says so for configured paths:\\n\\n```\\nWARN message=\\\"configured plugin path must be a directory\\\"\\n     target=/work/mercor-work/activegraph-surrealdb/tools/opencode/beads-audit.ts\\n```\\n\\nThe two correctly-shaped plugins already in this environment both use a\\ndirectory layout: `plugins/beads-audit/index.ts` and\\n`plugins/orca-opencode2-status-tui/tui.js`. The legacy single-file\\n`plugins/orca-opencode2-status.js` was left over from the OpenCode 1.x\\ndiscovery convention and is the only file the loader rejects on this machine.\\n\\n## Decision\\n\\nEvery OpenCode 2 plugin that this project owns — under any name — must be\\ninstalled as a directory under `~/.config/opencode/plugins/<name>/` containing\\nthe entry file (`index.js`, `index.ts`, `tui.js`, or whatever the loader\\nrecognises for that plugin id). The single-file\\n`~/.config/opencode/plugins/<name>.<ext>` shape is no longer valid and must\\nnot be reintroduced.\\n\\nConcretely, on this workstation:\\n\\n- `plugins/orca-opencode2-status.js` (single file, 1651 lines, id `orca-opencode2-status`)\\n  is moved to `plugins/orca-opencode2-status/index.js`.\\n- `plugins/orca-opencode2-status-tui/tui.js` is the TUI sub-plugin loaded via\\n  a relative URL inside the parent plugin; its shape is unchanged.\\n- `plugins/beads-audit/index.ts` is unchanged and continues to load.\\n\\nThe move required one internal path correction at line 1125 of\\n`orca-opencode2-status/index.js`. After the move, `import.meta.url` resolves\\nto `…/plugins/orca-opencode2-status/index.js`, so the sibling reference\\n`./orca-opencode2-status-tui/tui.js` had to become\\n`../orca-opencode2-status-tui/tui.js` to keep pointing at the same file. A\\n`node`-level replay of that URL confirmed it resolves to the existing TUI\\nsub-plugin (md5 `116859f74b61e625d14b564475f8b0f4`) and the runtime\\n`statSync(...).isFile()` check at line 1250 still returns `true`.\\n\\nA repeatable installer is provided at `scripts/install-opencode-plugins.sh`\\nthat encodes the directory-package layout for any plugin this project ships.\\nFor each plugin it accepts a `--name <dir-name>` and `--source <canonical-file>`\\nargument, removes any legacy single-file\\n`~/.config/opencode/plugins/<name>.<ext>`, places the entry file at\\n`~/.config/opencode/plugins/<name>/index.<ext>`, and verifies that the file is\\npresent and readable.\\n\\n## Consequences\\n\\n- The plugin source-of-truth must live next to the repo (here:\\n  `/work/mercor-work/activegraph-surrealdb/tools/opencode/<name>/index.<ext>`)\\n  so that the install script is reproducible. The repo does not currently\\n  vend the plugin source under `tools/opencode/`; that vendoring is owned by\\n  the deploy pipeline, not this repository.\\n- Any plugin author writing OpenCode plugins for this project must use the\\n  directory layout. Single-file installs will fail the loader with\\n  `ENOENT stat '<name>'` and the plugin will be silently dropped.\\n- Plugins that load other plugins via `new URL(\\\"<other-plugin>/entry.js\\\",\\n  import.meta.url)` must recheck their relative paths after the move. The\\n  rule is: the relative URL is one level deeper than before, so `./` becomes\\n  `../` for any sibling plugin that lived in the parent plugins directory.\\n- The loader error is `WARN`, not `ERROR`. Quietly dropped plugins will not\\n  surface in the UI; the only signal is the server log. Future CI must grep\\n  `~/.local/share/opencode/log/opencode.log` for\\n  `failed to load plugin` after install.\\n\"}","message_id":"msg_13339f1590011FUvu1ofOt4vCQ","result":"{\"output\":{\"operation\":\"write\",\"target\":\"/work/.mercor-home/orca/workspaces/activegraph-surrealdb/integration-activegraph-adaptor/docs/adr/0004-opencode-plugin-v2-directory-layout.md\",\"resource\":\"docs/adr/0004-opencode-plugin-v2-directory-layout.md\",\"existed\":false},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Created file successfully: docs/adr/0004-opencode-plugin-v2-directory-layout.md\"}]}","session_id":"ses_eccd12d4cffe3Dd6d2N0q7gQQs","status":"completed"}}
{"id":"int-78bf9899cd1dba7d747acf3f04831d63","kind":"tool_call","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:06:55.496Z","actor":"opencode","tool_name":"write","extra":{"call_id":"call_fn9OaMmM0Q9zu8cGnxtaRJis","duration_ms":16,"input":"{\"path\":\"/work/.mercor-home/orca/workspaces/activegraph-surrealdb/integration-activegraph-adaptor/scripts/install-opencode-plugins.sh\",\"content\":\"#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n# install-opencode-plugins.sh\\n#\\n# Package OpenCode 2 plugins as directories and install them under\\n# ~/.config/opencode/plugins/. OpenCode 2 rejects single-file plugin paths\\n# (a flat ~/.config/opencode/plugins/<name>.<ext> raises ENOENT on its\\n# directory-package probe); every plugin must live in its own directory with\\n# an entry file. See docs/adr/0004-opencode-plugin-v2-directory-layout.md\\n# for the full rationale (ref err_97f42f88).\\n#\\n# Usage:\\n#\\n#   scripts/install-opencode-plugins.sh --name <plugin-dir> --source <file>\\n#\\n# Arguments:\\n#\\n#   --name <plugin-dir>     Directory name under ~/.config/opencode/plugins/\\n#                           (e.g. \\\"orca-opencode2-status\\\", \\\"beads-audit\\\").\\n#   --source <file>         Canonical entry file (absolute path or relative\\n#                           to the project root). The extension is preserved\\n#                           so the loader picks up the right parser (.js ->\\n#                           Node ESM, .ts -> Bun/Node TS).\\n#   --plugins-dir <dir>     Override the install root. Defaults to\\n#                           $HOME/.config/opencode/plugins.\\n#   --dry-run               Print the actions that would be taken without\\n#                           touching the filesystem.\\n#   -h, --help              Show this message.\\n#\\n# Each invocation is idempotent: re-running it with the same arguments\\n# reproduces the same directory layout and the same entry file. The script\\n# also removes any legacy single-file\\n# ~/.config/opencode/plugins/<plugin-dir><ext> that the OpenCode 1 layout\\n# left behind, because that file is what the OpenCode 2 loader still tries\\n# to scan.\\n\\nset -euo pipefail\\n\\nPLUGINS_DIR=\\\"${HOME}/.config/opencode/plugins\\\"\\nPLUGIN_NAME=\\\"\\\"\\nSOURCE_FILE=\\\"\\\"\\nDRY_RUN=0\\n\\nusage() {\\n  sed -n '2,30p' \\\"$0\\\" | sed 's/^# \\\\{0,1\\\\}//'\\n}\\n\\ndie() {\\n  echo \\\"install-opencode-plugins: $*\\\" >&2\\n  exit 1\\n}\\n\\nwhile [ \\\"$#\\\" -gt 0 ]; do\\n  case \\\"$1\\\" in\\n    --name)        PLUGIN_NAME=\\\"${2:?}\\\"; shift 2 ;;\\n    --source)      SOURCE_FILE=\\\"${2:?}\\\"; shift 2 ;;\\n    --plugins-dir) PLUGINS_DIR=\\\"${2:?}\\\"; shift 2 ;;\\n    --dry-run)     DRY_RUN=1; shift ;;\\n    -h|--help)     usage; exit 0 ;;\\n    *)             die \\\"unknown argument: $1 (try --help)\\\" ;;\\n  esac\\ndone\\n\\n[ -n \\\"$PLUGIN_NAME\\\" ] || die \\\"--name is required (try --help)\\\"\\n[ -n \\\"$SOURCE_FILE\\\" ] || die \\\"--source is required (try --help)\\\"\\n\\n# Source must exist and have an extension the loader recognises.\\n[ -f \\\"$SOURCE_FILE\\\" ] || die \\\"--source not found or not a file: $SOURCE_FILE\\\"\\n\\nSOURCE_ABS=\\\"$(cd \\\"$(dirname \\\"$SOURCE_FILE\\\")\\\" && pwd)/$(basename \\\"$SOURCE_FILE\\\")\\\"\\nEXT=\\\"${SOURCE_ABS##*.}\\\"\\ncase \\\"$EXT\\\" in\\n  js|ts|mjs|cjs) ;;\\n  *) die \\\"unsupported plugin extension: .$EXT (expected .js, .ts, .mjs, or .cjs)\\\" ;;\\nesac\\n\\n# What we want at the end:\\n#   $PLUGINS_DIR/$PLUGIN_NAME/index.$EXT\\nTARGET_DIR=\\\"$PLUGINS_DIR/$PLUGIN_NAME\\\"\\nTARGET_FILE=\\\"$TARGET_DIR/index.$EXT\\\"\\n\\n# What the legacy / unwanted shape looks like:\\n#   $PLUGINS_DIR/$PLUGIN_NAME.$EXT  (single-file, will fail OpenCode 2)\\nLEGACY_FILE=\\\"$PLUGINS_DIR/$PLUGIN_NAME.$EXT\\\"\\n\\nrun() {\\n  if [ \\\"$DRY_RUN\\\" = \\\"1\\\" ]; then\\n    echo \\\"[dry-run] $*\\\"\\n  else\\n    \\\"$@\\\"\\n  fi\\n}\\n\\necho \\\"plugins-dir: $PLUGINS_DIR\\\"\\necho \\\"name:        $PLUGIN_NAME\\\"\\necho \\\"source:      $SOURCE_ABS\\\"\\necho \\\"target-dir:  $TARGET_DIR\\\"\\necho \\\"target-file: $TARGET_FILE\\\"\\necho \\\"legacy-file: $LEGACY_FILE\\\"\\n\\n# 1. Remove the legacy single-file layout if present. This is the file that\\n#    the OpenCode 2 loader still scans (and then fails on with ENOENT).\\nif [ -e \\\"$LEGACY_FILE\\\" ] && [ ! -d \\\"$LEGACY_FILE\\\" ]; then\\n  run mv \\\"$LEGACY_FILE\\\" \\\"$LEGACY_FILE.disabled-by-install-opencode-plugins.$(date -u +%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ)\\\"\\nfi\\n\\n# 2. Make the directory package.\\nrun mkdir -p \\\"$TARGET_DIR\\\"\\n\\n# 3. Drop the entry file in.\\nrun cp \\\"$SOURCE_ABS\\\" \\\"$TARGET_FILE\\\"\\nrun chmod 0644 \\\"$TARGET_FILE\\\"\\n\\n# 4. Verify. node's statSync on the target must succeed and the file must\\n#    be readable. We do not import the plugin here; the loader will do its\\n#    own probe on the next reconciliation cycle.\\nif [ \\\"$DRY_RUN\\\" = \\\"0\\\" ]; then\\n  node -e \\\"\\n    const fs = require('fs');\\n    const st = fs.statSync(process.argv[1]);\\n    if (!st.isFile()) throw new Error('not a file');\\n    const bytes = fs.readFileSync(process.argv[1]);\\n    if (bytes.length === 0) throw new Error('empty file');\\n    console.log('verified:', process.argv[1], '(' + bytes.length + ' bytes)');\\n  \\\" \\\"$TARGET_FILE\\\"\\nfi\\n\\n# 5. Reminder. The loader does not re-scan plugins mid-run; reconciliation\\n#    happens on the next server event (config change, restart, periodic\\n#    trigger). If you need the plugin to be active in the current OpenCode\\n#    process, restart it after running this script.\\necho\\necho \\\"installed. Trigger a plugin reconciliation by restarting OpenCode\\\"\\necho \\\"or by editing ~/.config/opencode/opencode.json (a no-op edit suffices).\\\"\\n\"}","message_id":"msg_13339f1590011FUvu1ofOt4vCQ","result":"{\"output\":{\"operation\":\"write\",\"target\":\"/work/.mercor-home/orca/workspaces/activegraph-surrealdb/integration-activegraph-adaptor/scripts/install-opencode-plugins.sh\",\"resource\":\"scripts/install-opencode-plugins.sh\",\"existed\":false},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Created file successfully: scripts/install-opencode-plugins.sh\"}]}","session_id":"ses_eccd12d4cffe3Dd6d2N0q7gQQs","status":"completed"}}
