{"id":"int-10faf8e3adddb1a6144dffc90ae7ec04","kind":"tool_call","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:22:13.969Z","actor":"opencode","tool_name":"read","extra":{"call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a4f9a14dd8a22b8","duration_ms":37,"input":"{\"path\":\"/work/mercor-work/activegraph-surrealdb/docs/conformance.md\"}","message_id":"msg_133482ad6001ltIPaTJjfJ5FMC","result":"{\"output\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"uri\":\"file:///work/mercor-work/activegraph-surrealdb/docs/conformance.md\",\"name\":\"conformance.md\",\"content\":\"# Conformance and evidence\\n\\nThe repository separates fast API contracts from live database and destructive\\nqualification evidence. A single green test count should not collapse these\\ndifferent claims.\\n\\n## Test layers\\n\\n| Layer | Marker/path | What it establishes |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| Serialization and configuration | unmarked unit tests | Canonical encoding, hashes, redaction, key scoping, and rejected paths |\\n| Write ordering | `tests/test_write_ordering.py` | A rejected append leaves no projected state (ActiveGraph 1.12) |\\n| Released ActiveGraph suites | `tests/integration/*conformance.py` | Compatibility with the public EventStore and GraphStore contracts |\\n| Native query pushdown | `tests/integration/test_graph_pushdown.py` | The query hooks run in SurrealQL, not the Python full-scan fallback |\\n| Projection order | `tests/integration/test_projection_order.py` | Objects read back in the reference store's insertion order, including across reopens |\\n| Schema upgrade | `tests/integration/test_schema_upgrade.py` | An older database upgrades in place; a newer schema is rejected |\\n| Provider invariants | `pytest -m surrealdb` | Real server transactions, isolation, native edges, replay/fork/diff, restart within a live server |\\n| Pack harness | `pytest -m packs tests/packs` | The published pack library loads and projects into one SurrealDB database |\\n| Pack fixture suites | `tests/packs/test_pack_fixtures_on_surrealdb.py` | Each pack's own `fixtures/run_fixtures.py` runs unchanged on SurrealDB-backed stores |\\n| Qualification | `pytest -m qualification` | Exact pinned image/SDK/engine and container restart/kill persistence |\\n| Upstream known issues | `tests/known_issues` | Strict expected failures for lifecycle gaps outside this provider |\\n\\n## Commands\\n\\nInstall the development dependencies, then run the layers explicitly:\\n\\n```bash\\npython -m pip install -e '.[dev]'\\npytest -m 'not surrealdb and not qualification'\\npytest -m surrealdb tests/integration\\nACTIVEGRAPH_PACKS_PATH=/path/to/activegraph-packs pytest -m packs tests/packs\\nACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_QUALIFY=1 pytest -m qualification tests/qualification\\n```\\n\\nThe live layers require the environment described in [deployment.md](deployment.md).\\nThe qualification command must target only the disposable container it is\\nauthorized to restart and kill.\\n\\n## Required invariants\\n\\nPromotion evidence must include at least:\\n\\n- released EventStore and GraphStore conformance;\\n- exact JSON round-trip and literal canonical/hash golden values;\\n- append-before-projection ordering (a rejected append leaves no projection);\\n- native query pushdown for every overridden GraphStore hook;\\n- projected objects returned in the reference store's insertion order;\\n- an in-place, data-preserving schema upgrade and rejection of a newer schema;\\n- loading the published pack library onto one SurrealDB-backed Runtime;\\n- running each pack's own fixture suite on SurrealDB-backed stores, with any\\n  non-portable suite recorded as an explicit expected divergence;\\n- transaction rollback without an orphan event or advanced head;\\n- deterministic same-run stale-writer rejection and independent run progress;\\n- scope/run isolation across reads, clears, truncation, forks, and relations;\\n- native `TYPE RELATION` records with bound `RecordID` endpoints;\\n- replay that clears stale state, marks failure, and becomes ready only on success;\\n- prefix-only forks with traceable parent metadata and independent suffixes;\\n- rejection of unsupported compacted histories;\\n- close/reopen, server restart, and abrupt container termination; and\\n- an existing-database upgrade test before any supported-version change.\\n\\n## Recording evidence\\n\\nA repeatable result records:\\n\\n- repository commit SHA and clean/dirty status;\\n- Python, ActiveGraph, SDK, and server versions;\\n- Docker image digest, command, transport, and storage engine;\\n- exact commands and marker selections;\\n- pass, fail, skip, and expected-failure counts;\\n- host/OS and test timestamp; and\\n- logs for any failure or replay repair.\\n\\nCI status is implementation evidence only for its recorded environment. It is\\nnot a performance benchmark, deployed-service proof, backup proof, or proof that\\nan application has modeled authorization correctly.\\n\\n## Contract-first status\\n\\nTests may intentionally be RED while a contract is being implemented. That is\\nuseful only when the failure is the expected missing behavior. Do not mark a\\ntest xfail, weaken an assertion, or replace a live path with a mock merely to\\nproduce green CI. Make the provider satisfy the contract, then record the green\\ntrace.\\n\",\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"mime\":\"text/markdown\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Read file /work/mercor-work/activegraph-surrealdb/docs/conformance.md, lines 1-84\\n1: # Conformance and evidence\\n2: \\n3: The repository separates fast API contracts from live database and destructive\\n4: qualification evidence. A single green test count should not collapse these\\n5: different claims.\\n6: \\n7: ## Test layers\\n8: \\n9: | Layer | Marker/path | What it establishes |\\n10: | --- | --- | --- |\\n11: | Serialization and configuration | unmarked unit tests | Canonical encoding, hashes, redaction, key scoping, and rejected paths |\\n12: | Write ordering | `tests/test_write_ordering.py` | A rejected append leaves no projected state (ActiveGraph 1.12) |\\n13: | Released ActiveGraph suites | `tests/integration/*conformance.py` | Compatibility with the public EventStore and GraphStore contracts |\\n14: | Native query pushdown | `tests/integration/test_graph_pushdown.py` | The query hooks run in SurrealQL, not the Python full-scan fallback |\\n15: | Projection order | `tests/integration/test_projection_order.py` | Objects read back in the reference store's insertion order, including across reopens |\\n16: | Schema upgrade | `tests/integration/test_schema_upgrade.py` | An older database upgrades in place; a newer schema is rejected |\\n17: | Provider invariants | `pytest -m surrealdb` | Real server transactions, isolation, native edges, replay/fork/diff, restart within a live server |\\n18: | Pack harness | `pytest -m packs tests/packs` | The published pack library loads and projects into one SurrealDB database |\\n19: | Pack fixture suites | `tests/packs/test_pack_fixtures_on_surrealdb.py` | Each pack's own `fixtures/run_fixtures.py` runs unchanged on SurrealDB-backed stores |\\n20: | Qualification | `pytest -m qualification` | Exact pinned image/SDK/engine and container restart/kill persistence |\\n21: | Upstream known issues | `tests/known_issues` | Strict expected failures for lifecycle gaps outside this provider |\\n22: \\n23: ## Commands\\n24: \\n25: Install the development dependencies, then run the layers explicitly:\\n26: \\n27: ```bash\\n28: python -m pip install -e '.[dev]'\\n29: pytest -m 'not surrealdb and not qualification'\\n30: pytest -m surrealdb tests/integration\\n31: ACTIVEGRAPH_PACKS_PATH=/path/to/activegraph-packs pytest -m packs tests/packs\\n32: ACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_QUALIFY=1 pytest -m qualification tests/qualification\\n33: ```\\n34: \\n35: The live layers require the environment described in [deployment.md](deployment.md).\\n36: The qualification command must target only the disposable container it is\\n37: authorized to restart and kill.\\n38: \\n39: ## Required invariants\\n40: \\n41: Promotion evidence must include at least:\\n42: \\n43: - released EventStore and GraphStore conformance;\\n44: - exact JSON round-trip and literal canonical/hash golden values;\\n45: - append-before-projection ordering (a rejected append leaves no projection);\\n46: - native query pushdown for every overridden GraphStore hook;\\n47: - projected objects returned in the reference store's insertion order;\\n48: - an in-place, data-preserving schema upgrade and rejection of a newer schema;\\n49: - loading the published pack library onto one SurrealDB-backed Runtime;\\n50: - running each pack's own fixture suite on SurrealDB-backed stores, with any\\n51:   non-portable suite recorded as an explicit expected divergence;\\n52: - transaction rollback without an orphan event or advanced head;\\n53: - deterministic same-run stale-writer rejection and independent run progress;\\n54: - scope/run isolation across reads, clears, truncation, forks, and relations;\\n55: - native `TYPE RELATION` records with bound `RecordID` endpoints;\\n56: - replay that clears stale state, marks failure, and becomes ready only on success;\\n57: - prefix-only forks with traceable parent metadata and independent suffixes;\\n58: - rejection of unsupported compacted histories;\\n59: - close/reopen, server restart, and abrupt container termination; and\\n60: - an existing-database upgrade test before any supported-version change.\\n61: \\n62: ## Recording evidence\\n63: \\n64: A repeatable result records:\\n65: \\n66: - repository commit SHA and clean/dirty status;\\n67: - Python, ActiveGraph, SDK, and server versions;\\n68: - Docker image digest, command, transport, and storage engine;\\n69: - exact commands and marker selections;\\n70: - pass, fail, skip, and expected-failure counts;\\n71: - host/OS and test timestamp; and\\n72: - logs for any failure or replay repair.\\n73: \\n74: CI status is implementation evidence only for its recorded environment. It is\\n75: not a performance benchmark, deployed-service proof, backup proof, or proof that\\n76: an application has modeled authorization correctly.\\n77: \\n78: ## Contract-first status\\n79: \\n80: Tests may intentionally be RED while a contract is being implemented. That is\\n81: useful only when the failure is the expected missing behavior. Do not mark a\\n82: test xfail, weaken an assertion, or replace a live path with a mock merely to\\n83: produce green CI. Make the provider satisfy the contract, then record the green\\n84: trace.\"}],\"metadata\":{\"truncated\":false}}","session_id":"ses_ecce71390ffe11p6yPgte61c3p","status":"completed"}}
