{"id":"int-202839f20066f4dbcce87a248f05c0cd","kind":"tool_call","created_at":"2026-10-13T16:04:20.291Z","actor":"opencode","tool_name":"read","extra":{"call_id":"call_d9efc8be328e46feb77c66e2","duration_ms":27,"input":"{\"path\":\"/home/mercor/orca/workspaces/activegraph-surrealdb/mercor-vm/tests/qualification/test_surrealkv_engine.py\"}","message_id":"msg_13601c8c0001786glMxw3C1VA0","result":"{\"output\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"uri\":\"file:///home/mercor/orca/workspaces/activegraph-surrealdb/mercor-vm/tests/qualification/test_surrealkv_engine.py\",\"name\":\"test_surrealkv_engine.py\",\"content\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"Lane C (surrealkv engine) evidence for ADR 0003: beta engine qualification.\\n\\nNon-gating exploration-lane evidence behind the existing ``qualification``\\nmarker. Ladder step V7 runs it with ``ACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_TEST_ENGINE=\\nsurrealkv`` on the engine's own volume; the test skips whenever that variable\\nis not ``surrealkv``, so the stable RocksDB qualification run (V3) never\\nattempts it.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nimport pytest\\n\\nfrom activegraph_surrealdb import SurrealEventStore\\n\\n\\n@pytest.mark.qualification\\ndef test_surrealkv_engine_serves_the_provider(qualification_environment) -> None:\\n    if qualification_environment.engine != \\\"surrealkv\\\":\\n        pytest.skip(\\\"set ACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_TEST_ENGINE=surrealkv for the lane C evidence\\\")\\n\\n    assert qualification_environment.storage_url == \\\"surrealkv:///data/activegraph.db\\\"\\n    events = SurrealEventStore(\\n        qualification_environment.config,\\n        run_id=\\\"environment\\\",\\n        scope=\\\"qualification\\\",\\n    )\\n    assert events.server_version() == \\\"3.3.0\\\"\\n    events.close()\\n\",\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"mime\":\"application/octet-stream\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Read file /home/mercor/orca/workspaces/activegraph-surrealdb/mercor-vm/tests/qualification/test_surrealkv_engine.py, lines 1-29\\n1: \\\"\\\"\\\"Lane C (surrealkv engine) evidence for ADR 0003: beta engine qualification.\\n2: \\n3: Non-gating exploration-lane evidence behind the existing ``qualification``\\n4: marker. Ladder step V7 runs it with ``ACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_TEST_ENGINE=\\n5: surrealkv`` on the engine's own volume; the test skips whenever that variable\\n6: is not ``surrealkv``, so the stable RocksDB qualification run (V3) never\\n7: attempts it.\\n8: \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n9: \\n10: from __future__ import annotations\\n11: \\n12: import pytest\\n13: \\n14: from activegraph_surrealdb import SurrealEventStore\\n15: \\n16: \\n17: @pytest.mark.qualification\\n18: def test_surrealkv_engine_serves_the_provider(qualification_environment) -> None:\\n19:     if qualification_environment.engine != \\\"surrealkv\\\":\\n20:         pytest.skip(\\\"set ACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_TEST_ENGINE=surrealkv for the lane C evidence\\\")\\n21: \\n22:     assert qualification_environment.storage_url == \\\"surrealkv:///data/activegraph.db\\\"\\n23:     events = SurrealEventStore(\\n24:         qualification_environment.config,\\n25:         run_id=\\\"environment\\\",\\n26:         scope=\\\"qualification\\\",\\n27:     )\\n28:     assert events.server_version() == \\\"3.3.0\\\"\\n29:     events.close()\"}],\"metadata\":{\"truncated\":false}}","session_id":"ses_ecd1f104affewX9x4cIqy5fLvq","status":"completed"}}
{"id":"int-483eb36a9b4d7c8b7e5d9cf53af57a55","kind":"tool_call","created_at":"2026-10-13T16:04:20.3Z","actor":"opencode","tool_name":"read","extra":{"call_id":"call_9f27a5ef7d14444aa0a2364f","duration_ms":35,"input":"{\"path\":\"/home/mercor/orca/workspaces/activegraph-surrealdb/mercor-vm/tests/embedded/test_embedded_transactions.py\"}","message_id":"msg_13601c8c0001786glMxw3C1VA0","result":"{\"output\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"uri\":\"file:///home/mercor/orca/workspaces/activegraph-surrealdb/mercor-vm/tests/embedded/test_embedded_transactions.py\",\"name\":\"test_embedded_transactions.py\",\"content\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"Lane D (embedded engine) evidence for ADR 0003: transactions are refused.\\n\\nNon-gating exploration-lane evidence, selected only with ``-m embedded``\\n(ladder step V8). The embedded engine ships as the ``surrealdb_embedded``\\nextension, so this module skips wherever that extension is absent — including\\nthe default development venv, whose ``surrealdb==2.0.0`` pin has no embedded\\nengine at all. Ladder step V8 runs it from the isolated ``.venv-embedded``\\nholding ``surrealdb[embedded]==3.0.0b10``.\\n\\n``attach``, ``begin``, ``commit``, and ``cancel`` raising\\n``UnsupportedFeatureError`` is the expected rejection evidence recorded by\\nADR 0003: multi-session and client-side transactions exist only on WebSocket\\nconnections.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nimport pytest\\n\\npytest.importorskip(\\\"surrealdb_embedded\\\")\\n\\nfrom surrealdb import Surreal  # noqa: E402\\nfrom surrealdb.errors import UnsupportedFeatureError  # noqa: E402\\n\\n_REFUSAL = \\\"only supported for WebSocket connections\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef _assert_transactions_are_refused(connection) -> None:\\n    with pytest.raises(UnsupportedFeatureError, match=_REFUSAL):\\n        connection.attach()\\n    with pytest.raises(UnsupportedFeatureError, match=_REFUSAL):\\n        connection.begin()\\n    with pytest.raises(UnsupportedFeatureError, match=_REFUSAL):\\n        connection.commit(\\\"unused-transaction\\\")\\n    with pytest.raises(UnsupportedFeatureError, match=_REFUSAL):\\n        connection.cancel(\\\"unused-transaction\\\")\\n\\n\\n@pytest.mark.embedded\\ndef test_memory_engine_refuses_client_side_transactions() -> None:\\n    with Surreal(\\\"mem://\\\") as connection:\\n        connection.use(\\\"embedded\\\", \\\"embedded\\\")\\n        _assert_transactions_are_refused(connection)\\n\\n\\n@pytest.mark.embedded\\ndef test_surrealkv_engine_refuses_client_side_transactions(tmp_path) -> None:\\n    with Surreal(f\\\"surrealkv://{tmp_path}/embedded-engine.skv\\\") as connection:\\n        connection.use(\\\"embedded\\\", \\\"embedded\\\")\\n        _assert_transactions_are_refused(connection)\\n\",\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"mime\":\"application/octet-stream\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Read file /home/mercor/orca/workspaces/activegraph-surrealdb/mercor-vm/tests/embedded/test_embedded_transactions.py, lines 1-50\\n1: \\\"\\\"\\\"Lane D (embedded engine) evidence for ADR 0003: transactions are refused.\\n2: \\n3: Non-gating exploration-lane evidence, selected only with ``-m embedded``\\n4: (ladder step V8). The embedded engine ships as the ``surrealdb_embedded``\\n5: extension, so this module skips wherever that extension is absent — including\\n6: the default development venv, whose ``surrealdb==2.0.0`` pin has no embedded\\n7: engine at all. Ladder step V8 runs it from the isolated ``.venv-embedded``\\n8: holding ``surrealdb[embedded]==3.0.0b10``.\\n9: \\n10: ``attach``, ``begin``, ``commit``, and ``cancel`` raising\\n11: ``UnsupportedFeatureError`` is the expected rejection evidence recorded by\\n12: ADR 0003: multi-session and client-side transactions exist only on WebSocket\\n13: connections.\\n14: \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n15: \\n16: from __future__ import annotations\\n17: \\n18: import pytest\\n19: \\n20: pytest.importorskip(\\\"surrealdb_embedded\\\")\\n21: \\n22: from surrealdb import Surreal  # noqa: E402\\n23: from surrealdb.errors import UnsupportedFeatureError  # noqa: E402\\n24: \\n25: _REFUSAL = \\\"only supported for WebSocket connections\\\"\\n26: \\n27: \\n28: def _assert_transactions_are_refused(connection) -> None:\\n29:     with pytest.raises(UnsupportedFeatureError, match=_REFUSAL):\\n30:         connection.attach()\\n31:     with pytest.raises(UnsupportedFeatureError, match=_REFUSAL):\\n32:         connection.begin()\\n33:     with pytest.raises(UnsupportedFeatureError, match=_REFUSAL):\\n34:         connection.commit(\\\"unused-transaction\\\")\\n35:     with pytest.raises(UnsupportedFeatureError, match=_REFUSAL):\\n36:         connection.cancel(\\\"unused-transaction\\\")\\n37: \\n38: \\n39: @pytest.mark.embedded\\n40: def test_memory_engine_refuses_client_side_transactions() -> None:\\n41:     with Surreal(\\\"mem://\\\") as connection:\\n42:         connection.use(\\\"embedded\\\", \\\"embedded\\\")\\n43:         _assert_transactions_are_refused(connection)\\n44: \\n45: \\n46: @pytest.mark.embedded\\n47: def test_surrealkv_engine_refuses_client_side_transactions(tmp_path) -> None:\\n48:     with Surreal(f\\\"surrealkv://{tmp_path}/embedded-engine.skv\\\") as connection:\\n49:         connection.use(\\\"embedded\\\", \\\"embedded\\\")\\n50:         _assert_transactions_are_refused(connection)\"}],\"metadata\":{\"truncated\":false}}","session_id":"ses_ecd1f104affewX9x4cIqy5fLvq","status":"completed"}}
