{"id":"int-55702c6368ce099fa3643518a9a02391","kind":"tool_call","created_at":"2026-10-13T16:55:32.157Z","actor":"opencode","tool_name":"read","extra":{"call_id":"call_fbbd186383914693b7a5865c","duration_ms":8,"input":"{\"path\":\"/home/mercor/orca/workspaces/activegraph-surrealdb/mercor-vm/README.md\",\"offset\":78,\"limit\":60}","message_id":"msg_13630b5ac0019FidbXK3DnlLbZ","result":"{\"output\":{\"type\":\"text-page\",\"content\":\"    F -->|diff outcomes| A\\n```\\n\\nThe two stores may share a namespace and database, but they do not share an\\nActiveGraph-owned transaction. On ActiveGraph `1.12.0`, a runtime operation\\n<<<<<<< HEAD\\nappends its event before projecting it. A failed append changes nothing; a\\nfailed projection leaves an event logged without its projection, and replay\\nis the documented repair path. The provider does **not** claim atomic\\nevent-plus-projection acceptance.\\n=======\\npersists its event before projecting it (CONTRACT v1.11 #2), so a rejected\\nappend leaves no projected state. The projection is still a separate write: if\\nit fails after a successful append, replay is the documented repair path and the\\nprovider does **not** claim atomic event-plus-projection acceptance.\\n\\n## Taking advantage of one database\\n\\nBecause the event log and the graph projection share one deployment, the\\nprovider pushes the released `GraphStore` query hooks down into SurrealQL rather\\nthan scanning in Python. Object type filters, relation source/target/type\\nfilters, existence probes, and the undirected neighbourhood walk are all bound\\nSurrealQL; `match_chain` composes those pushed-down primitives hop by hop. The\\nrich `where` predicate stays with ActiveGraph and is returned as an exact\\nresidual, per the released contract. Schema v2 adds the indexes those queries\\nuse. See [ADR 0003](docs/adr/0003-native-query-pushdown.md).\\n\\n## Pack library\\n\\nThe provider ships a harness that loads the published\\n[ActiveGraph pack library](https://github.com/yoheinakajima/activegraph-packs)\\nonto a `Runtime` whose event log and graph projection both live in SurrealDB:\\n\\n```python\\nfrom activegraph_surrealdb import SurrealConfig, build_runtime\\n\\nhandle = build_runtime(\\n    SurrealConfig(endpoint=\\\"ws://127.0.0.1:8000\\\", namespace=\\\"activegraph\\\",\\n                  database=\\\"assistant\\\", username=\\\"root\\\", password=\\\"root\\\"),\\n    run_id=\\\"run_1\\\",\\n    scope=\\\"assistant\\\",\\n)\\nhandle.runtime.graph.add_object(\\\"source\\\", {\\\"kind\\\": \\\"note\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"...\\\"})\\nhandle.runtime.run_until_idle()\\nhandle.close()\\n```\\n\\nPoint the harness at a checkout with `ACTIVEGRAPH_PACKS_PATH` (default: the\\nreference checkout). The `packs` test lane proves core, infrastructure,\\ncommunication (including composio), bridges, mcp, attention, evolution,\\nsemantic_extraction, eval_outcome, activity_normalizer, connector_control,\\nskills, usage, and the importers all load and project into one SurrealDB\\ndatabase.\\n>>>>>>> 8e1c86e (feat: enable the harness — ActiveGraph 1.12, SurrealQL pushdown, and the pack library on one store (#8))\\n\\nRead the full [architecture](docs/architecture.md) and [security model](docs/security-model.md).\\n\\n## Appropriate use cases\\n\\n- auditable agent or workflow state where alternative decisions need comparison;\",\"mime\":\"text/markdown\",\"offset\":78,\"truncated\":true,\"next\":138},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Read file /home/mercor/orca/workspaces/activegraph-surrealdb/mercor-vm/README.md, lines 78-137\\n78:     F -->|diff outcomes| A\\n79: ```\\n80: \\n81: The two stores may share a namespace and database, but they do not share an\\n82: ActiveGraph-owned transaction. On ActiveGraph `1.12.0`, a runtime operation\\n83: <<<<<<< HEAD\\n84: appends its event before projecting it. A failed append changes nothing; a\\n85: failed projection leaves an event logged without its projection, and replay\\n86: is the documented repair path. The provider does **not** claim atomic\\n87: event-plus-projection acceptance.\\n88: =======\\n89: persists its event before projecting it (CONTRACT v1.11 #2), so a rejected\\n90: append leaves no projected state. The projection is still a separate write: if\\n91: it fails after a successful append, replay is the documented repair path and the\\n92: provider does **not** claim atomic event-plus-projection acceptance.\\n93: \\n94: ## Taking advantage of one database\\n95: \\n96: Because the event log and the graph projection share one deployment, the\\n97: provider pushes the released `GraphStore` query hooks down into SurrealQL rather\\n98: than scanning in Python. Object type filters, relation source/target/type\\n99: filters, existence probes, and the undirected neighbourhood walk are all bound\\n100: SurrealQL; `match_chain` composes those pushed-down primitives hop by hop. The\\n101: rich `where` predicate stays with ActiveGraph and is returned as an exact\\n102: residual, per the released contract. Schema v2 adds the indexes those queries\\n103: use. See [ADR 0003](docs/adr/0003-native-query-pushdown.md).\\n104: \\n105: ## Pack library\\n106: \\n107: The provider ships a harness that loads the published\\n108: [ActiveGraph pack library](https://github.com/yoheinakajima/activegraph-packs)\\n109: onto a `Runtime` whose event log and graph projection both live in SurrealDB:\\n110: \\n111: ```python\\n112: from activegraph_surrealdb import SurrealConfig, build_runtime\\n113: \\n114: handle = build_runtime(\\n115:     SurrealConfig(endpoint=\\\"ws://127.0.0.1:8000\\\", namespace=\\\"activegraph\\\",\\n116:                   database=\\\"assistant\\\", username=\\\"root\\\", password=\\\"root\\\"),\\n117:     run_id=\\\"run_1\\\",\\n118:     scope=\\\"assistant\\\",\\n119: )\\n120: handle.runtime.graph.add_object(\\\"source\\\", {\\\"kind\\\": \\\"note\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"...\\\"})\\n121: handle.runtime.run_until_idle()\\n122: handle.close()\\n123: ```\\n124: \\n125: Point the harness at a checkout with `ACTIVEGRAPH_PACKS_PATH` (default: the\\n126: reference checkout). The `packs` test lane proves core, infrastructure,\\n127: communication (including composio), bridges, mcp, attention, evolution,\\n128: semantic_extraction, eval_outcome, activity_normalizer, connector_control,\\n129: skills, usage, and the importers all load and project into one SurrealDB\\n130: database.\\n131: >>>>>>> 8e1c86e (feat: enable the harness — ActiveGraph 1.12, SurrealQL pushdown, and the pack library on one store (#8))\\n132: \\n133: Read the full [architecture](docs/architecture.md) and [security model](docs/security-model.md).\\n134: \\n135: ## Appropriate use cases\\n136: \\n137: - auditable agent or workflow state where alternative decisions need comparison;\\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 138]\"}],\"metadata\":{\"truncated\":true}}","session_id":"ses_ecd1f104affewX9x4cIqy5fLvq","status":"completed"}}
{"id":"int-1be58038a4c9dc4f130d96ea2aa1f89a","kind":"tool_call","created_at":"2026-10-13T16:55:32.163Z","actor":"opencode","tool_name":"read","extra":{"call_id":"call_ef1fb6777e904c07aa3e62c9","duration_ms":14,"input":"{\"path\":\"/home/mercor/orca/workspaces/activegraph-surrealdb/mercor-vm/docs/compatibility.md\",\"offset\":40,\"limit\":70}","message_id":"msg_13630b5ac0019FidbXK3DnlLbZ","result":"{\"output\":{\"type\":\"text-page\",\"content\":\"\\n## ActiveGraph lifecycle limitations\\n\\nThe provider does not patch private ActiveGraph runtime methods or register a\\ndatabase URL scheme. Stores are constructed explicitly.\\n\\n<<<<<<< HEAD\\n- [ActiveGraph PR #78](https://github.com/yoheinakajima/activegraph/pull/78)\\n  proposed append-before-projection ordering and stronger run ownership. The\\n  released `1.12.0` baseline incorporates it: `Graph.emit` appends to the\\n  event store before projecting, and a failed append changes no graph,\\n  queue, projection, or observer state.\\n- [ActiveGraph issue #81](https://github.com/yoheinakajima/activegraph/issues/81)\\n  tracks `Runtime.load()` creating an unknown run instead of failing without a\\n  mutation. It is re-evaluated against `1.12.0`; the strict test stays until\\n  the fix is proven.\\n- [ActiveGraph issue #82](https://github.com/yoheinakajima/activegraph/issues/82)\\n  tracks replay into a stale supplied projection without clearing it first.\\n  It is re-evaluated against `1.12.0` the same way.\\n\\nThe ordering item is now a positive `1.12.0` contract test. The load and\\nstale-projection reproductions remain strict expected-failure tests until\\ntheir re-evaluation is proven. An upstream fix that makes one unexpectedly\\npass is a prompt to review and update the provider, not to delete the test\\nblindly.\\n\\n`1.12.0` also closes the patch vocabulary to `update` and `replace`:\\n`Patch` construction and replay both reject any other op with\\n`InvalidPatchOperation`. Provider-written stores are unaffected, because\\nevery stored patch passed framework validation at write time. A store\\nwritten by another `1.10`-era producer can hold `create` or `remove` ops\\n(which `1.10` accepted without validation and silently mis-applied); under\\n`1.12.0` such rows fail loudly at replay and at projection reads, with an\\nupstream error type rather than `SurrealProviderError`. That data requires\\nmigration or discard, not silent reads.\\n=======\\n- ActiveGraph `1.12.0` ships the append-before-projection ordering proposed by\\n  [PR #78](https://github.com/yoheinakajima/activegraph/pull/78) as CONTRACT\\n  v1.11 #2: a rejected durable append changes no projected state. The provider\\n  asserts that invariant directly in `tests/test_write_ordering.py`.\\n- [ActiveGraph issue #81](https://github.com/yoheinakajima/activegraph/issues/81)\\n  tracks `Runtime.load()` creating an unknown run instead of failing without a\\n  mutation. Still open in `1.12.0`.\\n- [ActiveGraph issue #82](https://github.com/yoheinakajima/activegraph/issues/82)\\n  tracks replay into a stale supplied projection without clearing it first.\\n  Still open in `1.12.0`.\\n\\nStrict expected-failure tests keep the remaining limitations visible. An\\nupstream fix that makes one unexpectedly pass is a prompt to review and update\\nthe provider, not to delete the test blindly.\\n>>>>>>> 8e1c86e (feat: enable the harness — ActiveGraph 1.12, SurrealQL pushdown, and the pack library on one store (#8))\\n\\n## Compaction\\n\\nReplay and fork helpers support uncompacted event histories only. They reject a\\nlog beginning with `runtime.snapshot` and reject a fork point outside the\\nretained prefix. Snapshot materialization, compaction horizons, and legacy\\nmigration are not implemented by guessing at private runtime state.\\n\\n## Claims this matrix does not make\\n\\n<<<<<<< HEAD\\n- ActiveGraph compatibility beyond the pinned `1.12.0` baseline.\\n=======\\n- ActiveGraph `1.13` compatibility before an upstream release is tested.\\n>>>>>>> 8e1c86e (feat: enable the harness — ActiveGraph 1.12, SurrealQL pushdown, and the pack library on one store (#8))\\n- Wire or storage compatibility across arbitrary SurrealDB versions.\\n- Distributed SurrealDB, SurrealDB Cloud, or multi-node high availability.\\n- TLS certificate, proxy, or workload-identity qualification.\\n- Atomic event-plus-projection acceptance.\",\"mime\":\"text/markdown\",\"offset\":40,\"truncated\":true,\"next\":110},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Read file /home/mercor/orca/workspaces/activegraph-surrealdb/mercor-vm/docs/compatibility.md, lines 40-109\\n40: \\n41: ## ActiveGraph lifecycle limitations\\n42: \\n43: The provider does not patch private ActiveGraph runtime methods or register a\\n44: database URL scheme. Stores are constructed explicitly.\\n45: \\n46: <<<<<<< HEAD\\n47: - [ActiveGraph PR #78](https://github.com/yoheinakajima/activegraph/pull/78)\\n48:   proposed append-before-projection ordering and stronger run ownership. The\\n49:   released `1.12.0` baseline incorporates it: `Graph.emit` appends to the\\n50:   event store before projecting, and a failed append changes no graph,\\n51:   queue, projection, or observer state.\\n52: - [ActiveGraph issue #81](https://github.com/yoheinakajima/activegraph/issues/81)\\n53:   tracks `Runtime.load()` creating an unknown run instead of failing without a\\n54:   mutation. It is re-evaluated against `1.12.0`; the strict test stays until\\n55:   the fix is proven.\\n56: - [ActiveGraph issue #82](https://github.com/yoheinakajima/activegraph/issues/82)\\n57:   tracks replay into a stale supplied projection without clearing it first.\\n58:   It is re-evaluated against `1.12.0` the same way.\\n59: \\n60: The ordering item is now a positive `1.12.0` contract test. The load and\\n61: stale-projection reproductions remain strict expected-failure tests until\\n62: their re-evaluation is proven. An upstream fix that makes one unexpectedly\\n63: pass is a prompt to review and update the provider, not to delete the test\\n64: blindly.\\n65: \\n66: `1.12.0` also closes the patch vocabulary to `update` and `replace`:\\n67: `Patch` construction and replay both reject any other op with\\n68: `InvalidPatchOperation`. Provider-written stores are unaffected, because\\n69: every stored patch passed framework validation at write time. A store\\n70: written by another `1.10`-era producer can hold `create` or `remove` ops\\n71: (which `1.10` accepted without validation and silently mis-applied); under\\n72: `1.12.0` such rows fail loudly at replay and at projection reads, with an\\n73: upstream error type rather than `SurrealProviderError`. That data requires\\n74: migration or discard, not silent reads.\\n75: =======\\n76: - ActiveGraph `1.12.0` ships the append-before-projection ordering proposed by\\n77:   [PR #78](https://github.com/yoheinakajima/activegraph/pull/78) as CONTRACT\\n78:   v1.11 #2: a rejected durable append changes no projected state. The provider\\n79:   asserts that invariant directly in `tests/test_write_ordering.py`.\\n80: - [ActiveGraph issue #81](https://github.com/yoheinakajima/activegraph/issues/81)\\n81:   tracks `Runtime.load()` creating an unknown run instead of failing without a\\n82:   mutation. Still open in `1.12.0`.\\n83: - [ActiveGraph issue #82](https://github.com/yoheinakajima/activegraph/issues/82)\\n84:   tracks replay into a stale supplied projection without clearing it first.\\n85:   Still open in `1.12.0`.\\n86: \\n87: Strict expected-failure tests keep the remaining limitations visible. An\\n88: upstream fix that makes one unexpectedly pass is a prompt to review and update\\n89: the provider, not to delete the test blindly.\\n90: >>>>>>> 8e1c86e (feat: enable the harness — ActiveGraph 1.12, SurrealQL pushdown, and the pack library on one store (#8))\\n91: \\n92: ## Compaction\\n93: \\n94: Replay and fork helpers support uncompacted event histories only. They reject a\\n95: log beginning with `runtime.snapshot` and reject a fork point outside the\\n96: retained prefix. Snapshot materialization, compaction horizons, and legacy\\n97: migration are not implemented by guessing at private runtime state.\\n98: \\n99: ## Claims this matrix does not make\\n100: \\n101: <<<<<<< HEAD\\n102: - ActiveGraph compatibility beyond the pinned `1.12.0` baseline.\\n103: =======\\n104: - ActiveGraph `1.13` compatibility before an upstream release is tested.\\n105: >>>>>>> 8e1c86e (feat: enable the harness — ActiveGraph 1.12, SurrealQL pushdown, and the pack library on one store (#8))\\n106: - Wire or storage compatibility across arbitrary SurrealDB versions.\\n107: - Distributed SurrealDB, SurrealDB Cloud, or multi-node high availability.\\n108: - TLS certificate, proxy, or workload-identity qualification.\\n109: - Atomic event-plus-projection acceptance.\\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 110]\"}],\"metadata\":{\"truncated\":true}}","session_id":"ses_ecd1f104affewX9x4cIqy5fLvq","status":"completed"}}
