{"id":"int-65f98376986708cc312884243bdcd8d6","kind":"tool_call","created_at":"2026-10-13T16:56:05.446Z","actor":"opencode","tool_name":"read","extra":{"call_id":"call_0aaef7c73c7d49a7a27ddc23","duration_ms":6,"input":"{\"limit\":45,\"offset\":100,\"path\":\"/home/mercor/orca/workspaces/activegraph-surrealdb/mercor-vm/docs/deployment.md\"}","message_id":"msg_136314dbf001FIXTt5CRQvAnlq","result":"{\"output\":{\"type\":\"text-page\",\"content\":\"pytest -m surrealdb tests/integration\\n```\\n\\nTests isolate provider state with generated scopes and runs. Use a disposable\\ndatabase anyway. Do not point the test variables at production, shared staging,\\nor customer data.\\n\\n<<<<<<< HEAD\\n## Studio\\n\\nThe documented visual interface is SurrealDB Studio at\\n`studio.surrealdb.com`, delivered as a hosted web application and a\\ndesktop application. No UI image is pinned in the Compose deployment\\nbecause Studio is not self-hostable; Surrealist, now end-of-life, is not\\nadopted.\\n\\nThe desktop application is the clean path to the local Compose service:\\nconnect to `ws://127.0.0.1:8000` with the `SURREALDB_USER` and\\n`SURREALDB_PASSWORD` values from `.env`, and treat that root identity as\\nlocal-only. A hosted web page reaching a local endpoint is a verification\\nnote, not a claim: whether the hosted page can reach `ws://127.0.0.1:8000`\\nis not verified here, and an operator who needs that path must verify it\\nin their own environment before relying on it.\\n\\nStudio is an operator convenience. Qualification evidence comes from the\\ntest suites, never from a UI session.\\n=======\\n## Pack harness lane\\n\\nThe pack lane loads the external ActiveGraph pack library onto a Runtime whose\\nevent log and graph projection both live in the test database. Point the harness\\nat a checkout:\\n\\n```bash\\nACTIVEGRAPH_PACKS_PATH=/path/to/activegraph-packs pytest -m packs tests/packs\\n```\\n\\nWhen `ACTIVEGRAPH_PACKS_PATH` is unset the harness uses the reference checkout\\nbaked into this environment; the lane skips cleanly when neither is present. The\\nlane is read-only with respect to the pack repository — it imports packs and\\nloads them, and never modifies the checkout.\\n>>>>>>> 8e1c86e (feat: enable the harness — ActiveGraph 1.12, SurrealQL pushdown, and the pack library on one store (#8))\\n\\n## Qualification lane\\n\",\"mime\":\"text/markdown\",\"offset\":100,\"truncated\":true,\"next\":145},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Read file /home/mercor/orca/workspaces/activegraph-surrealdb/mercor-vm/docs/deployment.md, lines 100-144\\n100: pytest -m surrealdb tests/integration\\n101: ```\\n102: \\n103: Tests isolate provider state with generated scopes and runs. Use a disposable\\n104: database anyway. Do not point the test variables at production, shared staging,\\n105: or customer data.\\n106: \\n107: <<<<<<< HEAD\\n108: ## Studio\\n109: \\n110: The documented visual interface is SurrealDB Studio at\\n111: `studio.surrealdb.com`, delivered as a hosted web application and a\\n112: desktop application. No UI image is pinned in the Compose deployment\\n113: because Studio is not self-hostable; Surrealist, now end-of-life, is not\\n114: adopted.\\n115: \\n116: The desktop application is the clean path to the local Compose service:\\n117: connect to `ws://127.0.0.1:8000` with the `SURREALDB_USER` and\\n118: `SURREALDB_PASSWORD` values from `.env`, and treat that root identity as\\n119: local-only. A hosted web page reaching a local endpoint is a verification\\n120: note, not a claim: whether the hosted page can reach `ws://127.0.0.1:8000`\\n121: is not verified here, and an operator who needs that path must verify it\\n122: in their own environment before relying on it.\\n123: \\n124: Studio is an operator convenience. Qualification evidence comes from the\\n125: test suites, never from a UI session.\\n126: =======\\n127: ## Pack harness lane\\n128: \\n129: The pack lane loads the external ActiveGraph pack library 