{"id":"int-b1dc819e8b678181e2837495fff1cac6","kind":"tool_call","created_at":"2026-10-13T16:58:54.521Z","actor":"opencode","tool_name":"read","extra":{"call_id":"call_9cefaa6ada3a42a58fe3c271","duration_ms":5,"input":"{\"limit\":20,\"offset\":86,\"path\":\"/home/mercor/orca/workspaces/activegraph-surrealdb/mercor-vm/README.md\"}","message_id":"msg_13633cc7f001PwFoKWxDMu5cCE","result":"{\"output\":{\"type\":\"text-page\",\"content\":\"Because the event log and the graph projection share one deployment, the\\nprovider pushes the released `GraphStore` query hooks down into SurrealQL rather\\nthan scanning in Python. Object type filters, relation source/target/type\\nfilters, existence probes, and the undirected neighbourhood walk are all bound\\nSurrealQL; `match_chain` composes those pushed-down primitives hop by hop. The\\nrich `where` predicate stays with ActiveGraph and is returned as an exact\\nresidual, per the released contract. Schema v2 adds the indexes those queries\\nuse; schema v3 records the object counter so reads return the reference store's\\ninsertion order. See [ADR 0003](docs/adr/0003-native-query-pushdown.md) and\\n[ADR 0004](docs/adr/0004-projection-order.md).\\n\\n## Pack library\\n\\nThe provider ships a harness that loads the published\\n[ActiveGraph pack library](https://github.com/yoheinakajima/activegraph-packs)\\nonto a `Runtime` whose event log and graph projection both live in SurrealDB:\\n\\n```python\\nfrom activegraph_surrealdb import SurrealConfig, build_runtime\\n\",\"mime\":\"text/markdown\",\"offset\":86,\"truncated\":true,\"next\":106},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Read file /home/mercor/orca/workspaces/activegraph-surrealdb/mercor-vm/README.md, lines 86-105\\n86: Because the event log and the graph projection share one deployment, the\\n87: provider pushes the released `GraphStore` query hooks down into SurrealQL rather\\n88: than scanning in Python. Object type filters, relation source/target/type\\n89: filters, existence probes, and the undirected neighbourhood walk are all bound\\n90: SurrealQL; `match_chain` composes those pushed-down primitives hop by hop. The\\n91: rich `where` predicate stays with ActiveGraph and is returned as an exact\\n92: residual, per the released contract. Schema v2 adds the indexes those queries\\n93: use; schema v3 records the object counter so reads return the reference store's\\n94: insertion order. See [ADR 0003](docs/adr/0003-native-query-pushdown.md) and\\n95: [ADR 0004](docs/adr/0004-projection-order.md).\\n96: \\n97: ## Pack library\\n98: \\n99: The provider ships a harness that loads the published\\n100: [ActiveGraph pack library](https://github.com/yoheinakajima/activegraph-packs)\\n101: onto a `Runtime` whose event log and graph projection both live in SurrealDB:\\n102: \\n103: ```python\\n104: from activegraph_surrealdb import SurrealConfig, build_runtime\\n105: \\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 106]\"}],\"metadata\":{\"truncated\":true}}","session_id":"ses_ecd1f104affewX9x4cIqy5fLvq","status":"completed"}}
{"id":"int-be1250dbf395af8324ebb16512e934bb","kind":"tool_call","created_at":"2026-10-13T16:59:11.673Z","actor":"opencode","tool_name":"read","extra":{"call_id":"call_c567b9362a064c93a2a94cd5","duration_ms":4,"input":"{\"limit\":40,\"offset\":1,\"path\":\"/home/mercor/orca/workspaces/activegraph-surrealdb/mercor-vm/ROADMAP.md\"}","message_id":"msg_13633eae9001sTpBgMFOB72X6z","result":"{\"output\":{\"type\":\"text-page\",\"content\":\"# Roadmap\\n\\nThis roadmap describes evidence gates, not release dates. Work moves forward\\nonly when the previous boundary is repeatably demonstrated.\\n\\n## Phase 0 — Contract-first research preview\\n\\n- [x] Separate authoritative event and disposable graph responsibilities.\\n- [x] Pin ActiveGraph `1.12.0`, SurrealDB `3.2.4`, and Python SDK `2.0.0` lanes.\\n- [x] Define serialization, isolation, replay, fork/diff, and qualification contracts.\\n- [x] Record upstream lifecycle limitations without private runtime patches.\\n\\n## Phase 1 — Generic provider implementation\\n\\n- [x] Pass unit serialization/configuration contracts.\\n- [x] Pass released EventStore and GraphStore conformance.\\n- [x] Implement transactional append/head checks and deterministic stale-writer tests.\\n- [x] Implement native relation storage without an in-memory mirror.\\n- [x] Push object, relation, existence, and neighbourhood queries into native SurrealQL; `match_chain` composes those primitives.\\n- [x] Implement fail-closed replay readiness and uncompacted prefix forks.\\n- [x] Load the published pack library onto one SurrealDB-backed Runtime.\\n- [x] Publish reproducible fork/diff/replay trace evidence.\\n\\n## Phase 2 — Stable qualification\\n\\n- [x] Pass live isolation, rollback, native-edge, and exact-JSON tests.\\n- [ ] Pass pinned RocksDB graceful restart and abrupt container termination tests.\\n- [x] Add an in-place, data-preserving schema upgrade lane and reject a newer schema.\\n- [x] Add a schema rollback lane before changing support.\\n- [x] Exercise backup and clean-environment restore, then verify event integrity and replay.\\n- [ ] Record bounded performance observations on controlled, representative data.\\n\\n## Phase 3 — Upstream lifecycle alignment\\n\\n- [x] Re-evaluate append/projection ordering after ActiveGraph 1.12 incorporated it\\n  (CONTRACT v1.11 #2); see\\n  [ADR 0003](docs/adr/0003-latest-stable-pins-and-exploration-lanes.md).\\n- [ ] Adopt a public store-driver/registry contract if upstream accepts one.\\n- [ ] Adopt store-neutral load/resume without phantom-run or stale-projection behavior.\\n- [ ] Design snapshot/compaction hydration only against an explicit upstream contract.\",\"mime\":\"text/markdown\",\"offset\":1,\"truncated\":true,\"next\":41},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Read file /home/mercor/orca/workspaces/activegraph-surrealdb/mercor-vm/ROADMAP.md, lines 1-40\\n1: # Roadmap\\n2: \\n3: This roadmap describes evidence gates, not release dates. Work moves forward\\n4: only when the previous boundary is repeatably demonstrated.\\n5: \\n6: ## Phase 0 — Contract-first research preview\\n7: \\n8: - [x] Separate authoritative event and disposable graph responsibilities.\\n9: - [x] Pin ActiveGraph `1.12.0`, SurrealDB `3.2.4`, and Python SDK `2.0.0` lanes.\\n10: - [x] Define serialization, isolation, replay, fork/diff, and qualification contracts.\\n11: - [x] Record upstream lifecycle limitations without private runtime patches.\\n12: \\n13: ## Phase 1 — Generic provider implementation\\n14: \\n15: - [x] Pass unit serialization/configuration contracts.\\n16: - [x] Pass released EventStore and GraphStore conformance.\\n17: - [x] Implement transactional append/head checks and deterministic stale-writer tests.\\n18: - [x] Implement native relation storage without an in-memory mirror.\\n19: - [x] Push object, relation, existence, and neighbourhood queries into native SurrealQL; `match_chain` composes those primitives.\\n20: - [x] Implement fail-closed replay readiness and uncompacted prefix forks.\\n21: - [x] Load the published pack library onto one SurrealDB-backed Runtime.\\n22: - [x] Publish reproducible fork/diff/replay trace evidence.\\n23: \\n24: ## Phase 2 — Stable qualification\\n25: \\n26: - [x] Pass live isolation, rollback, native-edge, and exact-JSON tests.\\n27: - [ ] Pass pinned RocksDB graceful restart and abrupt container termination tests.\\n28: - [x] Add an in-place, data-preserving schema upgrade lane and reject a newer schema.\\n29: - [x] Add a schema rollback lane before changing support.\\n30: - [x] Exercise backup and clean-environment restore, then verify event integrity and replay.\\n31: - [ ] Record bounded performance observations on controlled, representative data.\\n32: \\n33: ## Phase 3 — Upstream lifecycle alignment\\n34: \\n35: - [x] Re-evaluate append/projection ordering after ActiveGraph 1.12 incorporated it\\n36:   (CONTRACT v1.11 #2); see\\n37:   [ADR 0003](docs/adr/0003-latest-stable-pins-and-exploration-lanes.md).\\n38: - [ ] Adopt a public store-driver/registry contract if upstream accepts one.\\n39: - [ ] Adopt store-neutral load/resume without phantom-run or stale-projection behavior.\\n40: - [ ] Design snapshot/compaction hydration only against an explicit upstream contract.\\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 41]\"}],\"metadata\":{\"truncated\":true}}","session_id":"ses_ecd1f104affewX9x4cIqy5fLvq","status":"completed"}}
{"id":"int-2e0d699afd0b6008be5a39affa440972","kind":"tool_call","created_at":"2026-10-13T16:59:18.933Z","actor":"opencode","tool_name":"shell","extra":{"call_id":"call_d2ec93c7847c424d85d74cc2","duration_ms":30,"input":"{\"command\":\"cd /home/mercor/orca/workspaces/activegraph-surrealdb/mercor-vm\\necho \\\"=== ROADMAP: my pre-consolidation tip vs HEAD ===\\\"; git diff 02ab780..HEAD -- ROADMAP.md\\necho; echo \\\"=== compatibility: my pre-consolidation tip vs HEAD ===\\\"; git diff 02ab780..HEAD -- docs/compatibility.md\",\"timeout\":120000}","message_id":"msg_136342dee001BV0ZRTwIhPbyeq","result":"{\"output\":{\"exit\":0,\"truncated\":false,\"output\":\"=== ROADMAP: my pre-consolidation tip vs HEAD ===\\ndiff --git a/ROADMAP.md b/ROADMAP.md\\nindex 5bea594..2daee2e 100644\\n--- a/ROADMAP.md\\n+++ b/ROADMAP.md\\n@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@ only when the previous boundary is repeatably demonstrated.\\n ## Phase 0 — Contract-first research preview\\n \\n - [x] Separate authoritative event and disposable graph responsibilities.\\n-- [x] Pin ActiveGraph `1.10.0`, SurrealDB `3.2.4`, and Python SDK `2.0.0` lanes.\\n+- [x] Pin ActiveGraph `1.12.0`, SurrealDB `3.2.4`, and Python SDK `2.0.0` lanes.\\n - [x] Define serialization, isolation, replay, fork/diff, and qualification contracts.\\n - [x] Record upstream lifecycle limitations without private runtime patches.\\n \\n@@ -16,22 +16,24 @@ only when the previous boundary is repeatably demonstrated.\\n - [x] Pass released EventStore and GraphStore conformance.\\n - [x] Implement transactional append/head checks and deterministic stale-writer tests.\\n - [x] Implement native relation storage without an in-memory mirror.\\n-- [ ] Push neighborhood and chain matching into native SurrealQL queries.\\n+- [x] Push object, relation, existence, and neighbourhood queries into native SurrealQL; `match_chain` composes those primitives.\\n - [x] Implement fail-closed replay readiness and uncompacted prefix forks.\\n+- [x] Load the published pack library onto one SurrealDB-backed Runtime.\\n - [x] Publish reproducible fork/diff/replay trace evidence.\\n \\n ## Phase 2 — Stable qualification\\n \\n - [x] Pass live isolation, rollback, native-edge, and exact-JSON tests.\\n - [ ] Pass pinned RocksDB graceful restart and abrupt container termination tests.\\n-- [ ] Add an existing-database upgrade and rollback lane before changing support.\\n-- [ ] Exercise backup and clean-environment restore, then verify event integrity and replay.\\n+- [x] Add an in-place, data-preserving schema upgrade lane and reject a newer schema.\\n+- [x] Add a schema rollback lane before changing support.\\n+- [x] Exercise backup and clean-environment restore, then verify event integrity and replay.\\n - [ ] Record bounded performance observations on controlled, representative data.\\n \\n ## Phase 3 — Upstream lifecycle alignment\\n \\n-- [x] Re-evaluate append/projection ordering after an ActiveGraph release\\n-  incorporates it; see\\n+- [x] Re-evaluate append/projection ordering after ActiveGraph 1.12 incorporated it\\n+  (CONTRACT v1.11 #2); see\\n   [ADR 0003](docs/adr/0003-latest-stable-pins-and-exploration-lanes.md).\\n - [ ] Adopt a public store-driver/registry contract if upstream accepts one.\\n - [ ] Adopt store-neutral load/resume without phantom-run or stale-projection behavior.\\n\\n=== compatibility: my pre-consolidation tip vs HEAD ===\\ndiff --git a/docs/compatibility.md b/docs/compatibility.md\\nindex 51c07fa..da1f46d 100644\\n--- a/docs/compatibility.md\\n+++ b/docs/compatibility.md\\n@@ -16,12 +16,21 @@\\n | Path | Accepted by configuration | Qualification status |\\n | --- | --- | --- |\\n | `ws://` to pinned local server | Yes | Required qualification lane |\\n-| `wss://` to remote server | Yes | Syntax supported; no TLS qualification claim yet |\\n+| `wss://` to pinned local server | Yes | Preview TLS lane demonstrated: local CA via openssl, certificate verification enforced, full live suite green (2026-10-13). No rotation or workload-identity claim. |\\n | HTTP/HTTPS | No | Stateful SDK transaction handles are WebSocket-only |\\n-| `mem://` embedded | No | Not durable and outside the provider preview |\\n-| embedded `file://`, `rocksdb://`, or `surrealkv://` | No | Persistence and transaction semantics are not qualified |\\n+| `mem://` embedded | No | Not durable and outside the provider preview; rejection pinned by `tests/embedded/test_embedded_lane.py` |\\n+| embedded `file://`, `rocksdb://`, or `surrealkv://` | No | Persistence and transaction semantics are not qualified; rejection pinned by `tests/embedded/test_embedded_lane.py` |\\n | server-side RocksDB | Yes | Required stable storage path |\\n-| server-side SurrealKV | No recommendation | SurrealKV remains beta |\\n+| server-side SurrealKV | No recommendation | SurrealKV remains beta; full live integration suite green on a dedicated SurrealKV volume (V7 lane, 2026-10-13) |\\n+\\n+### Evidence recording note (2026-10-13)\\n+\\n+The V2/V4/V5/V6/V7 lane runs were recorded against the native `surreal v3.2.4`\\n+binary (same version as the pinned image) on fresh per-lane RocksDB/SurrealKV\\n+volumes, because the execution sandbox cannot run containers\\n+(`agvm-8ii`: devpts `gid=5` is unmappable without setuid `newuidmap`). The\\n+containerized qualification (compose bring-up, restart/kill sequences) remains\\n+the outstanding gap and is deferred to a VM-runtime sandbox.\\n \\n The Compose and qualification files intentionally pin complete versions. A new\\n server or SDK release is unsupported until its own compatibility branch passes\\n@@ -39,24 +48,20 @@ by this provider.\\n The provider does not patch private ActiveGraph runtime methods or register a\\n database URL scheme. Stores are constructed explicitly.\\n \\n-- [ActiveGraph PR #78](https://github.com/yoheinakajima/activegraph/pull/78)\\n-  proposed append-before-projection ordering and stronger run ownership. The\\n-  released `1.12.0` baseline incorporates it: `Graph.emit` appends to the\\n-  event store before projecting, and a failed append changes no graph,\\n-  queue, projection, or observer state.\\n+- ActiveGraph `1.12.0` ships the append-before-projection ordering proposed by\\n+  [PR #78](https://github.com/yoheinakajima/activegraph/pull/78) as CONTRACT\\n+  v1.11 #2: a rejected durable append changes no projected state. The provider\\n+  asserts that invariant directly in `tests/test_write_ordering.py`.\\n - [ActiveGraph issue #81](https://github.com/yoheinakajima/activegraph/issues/81)\\n   tracks `Runtime.load()` creating an unknown run instead of failing without a\\n-  mutation. It is re-evaluated against `1.12.0`; the strict test stays until\\n-  the fix is proven.\\n+  mutation. Still open in `1.12.0`.\\n - [ActiveGraph issue #82](https://github.com/yoheinakajima/activegraph/issues/82)\\n   tracks replay into a stale supplied projection without clearing it first.\\n-  It is re-evaluated against `1.12.0` the same way.\\n+  Still open in `1.12.0`.\\n \\n-The ordering item is now a positive `1.12.0` contract test. The load and\\n-stale-projection reproductions remain strict expected-failure tests until\\n-their re-evaluation is proven. An upstream fix that makes one unexpectedly\\n-pass is a prompt to review and update the provider, not to delete the test\\n-blindly.\\n+Strict expected-failure tests keep the remaining limitations visible. An\\n+upstream fix that makes one unexpectedly pass is a prompt to review and update\\n+the provider, not to delete the test blindly.\\n \\n `1.12.0` also closes the patch vocabulary to `update` and `replace`:\\n `Patch` construction and replay both reject any other op with\\n@@ -77,8 +82,22 @@ migration are not implemented by guessing at private runtime state.\\n \\n ## Claims this matrix does not make\\n \\n-- ActiveGraph compatibility beyond the pinned `1.12.0` baseline.\\n+- ActiveGraph `1.13` compatibility before an upstream release is tested.\\n - Wire or storage compatibility across arbitrary SurrealDB versions.\\n - Distributed SurrealDB, SurrealDB Cloud, or multi-node high availability.\\n-- TLS certificate, proxy, or workload-identity qualification.\\n+- TLS qualification beyond the pinned preview lane: public CAs, proxy\\n+  termination, least-privilege identities, and certificate rotation.\\n - Atomic event-plus-projection acceptance.\\n+\\n+## Provider schema\\n+\\n+The provider schema is versioned and additive. Schema v1 introduced the\\n+event/graph tables; schema v2 adds the indexes that back the native query\\n+pushdown; schema v3 records the object counter that gives projection reads the\\n+reference store's insertion order. Opening an older database upgrades it in\\n+place without data loss; a database written by a newer provider is rejected\\n+rather than mis-read. The upgrade path is pinned by\\n+`tests/integration/test_schema_upgrade.py`, and the backup / clean-environment\\n+restore rehearsal (export, restore into a fresh database, integrity and\\n+projection parity, newer-provider rollback rejection) by\\n+`tests/integration/test_backup_restore.py`.\\n\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"=== ROADMAP: my pre-consolidation tip vs HEAD ===\\ndiff --git a/ROADMAP.md b/ROADMAP.md\\nindex 5bea594..2daee2e 100644\\n--- a/ROADMAP.md\\n+++ b/ROADMAP.md\\n@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@ only when the previous boundary is repeatably demonstrated.\\n ## Phase 0 — Contract-first research preview\\n \\n - [x] Separate authoritative event and disposable graph responsibilities.\\n-- [x] Pin ActiveGraph `1.10.0`, SurrealDB `3.2.4`, and Python SDK `2.0.0` lanes.\\n+- [x] Pin ActiveGraph `1.12.0`, SurrealDB `3.2.4`, and Python SDK `2.0.0` lanes.\\n - [x] Define serialization, isolation, replay, fork/diff, and qualification contracts.\\n - [x] Record upstream lifecycle limitations without private runtime patches.\\n \\n@@ -16,22 +16,24 @@ only when the previous boundary is repeatably demonstrated.\\n - [x] Pass released EventStore and GraphStore conformance.\\n - [x] Implement transactional append/head checks and deterministic stale-writer tests.\\n - [x] Implement native relation storage without an in-memory mirror.\\n-- [ ] Push neighborhood and chain matching into native SurrealQL queries.\\n+- [x] Push object, relation, existence, and neighbourhood queries into native SurrealQL; `match_chain` composes those primitives.\\n - [x] Implement fail-closed replay readiness and uncompacted prefix forks.\\n+- [x] Load the published pack library onto one SurrealDB-backed Runtime.\\n - [x] Publish reproducible fork/diff/replay trace evidence.\\n \\n ## Phase 2 — Stable qualification\\n \\n - [x] Pass live isolation, rollback, native-edge, and exact-JSON tests.\\n - [ ] Pass pinned RocksDB graceful restart and abrupt container termination tests.\\n-- [ ] Add an existing-database upgrade and rollback lane before changing support.\\n-- [ ] Exercise backup and clean-environment restore, then verify event integrity and replay.\\n+- [x] Add an in-place, data-preserving schema upgrade lane and reject a newer schema.\\n+- [x] Add a schema rollback lane before changing support.\\n+- [x] Exercise backup and clean-environment restore, then verify event integrity and replay.\\n - [ ] Record bounded performance observations on controlled, representative data.\\n \\n ## Phase 3 — Upstream lifecycle alignment\\n \\n-- [x] Re-evaluate append/projection ordering after an ActiveGraph release\\n-  incorporates it; see\\n+- [x] Re-evaluate append/projection ordering after ActiveGraph 1.12 incorporated it\\n+  (CONTRACT v1.11 #2); see\\n   [ADR 0003](docs/adr/0003-latest-stable-pins-and-exploration-lanes.md).\\n - [ ] Adopt a public store-driver/registry contract if upstream accepts one.\\n - [ ] Adopt store-neutral load/resume without phantom-run or stale-projection behavior.\\n\\n=== compatibility: my pre-consolidation tip vs HEAD ===\\ndiff --git a/docs/compatibility.md b/docs/compatibility.md\\ninde