AP.md:19:- [x] Push object, relation, existence, and neighbourhood queries into native SurrealQL; `match_chain` composes those primitives.\\n./docs/adr/0001-provider-boundaries.md:15:SurrealDB can host both jobs, plus application documents and native graph\\n./docs/adr/0001-provider-boundaries.md:51:- Relations are native edges with `in` and `out` record endpoints. A separate\\n./docs/adr/0003-native-query-pushdown.md:73:`3.2.4`, native server lane per the recorded sandbox deviation, `agvm-8ii`):\\n./docs/architecture.md:54:vertices, and relations. Relations are planned as native `TYPE RELATION` records\\n./docs/compatibility.md:28:The V2/V4/V5/V6/V7 lane runs were recorded against the native `surreal v3.2.4`\\n./docs/compatibility.md:30:volumes, because the execution sandbox cannot run containers\\n./docs/compatibility.md:31:(`agvm-8ii`: devpts `gid=5` is unmappable without setuid `newuidmap`). The\\n./docs/compatibility.md:33:the outstanding gap and is deferred to a VM-runtime sandbox.\\n./docs/compatibility.md:95:event/graph tables; schema v2 adds the indexes that back the native query\\n./docs/conformance.md:17:| Provider invariants | `pytest -m surrealdb` | Real server transactions, isolation, native edges, replay/fork/diff, restart within a live server |\\n./docs/conformance.md:46:- native query pushdown for every overridden GraphStore hook;\\n./docs/conformance.md:55:- native `TYPE RELATION` records with bound `RecordID` endpoints;\\n./docs/experiment.md:60:- alternative suffixes produce a meaningful ActiveGraph diff;\\n./docs/experiment.md:65:recover a query model and investigators can compare alternative decisions\\n./docs/upgrade-plan.md:114:- The research sandbox that produced this plan could not reach Docker\\n\\n=== my old compatibility.md (02ab780) evidence section ===\\n# Compatibility and known issues\\n\\n## Qualified and preview lanes\\n\\n| Component | Status | Notes |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| ActiveGraph `1.12.0` | Baseline | Public store interfaces and released conformance suites |\\n| SurrealDB server `3.3.0` | Required stable lane | Pinned Docker image, remote WebSocket, server-side RocksDB |\\n| SurrealDB server `3.2.5` | Documented fallback | Re-pinned only if `3.3.0` fails conformance |\\n| SurrealDB Python SDK `2.0.0` | Required | Exact dependency pin for the research preview |\\n| SurrealDB prereleases beyond `3.3.0` | Preview only | Forward-compatibility signal; never gates the stable lane |\\n| Python `3.11+` | Package requirement | CI results, not the version declaration alone, determine qualified interpreters |\\n\\n## Transport and engine matrix\\n\\n| Path | Accepted by configuration | Qualification status |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| `ws://` to pinned local server | Yes | Required qualification lane |\\n| `wss://` to remote server | Yes | Syntax supported; no TLS qualification claim yet |\\n| HTTP/HTTPS | No | Stateful SDK transaction handles are WebSocket-only |\\n| `mem://` embedded | No | Not durable and outside the provider preview |\\n| embedded `file://`, `rocksdb://`, or `surrealkv://` | No | Persistence and transaction semantics are not qualified |\\n| server-side RocksDB | Yes | Required stable storage path |\\n| server-side SurrealKV | No recommendation | SurrealKV remains beta |\\n\\nThe Compose and qualification files intentionally pin complete versions. A new\\nserver or SDK release is unsupported until its own compatibility branch passes\\nthe same conformance, restart, concurrency, isolation, and exact-serialization\\ntests.\\n\\nThe SDK `2.0.0` blocking WebSocket implementation currently emits a\\n`DeprecationWarning` with `websockets 17.1` because the SDK opens its internal\\nsocket through a legacy direct-connect path. The stable contract suite passes;\\nthe warning is tracked as dependency-compatibility work and is not suppressed\\nby this provider.\\n\\n## ActiveGraph lifecycle limitations\\n\\nThe provider does not patch private ActiveGraph runtime methods or register a\\ndatabase URL scheme. Stores are constructed explicitly.\\n\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"=== native / agvm-8ii / container-deviation claims ===\\n./.beads/README.md:3:Welcome to Beads! This repository uses **Beads** for issue tracking - a modern, AI-native tool designed to live directly in your codebase alongside your code.\\n./.beads/README.md:54:- Dolt-native sync via bd dolt push / bd dolt pull\\n./.beads/README.md:56:- Dolt-native three-way merge resolution\\n./AGENTS.md:13:- Git-friendly: Dolt-powered version control with native sync\\n./AGENTS.md:186:  be erased and rebuilt (replayed) from the event log; native relation\\n./README.md:29:3. copy a run prefix to fork an alternative decision;\\n./README.md:41:| PostgreSQL plus a separate graph database | Mature event-store path | Yes | In the graph service | Two databases and a synchronization boundary | Strong alternative when operational maturity matters more than consolidation |\\n./README.md:42:| SQLite plus an in-process graph | Local durable events | Process-local | No shared native graph | Very small | Development and upstream reproduction |\\n./README.md:140:- auditable agent or workflow state where alternative decisions need comparison;\\n./ROADMAP.md:18:- [x] Implement native relation storage without an in-memory mirror.\\n./ROADMAP.md:19:- [x] Push object, relation, existence, and neighbourhood queries into native SurrealQL; `match_chain` composes those primitives.\\n./docs/adr/0001-provider-boundaries.md:15:SurrealDB can host both jobs, plus application documents and native graph\\n./docs/adr/0001-provider-boundaries.md:51:- Relations are native edges with `in` and `out` record endpoints. A separate\\n./docs/adr/0003-native-query-pushdown.md:73:`3.2.4`, native server lane per the recorded sandbox deviation, `agvm-8ii`):\\n./docs/architecture.md:54:vertices, and relations. Relations are planned as native `TYPE RELATION` records\\n./docs/compatibility.md:28:The 