{"id":"int-e620b8799105b3f093b2d15b23681e01","kind":"tool_call","created_at":"2026-10-13T17:00:20.357Z","actor":"opencode","tool_name":"read","extra":{"call_id":"call_505856dbdcbc475f9e79bbf4","duration_ms":7,"input":"{\"offset\":40,\"path\":\"/home/mercor/orca/workspaces/activegraph-surrealdb/mercor-vm/ROADMAP.md\"}","message_id":"msg_1363514c80018z6j5NO09wbF2a","result":"{\"output\":{\"type\":\"text-page\",\"content\":\"- [ ] Design snapshot/compaction hydration only against an explicit upstream contract.\\n- [ ] Evaluate an optional runtime-owned cross-store transaction coordinator.\\n\\n## Phase 4 — Production evaluation\\n\\n- [ ] Qualify `wss://`, certificate validation, least-privilege identities, and rotation.\\n- [ ] Define monitoring and operator response for failed/incomplete projections.\\n- [ ] Document data retention, restore objectives, and incident response.\\n- [ ] Decide whether single-node RocksDB meets availability requirements or a different\\n  deployment architecture is necessary.\\n- [ ] Complete an independent security and operational review.\\n\\n## Continuing non-goals\\n\\n- claiming cross-store atomicity without an upstream coordinator;\\n- hiding upstream gaps behind copied private runtime code;\\n- managing application contacts, auth, CRM records, or identity ontologies;\\n- qualifying every SurrealDB transport, engine, cloud, or prerelease; and\\n- calling the preview production-ready based only on CI.\",\"mime\":\"text/markdown\",\"offset\":40,\"truncated\":false},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Read file /home/mercor/orca/workspaces/activegraph-surrealdb/mercor-vm/ROADMAP.md, lines 40-58\\n40: - [ ] Design snapshot/compaction hydration only against an explicit upstream contract.\\n41: - [ ] Evaluate an optional runtime-owned cross-store transaction coordinator.\\n42: \\n43: ## Phase 4 — Production evaluation\\n44: \\n45: - [ ] Qualify `wss://`, certificate validation, least-privilege identities, and rotation.\\n46: - [ ] Define monitoring and operator response for failed/incomplete projections.\\n47: - [ ] Document data retention, restore objectives, and incident response.\\n48: - [ ] Decide whether single-node RocksDB meets availability requirements or a different\\n49:   deployment architecture is necessary.\\n50: - [ ] Complete an independent security and operational review.\\n51: \\n52: ## Continuing non-goals\\n53: \\n54: - claiming cross-store atomicity without an upstream coordinator;\\n55: - hiding upstream gaps behind copied private runtime code;\\n56: - managing application contacts, auth, CRM records, or identity ontologies;\\n57: - qualifying every SurrealDB transport, engine, cloud, or prerelease; and\\n58: - calling the preview production-ready based only on CI.\"}],\"metadata\":{\"truncated\":false}}","session_id":"ses_ecd1f104affewX9x4cIqy5fLvq","status":"completed"}}
