{"id":"int-bf12112f94862aaa6a1bb9882bbecfa3","kind":"tool_call","created_at":"2026-10-13T17:02:18.142Z","actor":"opencode","tool_name":"shell","extra":{"call_id":"call_3b50187a80df4fdc8053a33c","duration_ms":159,"input":"{\"command\":\"cd /home/mercor/orca/workspaces/activegraph-surrealdb/mercor-vm\\necho \\\"=== wss / CA refs in tests+docs ===\\\"; grep -rn 'wss\\\\|TLS_CA\\\\|ca_cert\\\\|ssl' tests/integration/conftest.py docs/deployment.md .env.example 2>/dev/null | head -30\\necho; echo \\\"=== CA files on disk ===\\\"; ls -1 /work/mercor-work/activegraph-surrealdb/*.pem /work/mercor-work/activegraph-surrealdb/*.crt 2>/dev/null; ls -1 *.pem *.crt 2>/dev/null; find /work -maxdepth 3 -name '*.pem' -o -maxdepth 3 -name '*.crt' 2>/dev/null | head\",\"timeout\":120000}","message_id":"msg_13636f192001AUG8FDQcbZaafC","result":"{\"output\":{\"exit\":0,\"truncated\":false,\"output\":\"=== wss / CA refs in tests+docs ===\\ndocs/deployment.md:189:The TLS lane qualifies `wss://`. Generate a local certificate authority\\ndocs/deployment.md:190:with `mkcert` or `openssl` and trust it on the host; the SDK applies\\ndocs/deployment.md:199:`ACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_TEST_URL=wss://127.0.0.1:8000` and\\n\\n=== CA files on disk ===\\n/work/.ladder/tls/ca.crt\\n/work/.ladder/tls/server.crt\\n\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"=== wss / CA refs in tests+docs ===\\ndocs/deployment.md:189:The TLS lane qualifies `wss://`. Generate a local certificate authority\\ndocs/deployment.md:190:with `mkcert` or `openssl` and trust it on the host; the SDK applies\\ndocs/deployment.md:199:`ACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_TEST_URL=wss://127.0.0.1:8000` and\\n\\n=== CA files on disk ===\\n/work/.ladder/tls/ca.crt\\n/work/.ladder/tls/server.crt\\n\"}],\"metadata\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"truncated\":false,\"exit\":0}}","session_id":"ses_ecd1f104affewX9x4cIqy5fLvq","status":"completed"}}
{"id":"int-618455970bd703fbe5e0b10860a6361f","kind":"tool_call","created_at":"2026-10-13T17:02:21.944Z","actor":"opencode","tool_name":"read","extra":{"call_id":"call_e02eb281a2ec4f15b4934e65","duration_ms":6,"input":"{\"limit\":30,\"offset\":185,\"path\":\"/home/mercor/orca/workspaces/activegraph-surrealdb/mercor-vm/docs/deployment.md\"}","message_id":"msg_1363706440014VQiubMy0h8SUP","result":"{\"output\":{\"type\":\"text-page\",\"content\":\"upgrade item open and is recorded.\\n\\n### TLS lane\\n\\nThe TLS lane qualifies `wss://`. Generate a local certificate authority\\nwith `mkcert` or `openssl` and trust it on the host; the SDK applies\\nstandard certificate verification. Set `SURREALDB_WEB_CRT` and\\n`SURREALDB_WEB_KEY` and start only the TLS service with\\n`docker compose --profile tls up -d surrealdb-tls`; a plain profile\\nstart would also start the default server and collide with it; likewise\\nstop an already-running default lane first (`docker compose stop\\nsurrealdb`), since both services publish the same port. Confirm\\nreadiness with `surreal is-ready --endpoint https://127.0.0.1:8000`,\\nand run the same integration and qualification suites with\\n`ACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_TEST_URL=wss://127.0.0.1:8000` and\\n`ACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_DOCKER_CONTAINER` set to the TLS container name\\n(`activegraph-surrealdb-tls` by default). The lane uses its own\\n`SURREALDB_VOLUME` value. It is non-gating: no TLS qualification claim\\nexists until it passes and the [compatibility](compatibility.md) matrix\\nrecords the result.\\n\\n### SurrealKV lane\\n\\nThe SurrealKV lane runs the server on the beta SurrealKV engine. Set\\n`SURREALDB_ENGINE=surrealkv` and a `SURREALDB_VOLUME` value that no\\nRocksDB lane has ever used; a storage location must never be shared\\nbetween backends. The service renders `surrealkv:///data/activegraph.db`.\\nRun the live integration suite; an optional qualification pass sets\\n`ACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_TEST_ENGINE=surrealkv` and asserts the SurrealKV\\nstorage URL and `server_version()`. The result is recorded as beta\",\"mime\":\"text/markdown\",\"offset\":185,\"truncated\":true,\"next\":215},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Read file /home/mercor/orca/workspaces/activegraph-surrealdb/mercor-vm/docs/deployment.md, lines 185-214\\n185: upgrade item open and is recorded.\\n186: \\n187: ### TLS lane\\n188: \\n189: The TLS lane qualifies `wss://`. Generate a local certificate authority\\n190: with `mkcert` or `openssl` and trust it on the host; the SDK applies\\n191: standard certificate verification. Set `SURREALDB_WEB_CRT` and\\n192: `SURREALDB_WEB_KEY` and start only the TLS service with\\n193: `docker compose --profile tls up -d surrealdb-tls`; a plain profile\\n194: start would also start the default server and collide with it; likewise\\n195: stop an already-running default lane first (`docker compose stop\\n196: surrealdb`), since both services publish the same port. Confirm\\n197: readiness with `surreal is-ready --endpoint https://127.0.0.1:8000`,\\n198: and run the same integration and qualification suites with\\n199: `ACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_TEST_URL=wss://127.0.0.1:8000` and\\n200: `ACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_DOCKER_CONTAINER` set to the TLS container name\\n201: (`activegraph-surrealdb-tls` by default). The lane uses its own\\n202: `SURREALDB_VOLUME` value. It is non-gating: no TLS qualification claim\\n203: exists until it passes and the [compatibility](compatibility.md) matrix\\n204: records the result.\\n205: \\n206: ### SurrealKV lane\\n207: \\n208: The SurrealKV lane runs the server on the beta SurrealKV engine. Set\\n209: `SURREALDB_ENGINE=surrealkv` and a `SURREALDB_VOLUME` value that no\\n210: RocksDB lane has ever used; a storage location must never be shared\\n211: between backends. The service renders `surrealkv:///data/activegraph.db`.\\n212: Run the live integration suite; an optional qualification pass sets\\n213: `ACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_TEST_ENGINE=surrealkv` and asserts the SurrealKV\\n214: storage URL and `server_version()`. The result is recorded as beta\\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 215]\"}],\"metadata\":{\"truncated\":true}}","session_id":"ses_ecd1f104affewX9x4cIqy5fLvq","status":"completed"}}
