{"id":"int-ab00f25cec6096c6a4c3b9b93c913aa4","kind":"tool_call","created_at":"2026-10-13T17:14:52.485Z","actor":"opencode","tool_name":"read","extra":{"call_id":"call_5d1556fc32d24f198bb294cf","duration_ms":8,"input":"{\"limit\":45,\"offset\":1,\"path\":\"/home/mercor/orca/workspaces/activegraph-surrealdb/mercor-vm/docs/compatibility.md\"}","message_id":"msg_136426b0b001HtRIPOvlFvPYva","result":"{\"output\":{\"type\":\"text-page\",\"content\":\"# Compatibility and known issues\\n\\n## Qualified and preview lanes\\n\\n| Component | Status | Notes |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| ActiveGraph `1.12.0` | Baseline | Public store interfaces and released conformance suites |\\n| SurrealDB server `3.3.0` | Required stable lane | Pinned Docker image, remote WebSocket, server-side RocksDB |\\n| SurrealDB server `3.2.5` | Documented fallback | Re-pinned only if `3.3.0` fails conformance |\\n| SurrealDB Python SDK `2.0.0` | Required | Exact dependency pin for the research preview |\\n| SurrealDB prereleases beyond `3.3.0` | Preview only | Forward-compatibility signal; never gates the stable lane |\\n| Python `3.11+` | Package requirement | CI results, not the version declaration alone, determine qualified interpreters |\\n\\n## Transport and engine matrix\\n\\n| Path | Accepted by configuration | Qualification status |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| `ws://` to pinned local server | Yes | Required qualification lane |\\n| `wss://` to pinned local server | Yes | Preview TLS lane demonstrated: local CA via openssl, certificate verification enforced, full live suite green (2026-10-13). No rotation or workload-identity claim. |\\n| HTTP/HTTPS | No | Stateful SDK transaction handles are WebSocket-only |\\n| `mem://` embedded | No | Not durable and outside the provider preview; rejection pinned by `tests/embedded/test_embedded_lane.py` |\\n| embedded `file://`, `rocksdb://`, or `surrealkv://` | No | Persistence and transaction semantics are not qualified; rejection pinned by `tests/embedded/test_embedded_lane.py` |\\n| server-side RocksDB | Yes | Required stable storage path |\\n| server-side SurrealKV | No recommendation | SurrealKV remains beta; full live integration suite green on a dedicated SurrealKV volume (V7 lane, 2026-10-13) |\\n\\n### Evidence recording note (2026-10-13)\\n\\nThe V2/V4/V5/V6/V7 lane runs were recorded against the native `surreal v3.2.4`\\nbinary (same version as the pinned image) on fresh per-lane RocksDB/SurrealKV\\nvolumes, because the execution sandbox cannot run containers\\n(`agvm-8ii`: devpts `gid=5` is unmappable without setuid `newuidmap`). The\\ncontainerized qualification (compose bring-up, restart/kill sequences) remains\\nthe outstanding gap and is deferred to a VM-runtime sandbox.\\n\\nThe Compose and qualification files intentionally pin complete versions. A new\\nserver or SDK release is unsupported until its own compatibility branch passes\\nthe same conformance, restart, concurrency, isolation, and exact-serialization\\ntests.\\n\\nThe SDK `2.0.0` blocking WebSocket implementation currently emits a\\n`DeprecationWarning` with `websockets 17.1` because the SDK opens its internal\\nsocket through a legacy direct-connect path. The stable contract suite passes;\\nthe warning is tracked as dependency-compatibility work and is not suppressed\\nby this provider.\\n\",\"mime\":\"text/markdown\",\"offset\":1,\"truncated\":true,\"next\":46},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Read file /home/mercor/orca/workspaces/activegraph-surrealdb/mercor-vm/docs/compatibility.md, lines 1-45\\n1: # Compatibility and known issues\\n2: \\n3: ## Qualified and preview lanes\\n4: \\n5: | Component | Status | Notes |\\n6: | --- | --- | --- |\\n7: | ActiveGraph `1.12.0` | Baseline | Public store interfaces and released conformance suites |\\n8: | SurrealDB server `3.3.0` | Required stable lane | Pinned Docker image, remote WebSocket, server-side RocksDB |\\n9: | SurrealDB server `3.2.5` | Documented fallback | Re-pinned only if `3.3.0` fails conformance |\\n10: | SurrealDB Python SDK `2.0.0` | Required | Exact dependency pin for the research preview |\\n11: | SurrealDB prereleases beyond `3.3.0` | Preview only | Forward-compatibility signal; never gates the stable lane |\\n12: | Python `3.11+` | Package requirement | CI results, not the version declaration alone, determine qualified interpreters |\\n13: \\n14: ## Transport and engine matrix\\n15: \\n16: | Path | Accepted by configuration | Qualification status |\\n17: | --- | --- | --- |\\n18: | `ws://` to pinned local server | Yes | Required qualification lane |\\n19: | `wss://` to pinned local server | Yes | Preview TLS lane demonstrated: local CA via openssl, certificate verification enforced, full live suite green (2026-10-13). No rotation or workload-identity claim. |\\n20: | HTTP/HTTPS | No | Stateful SDK transaction handles are WebSocket-only |\\n21: | `mem://` embedded | No | Not durable and outside the provider preview; rejection pinned by `tests/embedded/test_embedded_lane.py` |\\n22: | embedded `file://`, `rocksdb://`, or `surrealkv://` | No | Persistence and transaction semantics are not qualified; rejection pinned by `tests/embedded/test_embedded_lane.py` |\\n23: | server-side RocksDB | Yes | Required stable storage path |\\n24: | server-side SurrealKV | No recommendation | SurrealKV remains beta; full live integration suite green on a dedicated SurrealKV volume (V7 lane, 2026-10-13) |\\n25: \\n26: ### Evidence recording note (2026-10-13)\\n27: \\n28: The V2/V4/V5/V6/V7 lane runs were recorded against the native `surreal v3.2.4`\\n29: binary (same version as the pinned image) on fresh per-lane RocksDB/SurrealKV\\n30: volumes, because the execution sandbox cannot run containers\\n31: (`agvm-8ii`: devpts `gid=5` is unmappable without setuid `newuidmap`). The\\n32: containerized qualification (compose bring-up, restart/kill sequences) remains\\n33: the outstanding gap and is deferred to a VM-runtime sandbox.\\n34: \\n35: The Compose and qualification files intentionally pin complete versions. A new\\n36: server or SDK release is unsupported until its own compatibility branch passes\\n37: the same conformance, restart, concurrency, isolation, and exact-serialization\\n38: tests.\\n39: \\n40: The SDK `2.0.0` blocking WebSocket implementation currently emits a\\n41: `DeprecationWarning` with `websockets 17.1` because the SDK opens its internal\\n42: socket through a legacy direct-connect path. The stable contract suite passes;\\n43: the warning is tracked as dependency-compatibility work and is not suppressed\\n44: by this provider.\\n45: \\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 46]\"}],\"metadata\":{\"truncated\":true}}","session_id":"ses_ecd1f104affewX9x4cIqy5fLvq","status":"completed"}}
