pp and a desktop app, and\\n36:   connects to any SurrealDB instance. No self-hostable Studio image exists\\n37:   to pin.\\n38: - SurrealKV remains beta upstream. It targets embedded and local-first\\n39:   workloads; RocksDB remains the recommended write-heavy server engine.\\n40: - The server exposes TLS through `--web-crt`/`--web-key`. The SDK accepts\\n41:   `wss://` with standard certificate verification.\\n42: \\n43: ## Decision\\n44: \\n45: 1. The stable lane re-pins to the latest stable releases, gated by the\\n46:    qualification policy in\\n47:    [compatibility](../compatibility.md):\\n48: \\n49:    - SurrealDB server `v3.3.0` on a fresh disposable volume, with `v3.2.5`\\n50:      as the documented fallback if 3.3.0 fails conformance.\\n51:    - ActiveGraph `1.12.0`, including the append-before-projection ordering\\n52:      that ADR 0001 documented as missing.\\n53:    - SurrealDB Python SDK `2.0.0` unchanged; it is still the latest stable\\n54:      SDK.\\n55:    - Transport remains remote WebSocket `ws://`; storage remains\\n56:      server-side RocksDB.\\n57: \\n58: 2. The documented UI is SurrealDB Studio. No UI image is pinned in the\\n59:    Compose deployment because Studio is not self-hostable, and the\\n60:    end-of-life Surrealist image is deliberately not adopted.\\n61: \\n62: 3. Four exploration lanes open as non-gating evidence lanes that must not\\n63:    disturb the stable lane:\\n64: \\n65:    - Lane A, TLS: `wss://` against server `--web-crt`/`--web-key` with a\\n66:      locally generated certificate authority trusted by the host.\\n67:    - Lane B, existing-volume upgrade: a RocksDB volume written by 3.2.4,\\n68:      upgraded in place to 3.3.0, with a pre-upgrade `surreal export` and\\n69:      an export-restore rollback rehearsal.\\n70:    - Lane C, SurrealKV: server-side `surrealkv://` storage, still beta, on\\n71:      its own volume. A storage location is never shared between backends.\\n72:    - Lane D, embedded engine: SDK `3.0.0b10` with `surrealdb[embedded]` in\\n73:      an isolated environment. The expected result is a documented\\n74:      rejection: the embedded engine refuses the client-side transactions\\n75:      this provider's append and head contracts depend on.\\n76: \\n77: ## Required lanes\\n78: \\n79: | Lane | Server | Transport | Purpose |\\n80: | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n81: | stable | 3.3.0 (fallback 3.2.5) | WebSocket | required conformance and persistence proof |\\n82: | upgrade | 3.2.4 to 3.3.0 | WebSocket | in-place volume migration and export rollback proof |\\n83: | TLS | 3.3.0 | `wss://` | certificate qu{"id":"int-d457f74d4185f999056cef83e72e4ad9","kind":"plugin_start","created_at":"2026-10-13T20:05:45.626Z","actor":"opencode","extra":{"app_version":"2.0.27","directory":"/work/.mercor-home/orca/workspaces/activegraph-surrealdb/mercor-vm","project":"2d3a34f222bcdce382abffffe0827abe77e25387"}}
