{"id":"int-61bcb67e45b8287e74ccd8368e7c0ead","kind":"tool_call","created_at":"2026-10-13T20:06:02.014Z","actor":"opencode","tool_name":"shell","extra":{"call_id":"call_6e0cbc66d2ad40fda1f8050a","duration_ms":244,"input":"{\"command\":\"cd /home/mercor/orca/workspaces/activegraph-surrealdb/mercor-vm\\necho \\\"=== branch state ===\\\"; git status -sb | head -2\\necho; echo \\\"=== trial merge origin/main (no commit) ===\\\"\\ngit merge --no-commit --no-ff origin/main >/dev/null 2>&1\\necho \\\"--- conflicted paths (status codes) ---\\\"\\ngit status --short | grep -E '^(DD|AU|UD|UA|DU|AA|UU)'\\necho\\necho \\\"--- count by type ---\\\"\\ngit status --short | grep -E '^(DD|AU|UD|UA|DU|AA|UU)' | awk '{print $1}' | sort | uniq -c\\necho\\necho \\\"=== auto-merged files (main changed, no conflict) ===\\\"\\ngit diff --name-only --diff-filter=M origin/main...HEAD 2>/dev/null | head -40\\necho\\ngit merge --abort 2>/dev/null\\necho 2:   pre-upgrade export, so the upgrade lane must rehearse that path before\\n113:   any data-bearing volume is upgraded.\\n114: - Studio is not self-hostable, so the deployment carries no UI container\\n115:   and depends on an external hosted or desktop application.\\n116: - The embedded and surrealkv lanes require separate environments and\\n117:   volumes, widening the evidence matrix without gating progress.\\n118: - Until the 3.3.0 lane passes qualification, the fallback discussion\\n119:   (3.2.5 versus 3.3.0) is open and must be recorded in the\\n120:   [compatibility](../compatibility.md) matrix when resolved.\\n121: \\n122: ## Evidence required before this ADR is accepted\\n123: \\n124: 1. The full unit, live integration, and qualification suites pass against\\n125:    the re-pinned stable lane, including the destructive restart and kill\\n126:    sequences, on the implementation branch.\\n127: 2. The upgrade lane demonstrates, on a disposable volume: data written\\n128:    under 3.2.4, a verified pre-upgrade export, an in-place 3.3.0 start with\\n129:    automatic migrations applied, verified event hash-chain and run-head\\n130:    integrity, graph clear/replay equivalence, and a rollback rehearsal by\\n131:    export restore into a fresh 3.2.4 datastore.\\n132: 3. The TLS lane passes the same live integration and qualification suites\\n133:    over `wss://`, or the compatibility matrix records its failure.\\n134: 4. The surrealkv lane runs the live integration suite against server-side\\n135:    SurrealKV on its own volume, recorded as beta evidence.\\n136: 5. The embedded lane records the expected transaction-refusal evidence\\n137:    against SDK `3.0.0b10`, without changing the stable dependency pins.\\n138: 6. The known-issue tests for ActiveGraph 1.10 have been reviewed one by\\n139:    one against 1.12.0 and converted or retired with rationale, never\\n140:    deleted blindly.\\n141: \\n142: ## What this decision does not claim\\n143: \\n144: - Cross-store atomicity; a projection may still lag the event log, and\\n145:   replay remains the documented repair path.\\n146: - SurrealKV, the SDK 3.0 beta line, or the embedded engine as stable\\n147:   provider support.\\n148: - TLS qualification before Lane A passes.\\n149: - Production readiness, high availability, or backup sufficiency beyond\\n150:   the export rehearsal in the upgrade lane.\"}],\"metadata\":{\"truncated\":false}}","session_id":"ses_ecd1f104affewX9x4cIqy5fLvq","status":"completed"}}
