{"id":"int-ceaaf8e23f014196ffff9568651a9102","kind":"tool_call","created_at":"2026-10-13T22:39:22.053Z","actor":"opencode","tool_name":"edit","extra":{"call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b15bc6c4d8ee5f7f","duration_ms":9,"input":"{\"path\":\"/work/mercor-work/activegraph-surrealdb/docs/security-model.md\",\"oldString\":\"The initial configuration accepts `wss://` syntax but has no qualified TLS lane.\\nCertificate validation, proxies, workload identity, and rotation need explicit\\ndeployment tests before a remote security claim.\",\"newString\":\"The configuration accepts `wss://` syntax. A preview TLS lane is demonstrated\\n(local certificate authority, enforced certificate validation, full live suite\\ngreen; see [compatibility](compatibility.md)), but no TLS qualification claim is\\nmade: public CAs, proxy termination, least-privilege identities, and certificate\\nrotation need explicit deployment tests before a remote security claim.\"}","message_id":"msg_1376b849b001kF0fXBaa3jdFio","result":"{\"output\":{\"files\":[{\"file\":\"docs/security-model.md\",\"patch\":\"Index: docs/security-model.md\\n===================================================================\\n--- docs/security-model.md\\n+++ docs/security-model.md\\n@@ -49,11 +49,13 @@\\n   record IDs, event payloads, traces, or CI artifacts.\\n - Rotate any credential that appears in a public log or issue; deleting the text\\n   is not sufficient remediation.\\n \\n-The initial configuration accepts `wss://` syntax but has no qualified TLS lane.\\n-Certificate validation, proxies, workload identity, and rotation need explicit\\n-deployment tests before a remote security claim.\\n+The configuration accepts `wss://` syntax. A preview TLS lane is demonstrated\\n+(local certificate authority, enforced certificate validation, full live suite\\n+green; see [compatibility](compatibility.md)), but no TLS qualification claim is\\n+made: public CAs, proxy termination, least-privilege identities, and certificate\\n+rotation need explicit deployment tests before a remote security claim.\\n \\n ## Non-atomic runtime boundary\\n \\n The provider does not promise one transaction across event append and graph\\n\",\"additions\":5,\"deletions\":3,\"status\":\"modified\"}],\"replacements\":1},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Edited docs/security-model.md (1 replacement)\"}],\"metadata\":{\"files\":[{\"file\":\"docs/security-model.md\",\"patch\":\"Index: docs/security-model.md\\n===================================================================\\n--- docs/security-model.md\\n+++ docs/security-model.md\\n@@ -49,11 +49,13 @@\\n   record IDs, event payloads, traces, or CI artifacts.\\n - Rotate any credential that appears in a public log or issue; deleting the text\\n   is not sufficient remediation.\\n \\n-The initial configuration accepts `wss://` syntax but has no qualified TLS lane.\\n-Certificate validation, proxies, workload identity, and rotation need explicit\\n-deployment tests before a remote security claim.\\n+The configuration accepts `wss://` syntax. A preview TLS lane is demonstrated\\n+(local certificate authority, enforced certificate validation, full live suite\\n+green; see [compatibility](compatibility.md)), but no TLS qualification claim is\\n+made: public CAs, proxy termination, least-privilege identities, and certificate\\n+rotation need explicit deployment tests before a remote security claim.\\n \\n ## Non-atomic runtime boundary\\n \\n The provider does not promise one transaction across event append and graph\\n\",\"status\":\"modified\",\"additions\":5,\"deletions\":3}]}}","session_id":"ses_ecce71390ffe11p6yPgte61c3p","status":"completed"}}
{"id":"int-2848f6ffd7b501b39b960e652318b73c","kind":"tool_call","created_at":"2026-10-13T22:39:22.063Z","actor":"opencode","tool_name":"edit","extra":{"call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8203c760907fd72b","duration_ms":20,"input":"{\"path\":\"/work/mercor-work/activegraph-surrealdb/AGENTS.md\",\"oldString\":\"```bash\\n# Unit (no server needed)\\npytest -m 'not surrealdb and not qualification'\\n\\n# Live integration (needs a running server)\\ndocker compose up -d\\npytest -m surrealdb tests/integration\\n\\n# Qualification (controls a pinned Docker server; restart/kill sequences)\\nACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_QUALIFY=1 pytest -m qualification tests/qualification\\n\\n# Published evidence example\\npython examples/replay_fork_diff.py\\n```\",\"newString\":\"```bash\\n# Unit (no server needed; the embedded lane self-skips without its gate)\\npytest -m 'not surrealdb and not qualification and not embedded'\\n\\n# Live integration (needs a running server)\\ndocker compose up -d\\npytest -m surrealdb tests/integration\\n\\n# Qualification (controls a pinned Docker server; restart/kill sequences)\\nACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_QUALIFY=1 pytest -m qualification tests/qualification\\n\\n# Embedded SDK lane (isolated venv; expected-rejection evidence)\\nACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_EMBEDDED=1 .venv-embedded/bin/python -m pytest tests/embedded -m embedded\\n\\n# Published evidence example\\npython examples/replay_fork_diff.py\\n```\"}","message_id":"msg_1376b849b001kF0fXBaa3jdFio","result":"{\"output\":{\"files\":[{\"file\":\"AGENTS.md\",\"patch\":\"Index: AGENTS.md\\n===================================================================\\n--- AGENTS.md\\n+++ AGENTS.md\\n@@ -145,18 +145,21 @@\\n \\n Test ladder (see docs/upgrade-plan.md for the serialized evidence ladder V0–V9):\\n \\n ```bash\\n-# Unit (no server needed)\\n-pytest -m 'not surrealdb and not qualification'\\n+# Unit (no server needed; the embedded lane self-skips without its gate)\\n+pytest -m 'not surrealdb and not qualification and not embedded'\\n \\n # Live integration (needs a running server)\\n docker compose up -d\\n pytest -m surrealdb tests/integration\\n \\n # Qualification (controls a pinned Docker server; restart/kill sequences)\\n ACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_QUALIFY=1 pytest -m qualification tests/qualification\\n \\n+# Embedded SDK lane (isolated venv; expected-rejection evidence)\\n+ACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_EMBEDDED=1 .venv-embedded/bin/python -m pytest tests/embedded -m embedded\\n+\\n # Published evidence example\\n python examples/replay_fork_diff.py\\n ```\\n \\n\",\"additions\":5,\"deletions\":2,\"status\":\"modified\"}],\"replacements\":1},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Edited AGENTS.md (1 replacement)\"}],\"metadata\":{\"files\":[{\"file\":\"AGENTS.md\",\"patch\":\"Index: AGENTS.md\\n===================================================================\\n--- AGENTS.md\\n+++ AGENTS.md\\n@@ -145,18 +145,21 @@\\n \\n Test ladder (see docs/upgrade-plan.md for the serialized evidence ladder V0–V9):\\n \\n ```bash\\n-# Unit (no server needed)\\n-pytest -m 'not surrealdb and not qualification'\\n+# Unit (no server needed; the embedded lane self-skips without its gate)\\n+pytest -m 'not surrealdb and not qualification and not embedded'\\n \\n # Live integration (needs a running server)\\n docker compose up -d\\n pytest -m surrealdb tests/integration\\n \\n # Qualification (controls a pinned Docker server; restart/kill sequences)\\n ACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_QUALIFY=1 pytest -m qualification tests/qualification\\n \\n+# Embedded SDK lane (isolated venv; expected-rejection evidence)\\n+ACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_EMBEDDED=1 .venv-embedded/bin/python -m pytest tests/embedded -m embedded\\n+\\n # Published evidence example\\n python examples/replay_fork_diff.py\\n ```\\n \\n\",\"status\":\"modified\",\"additions\":5,\"deletions\":2}]}}","session_id":"ses_ecce71390ffe11p6yPgte61c3p","status":"completed"}}
{"id":"int-15471f4fa109f7667e2323773e969ead","kind":"tool_call","created_at":"2026-10-13T22:39:29.171Z","actor":"opencode","tool_name":"edit","extra":{"call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8dcfe557bc1a6a57","duration_ms":5,"input":"{\"path\":\"/work/mercor-work/activegraph-surrealdb/docs/conformance.md\",\"oldString\":\"| Schema upgrade | `tests/integration/test_schema_upgrade.py` | An older database upgrades in place; a newer schema is rejected |\\n| Provider invariants | `pytest -m surrealdb` | Real server transactions, isolation, native edges, replay/fork/diff, restart within a live server |\\n| Pack harness | `pytest -m packs tests/packs` | The published pack library loads and projects into one SurrealDB database |\\n| Pack fixture suites | `tests/packs/test_pack_fixtures_on_surrealdb.py` | Each pack's own `fixtures/run_fixtures.py` runs unchanged on SurrealDB-backed stores |\\n| Qualification | `pytest -m qualification` | Exact pinned image/SDK/engine and container restart/kill persistence |\\n| Upstream known issues | `tests/known_issues` | Strict expected failures for lifecycle gaps outside this provider |\",\"newString\":\"| Schema upgrade | `tests/integration/test_schema_upgrade.py` | An older database upgrades in place; a newer schema is rejected |\\n| Backup and restore | `tests/integration/test_backup_restore.py` | Export restores into a clean database with identical integrity and projection; a newer schema is rejected there too |\\n| Provider invariants | `pytest -m surrealdb` | Real server transactions, isolation, native edges, replay/fork/diff, restart within a live server |\\n| Pack harness | `pytest -m packs tests/packs` | The published pack library loads and projects into one SurrealDB database |\\n| Pack fixture suites | `tests/packs/test_pack_fixtures_on_surrealdb.py` | Each pack's own `fixtures/run_fixtures.py` runs unchanged on SurrealDB-backed stores |\\n| Embedded SDK lane | `tests/embedded` (`-m embedded`) | Under `surrealdb[embedded]==3.0.0b10`, embedded transports stay rejected — expected-rejection evidence |\\n| Qualification | `pytest -m qualification` | Exact pinned image/SDK/engine and container restart/kill persistence |\\n| Upstream known issues | `tests/known_issues` | Strict expected failures for lifecycle gaps outside this provider |\"}","message_id":"msg_1376b9eb7001NtoNhu53po0xYm","result":"{\"output\":{\"files\":[{\"file\":\"docs/conformance.md\",\"patch\":\"Index: docs/conformance.md\\n===================================================================\\n--- docs/conformance.md\\n+++ docs/conformance.md\\n@@ -13,11 +13,13 @@\\n | Released ActiveGraph suites | `tests/integration/*conformance.py` | Compatibility with the public EventStore and GraphStore contracts |\\n | Native query pushdown | `tests/integration/test_graph_pushdown.py` | The query hooks run in SurrealQL, not the Python full-scan fallback |\\n | Projection order | `tests/integration/test_projection_order.py` | Objects read back in the reference store's insertion order, including across reopens |\\n | Schema upgrade | `tests/integration/test_schema_upgrade.py` | An older database upgrades in place; a newer schema is rejected |\\n+| Backup and restore | `tests/integration/test_backup_restore.py` | Export restores into a clean database with identical integrity and projection; a newer schema is rejected there too |\\n | Provider invariants | `pytest -m surrealdb` | Real server transactions, isolation, native edges, replay/fork/diff, restart within a live server |\\n | Pack harness | `pytest -m packs tests/packs` | The published pack library loads and projects into one SurrealDB database |\\n | Pack fixture suites | `tests/packs/test_pack_fixtures_on_surrealdb.py` | Each pack's own `fixtures/run_fixtures.py` runs unchanged on SurrealDB-backed stores |\\n+| Embedded SDK lane | `tests/embedded` (`-m embedded`) | Under `surrealdb[embedded]==3.0.0b10`, embedded transports stay rejected — expected-rejection evidence |\\n | Qualification | `pytest -m qualification` | Exact pinned image/SDK/engine and container restart/kill persistence |\\n | Upstream known issues | `tests/known_issues` | Strict expected failures for lifecycle gaps outside this provider |\\n \\n ## Commands\\n\",\"additions\":2,\"deletions\":0,\"status\":\"modified\"}],\"replacements\":1},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Edited docs/conformance.md (1 replacement)\"}],\"metadata\":{\"files\":[{\"file\":\"docs/conformance.md\",\"patch\":\"Index: docs/conformance.md\\n===================================================================\\n--- docs/conformance.md\\n+++ docs/conformance.md\\n@@ -13,11 +13,13 @@\\n | Released ActiveGraph suites | `tests/integration/*conformance.py` | Compatibility with the public EventStore and GraphStore contracts |\\n | Native query pushdown | `tests/integration/test_graph_pushdown.py` | The query hooks run in SurrealQL, not the Python full-scan fallback |\\n | Projection order | `tests/integration/test_projection_order.py` | Objects read back in the reference store's insertion order, including across reopens |\\n | Schema upgrade | `tests/integration/test_schema_upgrade.py` | An older database upgrades in place; a newer schema is rejected |\\n+| Backup and restore | `tests/integration/test_backup_restore.py` | Export restores into a clean database with identical integrity and projection; a newer schema is rejected there too |\\n | Provider invariants | `pytest -m surrealdb` | Real server transactions, isolation, native edges, replay/fork/diff, restart within a live server |\\n | Pack harness | `pytest -m packs tests/packs` | The published pack library loads and projects into one SurrealDB database |\\n | Pack fixture suites | `tests/packs/test_pack_fixtures_on_surrealdb.py` | Each pack's own `fixtures/run_fixtures.py` runs unchanged on SurrealDB-backed stores |\\n+| Embedded SDK lane | `tests/embedded` (`-m embedded`) | Under `surrealdb[embedded]==3.0.0b10`, embedded transports stay rejected — expected-r