{"id":"int-6c61b0b978ee05b7c96f0b9356fe84ba","kind":"tool_call","created_at":"2026-10-13T22:39:29.187Z","actor":"opencode","tool_name":"edit","extra":{"call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-93ea93986bc6a426","duration_ms":20,"input":"{\"path\":\"/work/mercor-work/activegraph-surrealdb/docs/conformance.md\",\"oldString\":\"```bash\\npython -m pip install -e '.[dev]'\\npytest -m 'not surrealdb and not qualification'\\npytest -m surrealdb tests/integration\\nACTIVEGRAPH_PACKS_PATH=/path/to/activegraph-packs pytest -m packs tests/packs\\nACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_QUALIFY=1 pytest -m qualification tests/qualification\\n```\\n\\nThe live layers require the environment described in [deployment.md](deployment.md).\\nThe qualification command must target only the disposable container it is\\nauthorized to restart and kill.\",\"newString\":\"```bash\\npython -m pip install -e '.[dev]'\\npytest -m 'not surrealdb and not qualification and not embedded'\\npytest -m surrealdb tests/integration\\nACTIVEGRAPH_PACKS_PATH=/path/to/activegraph-packs pytest -m packs tests/packs\\nACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_QUALIFY=1 pytest -m qualification tests/qualification\\nACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_EMBEDDED=1 .venv-embedded/bin/python -m pytest tests/embedded -m embedded\\n```\\n\\nThe live layers require the environment described in [deployment.md](deployment.md).\\nThe qualification command must target only the disposable container it is\\nauthorized to restart and kill. Lane tests (embedded and the exploration lanes)\\nare selected-but-skipped unless their gate environment variable is set; the\\nembedded lane runs inside an isolated `.venv-embedded` built with\\n`surrealdb[embedded]==3.0.0b10` on top of the normal dev install.\"}","message_id":"msg_1376b9eb7001NtoNhu53po0xYm","result":"{\"output\":{\"files\":[{\"file\":\"docs/conformance.md\",\"patch\":\"Index: docs/conformance.md\\n===================================================================\\n--- docs/conformance.md\\n+++ docs/conformance.md\\n@@ -27,17 +27,21 @@\\n Install the development dependencies, then run the layers explicitly:\\n \\n ```bash\\n python -m pip install -e '.[dev]'\\n-pytest -m 'not surrealdb and not qualification'\\n+pytest -m 'not surrealdb and not qualification and not embedded'\\n pytest -m surrealdb tests/integration\\n ACTIVEGRAPH_PACKS_PATH=/path/to/activegraph-packs pytest -m packs tests/packs\\n ACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_QUALIFY=1 pytest -m qualification tests/qualification\\n+ACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_EMBEDDED=1 .venv-embedded/bin/python -m pytest tests/embedded -m embedded\\n ```\\n \\n The live layers require the environment described in [deployment.md](deployment.md).\\n The qualification command must target only the disposable container it is\\n-authorized to restart and kill.\\n+authorized to restart and kill. Lane tests (embedded and the exploration lanes)\\n+are selected-but-skipped unless their gate environment variable is set; the\\n+embedded lane runs inside an isolated `.venv-embedded` built with\\n+`surrealdb[embedded]==3.0.0b10` on top of the normal dev install.\\n \\n ## Required invariants\\n \\n Promotion evidence must include at least:\\n\",\"additions\":6,\"deletions\":2,\"status\":\"modified\"}],\"replacements\":1},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Edited docs/conformance.md (1 replacement)\"}],\"metadata\":{\"files\":[{\"file\":\"docs/conformance.md\",\"patch\":\"Index: docs/conformance.md\\n===================================================================\\n--- docs/conformance.md\\n+++ docs/conformance.md\\n@@ -27,17 +27,21 @@\\n Install the development dependencies, then run the layers explicitly:\\n \\n ```bash\\n python -m pip install -e '.[dev]'\\n-pytest -m 'not surrealdb and not qualification'\\n+pytest -m 'not surrealdb and not qualification and not embedded'\\n pytest -m surrealdb tests/integration\\n ACTIVEGRAPH_PACKS_PATH=/path/to/activegraph-packs pytest -m packs tests/packs\\n ACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_QUALIFY=1 pytest -m qualification tests/qualification\\n+ACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_EMBEDDED=1 .venv-embedded/bin/python -m pytest tests/embedded -m embedded\\n ```\\n \\n The live layers require the environment described in [deployment.md](deployment.md).\\n The qualification command must target only the disposable container it is\\n-authorized to restart and kill.\\n+authorized to restart and kill. Lane tests (embedded and the exploration lanes)\\n+are selected-but-skipped unless their gate environment variable is set; the\\n+embedded lane runs inside an isolated `.venv-embedded` built with\\n+`surrealdb[embedded]==3.0.0b10` on top of the normal dev install.\\n \\n ## Required invariants\\n \\n Promotion evidence must include at least:\\n\",\"status\":\"modified\",\"additions\":6,\"deletions\":2}]}}","session_id":"ses_ecce71390ffe11p6yPgte61c3p","status":"completed"}}
{"id":"int-2fd54a1d56b916a15ebad1a8533d934f","kind":"tool_call","created_at":"2026-10-13T22:39:34.655Z","actor":"opencode","tool_name":"edit","extra":{"call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-838629bd5b31759d","duration_ms":11,"input":"{\"path\":\"/work/mercor-work/activegraph-surrealdb/docs/deployment.md\",\"oldString\":\"## Backup and restore\\n\\nBackup and restore are promotion gates, not completed features of this preview.\\nA production evaluation must document and exercise:\\n\\n1. the SurrealDB-supported backup/export mechanism for the selected deployment;\\n2. credential and encryption handling;\\n3. restoration into a separate clean environment;\\n4. event-chain and run-head verification after restore;\\n5. graph clear/replay after restore; and\\n6. recovery-time and recovery-point observations.\\n\\nA copied file, successful export command, or green application health check is\\nnot by itself restore proof.\",\"newString\":\"## Backup and restore\\n\\nBackup and restore remain promotion gates, not completed production features of\\nthis preview. A rehearsal lane is now pinned:\\n`tests/integration/test_backup_restore.py` exports the event log, restores it\\ninto a clean database, verifies event-chain and run-head integrity plus\\nprojection parity after replay, and confirms a database written by a newer\\nprovider is rejected rather than mis-read.\\n\\nA production evaluation must additionally document and exercise:\\n\\n1. the SurrealDB-supported backup/export mechanism for the selected deployment;\\n2. credential and encryption handling;\\n3. restoration into a separate clean environment;\\n4. event-chain and run-head verification after restore;\\n5. graph clear/replay after restore; and\\n6. recovery-time and recovery-point observations.\\n\\nA copied file, successful export command, or green application health check is\\nnot by itself restore proof.\\n\\n## Exploration lanes\\n\\nThe exploration lanes are non-gating: evidence recorded on them never changes\\nthe stable lane's claims. Each uses its own volume or environment. Status and\\nclaims live in [compatibility.md](compatibility.md).\\n\\n- **TLS (`wss://`)**: serve with `--web-crt`/`--web-key` (env\\n  `SURREAL_WEB_CRT`/`SURREAL_WEB_KEY`), or mount certificates through the\\n  Compose TLS profile (`docker compose --profile tls`). The demonstrated\\n  preview lane uses a local certificate authority and `SSL_CERT_FILE` on the\\n  client; public CAs, proxies, and rotation are unqualified.\\n- **SurrealKV engine**: start the server with `surrealkv:///path/to/db` on a\\n  dedicated volume (or set the lane's engine variable). SurrealKV remains\\n  beta; never share a storage location between backends.\\n- **Embedded SDK**: an isolated `.venv-embedded` with\\n  `surrealdb[embedded]==3.0.0b10` runs `tests/embedded`, which pins the\\n  expected rejection of embedded transports; it is evidence of the contract,\\n  not support for embedded mode.\"}","message_id":"msg_1376bba71001eBejC7v229aYGT","result":"{\"output\":{\"files\":[{\"file\":\"docs/deployment.md\",\"patch\":\"Index: docs/deployment.md\\n===================================================================\\n--- docs/deployment.md\\n+++ docs/deployment.md\\n@@ -100,11 +100,17 @@\\n under every failure, storage durability guarantees, or restore readiness.\\n \\n ## Backup and restore\\n \\n-Backup and restore are promotion gates, not completed features of this preview.\\n-A production evaluation must document and exercise:\\n+Backup and restore remain promotion gates, not completed production features of\\n+this preview. A rehearsal lane is now pinned:\\n+`tests/integration/test_backup_restore.py` exports the event log, restores it\\n+into a clean database, verifies event-chain and run-head integrity plus\\n+projection parity after replay, and confirms a database written by a newer\\n+provider is rejected rather than mis-read.\\n \\n+A production evaluation must additionally document and exercise:\\n+\\n 1. the SurrealDB-supported backup/export mechanism for the selected deployment;\\n 2. credential and encryption handling;\\n 3. restoration into a separate clean environment;\\n 4. event-chain and run-head verification after restore;\\n@@ -113,8 +119,27 @@\\n \\n A copied file, successful export command, or green application health check is\\n not by itself restore proof.\\n \\n+## Exploration lanes\\n+\\n+The exploration lanes are non-gating: evidence recorded on them never changes\\n+the stable lane's claims. Each uses its own volume or environment. Status and\\n+claims live in [compatibility.md](compatibility.md).\\n+\\n+- **TLS (`wss://`)**: serve with `--web-crt`/`--web-key` (env\\n+  `SURREAL_WEB_CRT`/`SURREAL_WEB_KEY`), or mount certificates through the\\n+  Compose TLS profile (`docker compose --profile tls`). The demonstrated\\n+  preview lane uses a local certificate authority and `SSL_CERT_FILE` on the\\n+  client; public CAs, proxies, and rotation are unqualified.\\n+- **SurrealKV engine**: start the server with `surrealkv:///path/to/db` on a\\n+  dedicated volume (or set the lane's engine variable). SurrealKV remains\\n+  beta; never share a storage location between backends.\\n+- **Embedded SDK**: an isolated `.venv-embedded` with\\n+  `surrealdb[embedded]==3.0.0b10` runs `tests/embedded`, which pins the\\n+  expected rejection of embedded transports; it is evidence of the contract,\\n+  not support for embedded mode.\\n+\\n ## Production evaluation checklist\\n \\n Before any production use, require evidence for all of the following:\\n \\n\",\"additions\":27,\"deletions\":2,\"status\":\"modified\"}],\"replacements\":1},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Edited docs/deployment.md (1 replacement)\"}],\"metadata\":{\"files\":[{\"file\":\"docs/deployment.md\",\"patch\":\"Index: docs/deployment.md\\n===================================================================\\n--- docs/deployment.md\\n+++ docs/deployment.md\\n@@ -100,11 +100,17 @@\\n under every failure, storage durability guarantees, or restore readiness.\\n \\n ## Backup and restore\\n \\n-Backup and restore are promotion gates, not completed features of this preview.\\n-A production evaluation must document and exercise:\\n+Backup and restore remain promotion gates, not completed production features of\\n+this preview. A rehearsal lane is now pinned:\\n+`tests/integration/test_backup_restore.py` exports the event log, restores it\\n+into a clean database, verifies event-chain and run-head integrity plus\\n+projection parity after replay, and confirms a database written by a newer\\n+provider is rejected rather than mis-read.\\n \\n+A production evaluation must additionally document and exercise:\\n+\\n 1. the SurrealDB-supported backup/export mechanism for the selected deployment;\\n 2. credential and encryption handling;\\n 3. restoration into a separate clean environment;\\n 4. event-chain and run-head verification after restore;\\n@@ -113,8 +119,27 @@\\n \\n A copied file, successful export command, or green application health check is\\n not by itself restore proof.\\n \\n+## Exploration lanes\\n+\\n+The exploration lanes are non-gating: evidence recorded on them never changes\\n+the stable lane's claims. Each uses its own volume or environment. Status and\\n+claims live in [compatibility.md](compatibility.md).\\n+\\n+- **TLS (`wss://`)**: serve with `--web-crt`/`--web-key` (env\\n+  `SURREAL_WEB_CRT`/`SURREAL_WEB_KEY`), or mount certificates through the\\n+  Compose TLS profile (`docker compose --profile tls`). The demonstrated\\n+  preview lane uses a local certificate authority and `SSL_CERT_FILE` on the\\n+  client; public CAs, proxies, and rotation are unqualified.\\n+- **SurrealKV engine**: start the server with `surrealkv:///path/to/db` on a\\n+  dedicated volume (or set the lane's engine variable). SurrealKV remains\\n+  beta; never share a storage location between backends.\\n+- **Embedded SDK**: an isolated `.venv-embedded` with\\n+  `surrealdb[embedded]==3.0.0b10` runs `tests/embedded`, which pins the\\n+  expected rejection of embedded transports; it is evidence of the contract,\\n+  not support for embedded mode.\\n+\\n ## Production evaluation checklist\\n \\n Before any production use, require evidence for all of the following:\\n \\n\",\"status\":\"modified\",\"additions\":27,\"deletions\":2}]}}","session_id":"ses_ecce71390ffe11p6yPgte61c3p","status":"completed"}}
{"id":"int-ca727e5b0fda086ee02568939b5aead4","kind":"tool_call","created_at":"2026-10-13T22:39:40.953Z","actor":"opencode","tool_name":"edit","extra":{"call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ce1eaff3bedfa6a","duration_ms":10,"input":"{\"path\":\"/work/mercor-work/activegraph-surrealdb/README.md\",\"oldString\":\"SurrealDB `3.3.x` prereleases are a non-gating preview lane. HTTP, embedded\\nengines, and TLS qualification are not part of the initial evidence. Details\\nare in [compatibility and known issues](docs/compatibility.md).\",\"newString\":\"SurrealDB `3.3.x` prereleases are a non-gating preview lane. HTTP and embedded\\nengines are rejected by configuration (pinned by the embedded lane in\\n`tests/embedded/`). TLS has a demonstrated preview lane only — a local\\ncertificate authority with enforced certificate validation; public CAs, proxy\\ntermination, and rotation are unqualified. Details are in\\n[compatibility and known issues](docs/compatibility.md).\"}","message_id":"msg_1376bcf8e001tFDc7Xj3WXskmw","result":"{\"output\":{\"files\":[{\"file\":\"README.md\",\"patch\":\"Index: README.md\\n===================================================================\\n--- README.md\\n+++ README.md\\n@@ -56,11 +56,14 @@\\n | Python | `3.11+` |\\n | Transport | remote WebSocket; local qualification uses `ws://` |\\n | Storage engine | server-side RocksDB |\\n \\n-SurrealDB `3.3.x` prereleases are a non-gating preview lane. HTTP, embedded\\n-engines, and TLS qualification are not part of the initial evidence. Details\\n-are in [compatibility and known issues](docs/compatibility.md).\\n+SurrealDB `3.3.x` prereleases are a non-gating preview lane. HTTP and embedded\\n+engines are rejected by configuration (pinned by the embedded lane in\\n+`tests/embedded/`). TLS has a demonstrated preview lane only — a local\\n+certificate authority with enforced certificate validation; public CAs, proxy\\n+termination, and rotation are unqualified. Details are in\\n+[compatibility and known issues](docs/compatibility.md).\\n \\n ## Architecture at a glance\\n \\n ```mermaid\\n\",\"additions\":6,\"deletions\":3,\"status\":\"modified\"}],\"replacements\":1},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Edited README.md (1 replacement)\"}],\"metadata\":{\"files\":[{\"file\":\"README.md\",\"patch\":\"Index: README.md\\n===================================================================\\n--- README.md\\n+++ README.md\\n@@ -56,11 +56,14 @@\\n | Python | `3.11+` |\\n | Transport | remote WebSocket; local qualification uses `ws://` |\\n | Storage engine | server-side RocksDB |\\n \\n-SurrealDB `3.3.x` prereleases are a non-gating preview lane. HTTP, embedded\\n-engines, and TLS qualification are not part of the initial evidence. Details\\n-are in [compatibility and known issues](docs/compatibility.md).\\n+SurrealDB `3.3.x` prereleases are a non-gating preview lane. HTTP and embedded\\n+engines are rejected by configuration (pinned by the embedded lane in\\n+`tests/embedded/`). TLS has a demonstrated preview lane only — a local\\n+certificate authority with enforced certificate validation; public CAs, proxy\\n+termination, and rotation are unqualified. Details are in\\n+[compatibility and known issues](docs/compatibility.md).\\n \\n ## Architecture at a glance\\n \\n ```mermaid\\n\",\"status\":\"modified\",\"additions\":6,\"deletions\":3}]}}","session_id":"ses_ecce71390ffe11p6yPgte61c3p","status":"completed"}}
{"id":"int-44339f68770aba7e3cd7402867f1d7ff","kind":"tool_call","created_at":"2026-10-13T22:39:40.965Z","actor":"opencode","tool_name":"edit","extra":{"call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-88bf82a43394ed39","duration_ms":22,"input":"{\"path\":\"/work/mercor-work/activegraph-surrealdb/README.md\",\"oldString\":\"```bash\\npytest -m 'not surrealdb and not qualification'\\npytest -m surrealdb tests/integration\\npytest -m packs tests/packs            # pack harness + per-pack fixture suites\\npython examples/replay_fork_diff.py\\n```\",\"newString\":\"```bash\\npytest -m 'not surrealdb and not qualification and not embedded'\\npytest -m surrealdb tests/integration\\npytest -m packs tests/packs            # pack harness + per-pack fixture suites\\npython examples/replay_fork_diff.py\\n```\"}","message_id":"msg_1376bcf8e001tFDc7Xj3WXskmw","result":"{\"output\":{\"files\":[{\"file\":\"README.md\",\"patch\":\"Index: README.md\\n===================================================================\\n--- README.md\\n+++ README.md\\n@@ -174,9 +174,9 @@\\n \\n Run the contract layers separately:\\n \\n ```bash\\n-pytest -m 'not surrealdb and not qualification'\\n+pytest -m 'not surrealdb and not qualification and not embedded'\\n pytest -m surrealdb tests/integration\\n pytest -m packs tests/packs            # pack harness + per-pack fixture suites\\n python examples/replay_fork_diff.py\\n ```\\n\",\"additions\":1,\"deletions\":1,\"status\":\"modified\"}],\"replacements\":1},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Edited README.md (1 replacement)\"}],\"metadata\":{\"files\":[{\"file\":\"README.md\",\"patch\":\"Index: README.md\\n===================================================================\\n--- README.md\\n+++ README.md\\n@@ -174,9 +174,9 @@\\n \\n Run the contract layers separately:\\n \\n ```bash\\n-pytest -m 'not surrealdb and not qualification'\\n+pytest -m 'not surrealdb and not qualification and not embedded'\\n pytest -m surrealdb tests/integration\\n pytest -m packs tests/packs            # pack harness + per-pack fixture suites\\n python examples/replay_fork_diff.py\\n ```\\n\",\"status\":\"modified\",\"additions\":1,\"deletions\":1}]}}","session_id":"ses_ecce71390ffe11p6yPgte61c3p","status":"completed"}}
{"id":"int-0a0c06be0854fe927fe72745c70d3e0d","kind":"tool_call","created_at":"2026-10-13T22:39:41.007Z","actor":"opencode","tool_name":"edit","extra":{"call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ef5033afe626b04","duration_ms":64,"input":"{\"path\":\"/work/mercor-work/activegraph-surrealdb/README.md\",\"oldString\":\"The important idea is not “put everything in one table.” It is “operate one\\ndatabase without confusing the record of what happened with a disposable view\\nof what the world looks like now.”\\n\\n> **Status: research preview.** The repository uses contract-first development.\",\"newString\":\"The important idea is not “put everything in one table.” It is “operate one\\ndatabase without confusing the record of what happened with a disposable view\\nof what the world looks like now.”\\n\\n## What is ActiveGraph?\\n\\n[ActiveGraph](https://github.com/yoheinakajima/activegraph-packs) is a Python\\nframework for building agents on an event-sourced graph. A runtime appends\\nevery decision and observation to an ordered event log, projects those events\\ninto a graph of objects and relations, and runs queued behaviors until the\\ngraph is idle. The event log is the authority; the graph is rebuildable state.\\nAn optional pack library defines agent behaviors and fixtures on top.\\n\\nThis provider implements ActiveGraph's two store contracts — the `EventStore`\\n(append-ordered, hash-chained events with per-run heads, stale-writer\\ndetection, and prefix forks) and the `GraphStore` (objects, patches, and\\nnative `TYPE RELATION` edges) — on one SurrealDB deployment, with the query\\nhooks pushed down into SurrealQL. One database holds both the record of what\\nhappened and the current view of the world, and the projection can always be\\nerased and replayed from events.\\n\\n> **Status: research preview.** The repository uses contract-first development.\"}","message_id":"msg_1376bcf8e001tFDc7Xj3WXskmw","result":"{\"output\":{\"files\":[{\"file\":\"README.md\",\"patch\":\"Index: README.md\\n===================================================================\\n--- README.md\\n+++ README.md\\n@@ -9,8 +9,25 @@\\n The important idea is not “put everything in one table.” It is “operate one\\n database without confusing the record of what happened with a disposable view\\n of what the world looks like now.”\\n \\n+## What is ActiveGraph?\\n+\\n+[ActiveGraph](https://github.com/yoheinakajima/activegraph-packs) is a Python\\n+framework for building agents on an event-sourced graph. A runtime appends\\n+every decision and observation to an ordered event log, projects those events\\n+into a graph of objects and relations, and runs queued behaviors until the\\n+graph is idle. The event log is the authority; the graph is rebuildable state.\\n+An optional pack library defines agent behaviors and fixtures on top.\\n+\\n+This provider implements ActiveGraph's two store contracts — the `EventStore`\\n+(append-ordered, hash-chained events with per-run heads, stale-writer\\n+detection, and prefix forks) and the `GraphStore` (objects, patches, and\\n+native `TYPE RELATION` edges) — on one SurrealDB deployment, with the query\\n+hooks pushed down into SurrealQL. One database holds both the record of what\\n+happened and the current view of the world, and the projection can always be\\n+erased and replayed from events.\\n+\\n > **Status: research preview.** The repository uses contract-first development.\\n > Passing tests are evidence for the tested versions and failure paths only;\\n > they are not a production-readiness, high-availability, backup, performance,\\n > or security certification.\\n\",\"additions\":17,\"deletions\":0,\"status\":\"modified\"}],\"replacements\":1},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Edited README.md (1 replacement)\"}],\"metadata\":{\"files\":[{\"file\":\"README.md\",\"patch\":\"Index: README.md\\n===================================================================\\n--- README.md\\n+++ README.md\\n@@ -9,8 +9,25 @@\\n The important idea is not “put everything in one table.” It is “operate one\\n database without confusing the record of what happened with a disposable view\\n of what the world looks like now.”\\n \\n+## What is ActiveGraph?\\n+\\n+[ActiveGraph](https://github.com/yoheinakajima/activegraph-packs) is a Python\\n+framework for building agents on an event-sourced graph. A runtime appends\\n+every decision and observation to an ordered event log, projects those events\\n+into a graph of objects and relations, and runs queued behaviors until the\\n+graph is idle. The event log is the authority; the graph is rebuildable state.\\n+An optional pack library defines agent behaviors and fixtures on top.\\n+\\n+This provider implements ActiveGraph's two store contracts — the `EventStore`\\n+(append-ordered, hash-chained events with per-run heads, stale-writer\\n+detection, and prefix forks) and the `GraphStore` (objects, patches, and\\n+native `TYPE RELATION` edges) — on one SurrealDB deployment, with the query\\n+hooks pushed down into SurrealQL. One database holds both the record of what\\n+happened and the current view of the world, and the projection can always be\\n+erased and replayed from events.\\n+\\n > **Status: research preview.** The repository uses contract-first development.\\n > Passing tests are evidence for the tested versions and failure paths only;\\n > they are not a production-readiness, high-availability, backup, performance,\\n > or security certification.\\n\",\"status\":\"modified\",\"additions\":17,\"deletions\":0}]}}","session_id":"ses_ecce71390ffe11p6yPgte61c3p","status":"completed"}}
