{"id":"int-1ff2ff858bb3bfa3c1ffde70979feadc","kind":"tool_call","created_at":"2026-10-13T22:51:11.692Z","actor":"opencode","tool_name":"shell","extra":{"call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8fa32ff3b9b85a0c","duration_ms":153,"input":"{\"command\":\"python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport subprocess, re, json\\nours = subprocess.run(['git','show','origin/main:.beads/interactions.jsonl'],capture_output=True).stdout.splitlines()\\ntheirs = subprocess.run(['git','show','agentic/ladder-v6-v9:.beads/interactions.jsonl'],capture_output=True).stdout.splitlines()\\nseen, out = set(), []\\nidre = re.compile(rb'\\\"id\\\":\\\"([^\\\"]+)\\\"')\\ncreatere = re.compile(rb'\\\"created_at\\\":\\\"([^\\\"]+)\\\"')\\nfor line in ours + theirs:\\n    if not line.strip(): continue\\n    m = idre.search(line)\\n    key = m.group(1) if m else None\\n    if key:\\n        if key in seen: continue\\n        seen.add(key)\\n    out.append(line)\\nout.sort(key=lambda l: (createre.search(l) or b'').group(1) if createre.search(l) else b'')\\nopen('.beads/interactions.jsonl','wb').write(b'\\\\n'.join(out) + b'\\\\n')\\nprint('entries:', len(out))\\nEOF\\ngit add .beads/interactions.jsonl && git status --short | head -3\"}","message_id":"msg_137765c8c0017R9XhWEx5VxGin","result":"{\"output\":{\"exit\":0,\"truncated\":false,\"output\":\"entries: 1337\\nM  .beads/interactions.jsonl\\nA  docs/overview.md\\n\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"entries: 1337\\nM  .beads/interactions.jsonl\\nA  docs/overview.md\\n\"}],\"metadata\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"truncated\":false,\"exit\":0}}","session_id":"ses_ecce71390ffe11p6yPgte61c3p","status":"completed"}}
{"id":"int-5ce2bab5239ff127fe91170aab31c8e2","kind":"tool_call","created_at":"2026-10-13T22:51:21.957Z","actor":"opencode","tool_name":"edit","extra":{"call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a93bd0e03c1a152","duration_ms":62,"input":"{\"path\":\"/work/mercor-work/activegraph-surrealdb/AGENTS.md\",\"oldString\":\"```bash\\n# Unit (no server needed)\\npytest -m 'not surrealdb and not qualification'\\n\\n# Live integration (needs a running server)\\ndocker compose up -d\\npytest -m surrealdb tests/integration\\n\\n# Qualification (controls a pinned Docker server; restart/kill sequences)\\nACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_QUALIFY=1 pytest -m qualification tests/qualification\\n\\n# Published evidence example\\npython examples/replay_fork_diff.py\\n```\",\"newString\":\"```bash\\n# Unit (no server needed; the embedded lane self-skips without its gate)\\npytest -m 'not surrealdb and not qualification and not embedded'\\n\\n# Live integration (needs a running server)\\ndocker compose up -d\\npytest -m surrealdb tests/integration\\n\\n# Qualification (controls a pinned Docker server; restart/kill sequences)\\nACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_QUALIFY=1 pytest -m qualification tests/qualification\\n\\n# Embedded SDK lane (isolated venv; expected-rejection evidence)\\nACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_EMBEDDED=1 .venv-embedded/bin/python -m pytest tests/embedded -m embedded\\n\\n# Published evidence example\\npython examples/replay_fork_diff.py\\n```\"}","message_id":"msg_13776722c0011bvT0pSYp2dhER","result":"{\"output\":{\"files\":[{\"file\":\"AGENTS.md\",\"patch\":\"Index: AGENTS.md\\n===================================================================\\n--- AGENTS.md\\n+++ AGENTS.md\\n@@ -145,18 +145,21 @@\\n \\n Test ladder (see docs/upgrade-plan.md for the serialized evidence ladder V0–V9):\\n \\n ```bash\\n-# Unit (no server needed)\\n-pytest -m 'not surrealdb and not qualification'\\n+# Unit (no server needed; the embedded lane self-skips without its gate)\\n+pytest -m 'not surrealdb and not qualification and not embedded'\\n \\n # Live integration (needs a running server)\\n docker compose up -d\\n pytest -m surrealdb tests/integration\\n \\n # Qualification (controls a pinned Docker server; restart/kill sequences)\\n ACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_QUALIFY=1 pytest -m qualification tests/qualification\\n \\n+# Embedded SDK lane (isolated venv; expected-rejection evidence)\\n+ACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_EMBEDDED=1 .venv-embedded/bin/python -m pytest tests/embedded -m embedded\\n+\\n # Published evidence example\\n python examples/replay_fork_diff.py\\n ```\\n \\n\",\"additions\":5,\"deletions\":2,\"status\":\"modified\"}],\"replacements\":1},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Edited AGENTS.md (1 replacement)\"}],\"metadata\":{\"files\":[{\"file\":\"AGENTS.md\",\"patch\":\"Index: AGENTS.md\\n===================================================================\\n--- AGENTS.md\\n+++ AGENTS.md\\n@@ -145,18 +145,21 @@\\n \\n Test ladder (see docs/upgrade-plan.md for the serialized evidence ladder V0–V9):\\n \\n ```bash\\n-# Unit (no server needed)\\n-pytest -m 'not surrealdb and not qualification'\\n+# Unit (no server needed; the embedded lane self-skips without its gate)\\n+pytest -m 'not surrealdb and not qualification and not embedded'\\n \\n # Live integration (needs a running server)\\n docker compose up -d\\n pytest -m surrealdb tests/integration\\n \\n # Qualification (controls a pinned Docker server; restart/kill sequences)\\n ACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_QUALIFY=1 pytest -m qualification tests/qualification\\n \\n+# Embedded SDK lane (isolated venv; expected-rejection evidence)\\n+ACTIVEGRAPH_SURREALDB_EMBEDDED=1 .venv-embedded/bin/python -m pytest tests/embedded -m embedded\\n+\\n # Published evidence example\\n python examples/replay_fork_diff.py\\n ```\\n \\n\",\"status\":\"modified\",\"additions\":5,\"deletions\":2}]}}","session_id":"ses_ecce71390ffe11p6yPgte61c3p","status":"completed"}}
{"id":"int-ead4a2338f020990f8d6c09e6b1fa492","kind":"tool_call","created_at":"2026-10-13T22:51:21.983Z","actor":"opencode","tool_name":"edit","extra":{"call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a155703f625ebf89","duration_ms":43,"input":"{\"path\":\"/work/mercor-work/activegraph-surrealdb/docs/security-model.md\",\"oldString\":\"The initial configuration accepts `wss://` syntax but has no qualified TLS lane.\\nCertificate validation, proxies, workload identity, and rotation need explicit\\ndeployment tests before a remote security claim.\",\"newString\":\"The configuration accepts `wss://` syntax. A preview TLS lane is demonstrated\\n(local certificate authority, enforced certificate validation, full live suite\\ngreen; see [compatibility](compatibility.md)), but no TLS qualification claim is\\nmade: public CAs, proxy termination, least-privilege identities, and certificate\\nrotation need explicit deployment tests before a remote security claim.\"}","message_id":"msg_13776722c0011bvT0pSYp2dhER","result":"{\"output\":{\"files\":[{\"file\":\"docs/security-model.md\",\"patch\":\"Index: docs/security-model.md\\n===================================================================\\n--- docs/security-model.md\\n+++ docs/security-model.md\\n@@ -49,11 +49,13 @@\\n   record IDs, event payloads, traces, or CI artifacts.\\n - Rotate any credential that appears in a public log or issue; deleting the text\\n   is not sufficient remediation.\\n \\n-The initial configuration accepts `wss://` syntax but has no qualified TLS lane.\\n-Certificate validation, proxies, workload identity, and rotation need explicit\\n-deployment tests before a remote security claim.\\n+The configuration accepts `wss://` syntax. A preview TLS lane is demonstrated\\n+(local certificate authority, enforced certificate validation, full live suite\\n+green; see [compatibility](compatibility.md)), but no TLS qualification claim is\\n+made: public CAs, proxy termination, least-privilege identities, and certificate\\n+rotation need explicit deployment tests before a remote security claim.\\n \\n ## Non-atomic runtime boundary\\n \\n The provider does not promise one transaction across event append and graph\\n\",\"additions\":5,\"deletions\":3,\"status\":\"modified\"}],\"replacements\":1},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Edited docs/security-model.md (1 replacement)\"}],\"metadata\":{\"files\":[{\"file\":\"docs/security-model.md\",\"patch\":\"Index: docs/security-model.md\\n===================================================================\\n--- docs/security-model.md\\n+++ docs/security-model.md\\n@@ -49,11 +49,13 @@\\n   record IDs, event payloads, traces, or CI artifacts.\\n - Rotate any credential that appears in a public log or issue; deleting the text\\n   is not sufficient remediation.\\n \\n-The initial configuration accepts `wss://` syntax but has no qualified TLS lane.\\n-Certificate validation, proxies, workload identity, and rotation need explicit\\n-deployment tests before a remote security claim.\\n+The configuration accepts `wss://` syntax. A preview TLS lane is demonstrated\\n+(local certificate authority, enforced certificate validation, full live suite\\n+green; see [compatibility](compatibility.md)), but no TLS qualification claim is\\n+made: public CAs, proxy termination, least-privilege identities, and certificate\\n+rotation need explicit deployment tests before a remote security claim.\\n \\n ## Non-atomic runtime boundary\\n \\n The provider does not promise one transaction across event append and graph\\n\",\"status\":\"modified\",\"additions\":5,\"deletions\":3}]}}","session_id":"ses_ecce71390ffe11p6yPgte61c3p","status":"completed"}}
