{"id":"int-11a612ef200a3ec0a21d975f85413895","kind":"tool_call","created_at":"2026-10-13T22:51:21.949Z","actor":"opencode","tool_name":"edit","extra":{"call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-99aa2851f11f59e4","duration_ms":53,"input":"{\"path\":\"/work/mercor-work/activegraph-surrealdb/docs/conformance.md\",\"oldString\":\"| Schema upgrade | `tests/integration/test_schema_upgrade.py` | An older database upgrades in place; a newer schema is rejected |\\n| Provider invariants | `pytest -m surrealdb` | Real server transactions, isolation, native edges, replay/fork/diff, restart within a live server |\\n| Pack harness | `pytest -m packs tests/packs` | The published pack library loads and projects into one SurrealDB database |\\n| Pack fixture suites | `tests/packs/test_pack_fixtures_on_surrealdb.py` | Each pack's own `fixtures/run_fixtures.py` runs unchanged on SurrealDB-backed stores |\\n| Qualification | `pytest -m qualification` | Exact pinned image/SDK/engine and container restart/kill persistence |\",\"newString\":\"| Schema upgrade | `tests/integration/test_schema_upgrade.py` | An older database upgrades in place; a newer schema is rejected |\\n| Backup and restore | `tests/integration/test_backup_restore.py` | Export restores into a clean database with identical integrity and projection; a newer schema is rejected there too |\\n| Provider invariants | `pytest -m surrealdb` | Real server transactions, isolation, native edges, replay/fork/diff, restart within a live server |\\n| Pack harness | `pytest -m packs tests/packs` | The published pack library loads and projects into one SurrealDB database |\\n| Pack fixture suites | `tests/packs/test_pack_fixtures_on_surrealdb.py` | Each pack's own `fixtures/run_fixtures.py` runs unchanged on SurrealDB-backed stores |\\n| Embedded SDK lane | `tests/embedded` (`-m embedded`) | Under `surrealdb[embedded]==3.0.0b10`, embedded transports stay rejected — expected-rejection evidence |\\n| Qualification | `pytest -m qualification` | Exact pinned image/SDK/engine and container restart/kill persistence |\"}","message_id":"msg_13776722c0011bvT0pSYp2dhER","result":"{\"output\":{\"files\":[{\"file\":\"docs/conformance.md\",\"patch\":\"Index: docs/conformance.md\\n===================================================================\\n--- docs/conformance.md\\n+++ docs/conformance.md\\n@@ -13,11 +13,13 @@\\n | Released ActiveGraph suites | `tests/integration/*conformance.py` | Compatibility with the public EventStore and GraphStore contracts |\\n | Native query pushdown | `tests/integration/test_graph_pushdown.py` | The query hooks run in SurrealQL, not the Python full-scan fallback |\\n | Projection order | `tests/integration/test_projection_order.py` | Objects read back in the reference store's insertion order, including across reopens |\\n | Schema upgrade | `tests/integration/test_schema_upgrade.py` | An older database upgrades in place; a newer schema is rejected |\\n+| Backup and restore | `tests/integration/test_backup_restore.py` | Export restores into a clean database with identical integrity and projection; a newer schema is rejected there too |\\n | Provider invariants | `pytest -m surrealdb` | Real server transactions, isolation, native edges, replay/fork/diff, restart within a live server |\\n | Pack harness | `pytest -m packs tests/packs` | The published pack library loads and projects into one SurrealDB database |\\n | Pack fixture suites | `tests/packs/test_pack_fixtures_on_surrealdb.py` | Each pack's own `fixtures/run_fixtures.py` runs unchanged on SurrealDB-backed stores |\\n+| Embedded SDK lane | `tests/embedded` (`-m embedded`) | Under `surrealdb[embedded]==3.0.0b10`, embedded transports stay rejected — expected-rejection evidence |\\n | Qualification | `pytest -m qualification` | Exact pinned image/SDK/engine and container restart/kill persistence |\\n | Upstream known issues | `tests/known_issues` | Strict expected failures for lifecycle gaps outside this provider |\\n \\n ## Commands\\n\",\"additions\":2,\"deletions\":0,\"status\":\"modified\"}],\"replacements\":1},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Edited docs/conformance.md (1 replacement)\"}],\"metadata\":{\"files\":[{\"file\":\"docs/conformance.md\",\"patch\":\"Index: docs/conformance.md\\n===================================================================\\n--- docs/conformance.md\\n+++ docs/conformance.md\\n@@ -13,11 +13,13 @@\\n | Released ActiveGraph suites | `tests/integration/*conformance.py` | Compatibility with the public EventStore and GraphStore contracts |\\n | Native query pushdown | `tests/integration/test_graph_pushdown.py` | The query hooks run in SurrealQL, not the Python full-scan fallback |\\n | Projection order | `tests/integration/test_projection_order.py` | Objects read back in the reference store's insertion order, including across reopens |\\n | Schema upgrade | `tests/integration/test_schema_upgrade.py` | An older database upgrades in place; a newer schema is rejected |\\n+| Backup and restore | `tests/integration/test_backup_restore.py` | Export restores into a clean database with identical integrity and projection; a newer schema is rejected there too |\\n | Provider invariants | `pytest -m surrealdb` | Real server transactions, isolation, native edges, replay/fork/diff, restart within a live server |\\n | Pack harness | `pytest -m packs tests/packs` | The published pack library loads and projects into one SurrealDB database |\\n | Pack fixture suites | `tests/packs/test_pack_fixtures_on_surrealdb.py` | Each pack's own `fixtures/run_fixtures.py` runs unchanged on SurrealDB-backed stores |\\n+| Embedded SDK lane | `tests/embedded` (`-m embedded`) | Under `surrealdb[embedded]==3.0.0b10`, embedded transports stay rejected — expected-rejection evidence |\\n | Qualification | `pytest -m qualification` | Exact pinned image/SDK/engine and container restart/kill persistence |\\n | Upstream known issues | `tests/known_issues` | Strict expected failures for lifecycle gaps outside this provider |\\n \\n ## Commands\\n\",\"status\":\"modified\",\"additions\":2,\"deletions\":0}]}}","session_id":"ses_ecce71390ffe11p6yPgte61c3p","status":"completed"}}
{"id":"int-add785f54c1d6b9cd42832f53d992a74","kind":"tool_call","created_at":"2026-10-13T22:51:31.913Z","actor":"opencode","tool_name":"edit","extra":{"call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8c6f8fa109798a2f","duration_ms":20,"input":"{\"path\":\"/work/mercor-work/activegraph-surrealdb/README.md\",\"oldString\":\"The important idea is not “put everything in one table.” It is “operate one\\ndatabase without confusing the record of what happened with a disposable view\\nof what the world looks like now.”\\n\\n> **Status: research preview.** The repository uses contract-first development.\",\"newString\":\"The important idea is not “put everything in one table.” It is “operate one\\ndatabase without confusing the record of what happened with a disposable view\\nof what the world looks like now.”\\n\\n## What is ActiveGraph?\\n\\n[ActiveGraph](https://github.com/yoheinakajima/activegraph-packs) is a Python\\nframework for building agents on an event-sourced graph. A runtime appends\\nevery decision and observation to an ordered event log, projects those events\\ninto a graph of objects and relations, and runs queued behaviors until the\\ngraph is idle. The event log is the authority; the graph is rebuildable state.\\nAn optional pack library defines agent behaviors and fixtures on top.\\n\\nThis provider implements ActiveGraph's two store contracts — the `EventStore`\\n(append-ordered, hash-chained events with per-run heads, stale-writer\\ndetection, and prefix forks) and the `GraphStore` (objects, patches, and\\nnative `TYPE RELATION` edges) — on one SurrealDB deployment, with the query\\nhooks pushed down into SurrealQL. One database holds both the record of what\\nhappened and the current view of the world, and the projection can always be\\nerased and replayed from events. See the [plain-language\\noverview](docs/overview.md) for how the three workstreams (upgrade evidence,\\ntraces for evals, and the agentic harness) fit together.\\n\\n> **Status: research preview.** The repository uses contract-first development.\"}","message_id":"msg_137769b84001FaUzrl5jIUjScX","result":"{\"output\":{\"files\":[{\"file\":\"README.md\",\"patch\":\"Index: README.md\\n===================================================================\\n--- README.md\\n+++ README.md\\n@@ -9,8 +9,27 @@\\n The important idea is not “put everything in one table.” It is “operate one\\n database without confusing the record of what happened with a disposable view\\n of what the world looks like now.”\\n \\n+## What is ActiveGraph?\\n+\\n+[ActiveGraph](https://github.com/yoheinakajima/activegraph-packs) is a Python\\n+framework for building agents on an event-sourced graph. A runtime appends\\n+every decision and observation to an ordered event log, projects those events\\n+into a graph of objects and relations, and runs queued behaviors until the\\n+graph is idle. The event log is the authority; the graph is rebuildable state.\\n+An optional pack library defines agent behaviors and fixtures on top.\\n+\\n+This provider implements ActiveGraph's two store contracts — the `EventStore`\\n+(append-ordered, hash-chained events with per-run heads, stale-writer\\n+detection, and prefix forks) and the `GraphStore` (objects, patches, and\\n+native `TYPE RELATION` edges) — on one SurrealDB deployment, with the query\\n+hooks pushed down into SurrealQL. One database holds both the record of what\\n+happened and the current view of the world, and the projection can always be\\n+erased and replayed from events. See the [plain-language\\n+overview](docs/overview.md) for how the three workstreams (upgrade evidence,\\n+traces for evals, and the agentic harness) fit together.\\n+\\n > **Status: research preview.** The repository uses contract-first development.\\n > Passing tests are evidence for the tested versions and failure paths only;\\n > they are not a production-readiness, high-availability, backup, performance,\\n > or security certification.\\n\",\"additions\":19,\"deletions\":0,\"status\":\"modified\"}],\"replacements\":1},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Edited README.md (1 replacement)\"}],\"metadata\":{\"files\":[{\"file\":\"README.md\",\"patch\":\"Index: README.md\\n===================================================================\\n--- README.md\\n+++ README.md\\n@@ -9,8 +9,27 @@\\n The important idea is not “put everything in one table.” It is “operate one\\n database without confusing the record of what happened with a disposable view\\n of what the world looks like now.”\\n \\n+## What is ActiveGraph?\\n+\\n+[ActiveGraph](https://github.com/yoheinakajima/activegraph-packs) is a Python\\n+framework for building agents on an event-sourced graph. A runtime appends\\n+every decision and observation to an ordered event log, projects those events\\n+into a graph of objects and relations, and runs queued behaviors until the\\n+graph is idle. The event log is the authority; the graph is rebuildable state.\\n+An optional pack library defines agent behaviors and fixtures on top.\\n+\\n+This provider implements ActiveGraph's two store contracts — the `EventStore`\\n+(append-ordered, hash-chained events with per-run heads, stale-writer\\n+detection, and prefix forks) and the `GraphStore` (objects, patches, and\\n+native `TYPE RELATION` edges) — on one SurrealDB deployment, with the query\\n+hooks pushed down into SurrealQL. One database holds both the record of what\\n+happened and the current view of the world, and the projection can always be\\n+erased and replayed from events. See the [plain-language\\n+overview](docs/overview.md) for how the three workstreams (upgrade evidence,\\n+traces for evals, and the agentic harness) fit together.\\n+\\n > **Status: research preview.** The repository uses contract-first development.\\n > Passing tests are evidence for the tested versions and failure paths only;\\n > they are not a production-readiness, high-availability, backup, performance,\\n > or security certification.\\n\",\"status\":\"modified\",\"additions\":19,\"deletions\":0}]}}","session_id":"ses_ecce71390ffe11p6yPgte61c3p","status":"completed"}}
